01:22:48.130 --> 01:22:49.165
But we are here and I am Darren

01:22:50.299 --> 01:22:51.167
and I'm so excited
to spend the stay with you.

01:22:52.735 --> 01:22:53.369
Thank you, thank you,
Thank you all

01:22:54.370 --> 01:22:55.037
for sharing your time with us.

01:22:55.304 --> 01:22:56.338
Wherever you are watching from,

01:22:58.574 --> 01:22:58.908
I hope that you and yours
are safe and healthy

01:23:00.810 --> 01:23:01.177
because we have a
wonderful show planned.

01:23:02.645 --> 01:23:03.112
I am thrilled

01:23:03.779 --> 01:23:04.680
to be back with you.

01:23:06.248 --> 01:23:07.082
Thrilled,
do you hear me saying this?

01:23:08.384 --> 01:23:08.951
It's Darren, I'm always
thrilled.

01:23:10.352 --> 01:23:11.187
Thank you all for enjoying

01:23:12.121 --> 01:23:12.521
what I have brought to
Community Night

01:23:13.689 --> 01:23:14.190
over the years.

01:23:14.723 --> 01:23:14.857
You are all very kind.

01:23:16.392 --> 01:23:16.859
It means the world to me.

01:23:18.194 --> 01:23:18.794
Tonight, just think of me as...

01:23:21.430 --> 01:23:21.630
the human equivalent of
comfort food.

01:23:23.132 --> 01:23:23.332
I am meatloaf in a suit

01:23:25.134 --> 01:23:25.868
or if you're vegan I am

01:23:27.603 --> 01:23:27.870
tofu with a pocket handkerchief.
Either way,

01:23:31.440 --> 01:23:31.607
I am so looking
forward to today.

01:23:33.442 --> 01:23:33.709
When Blizzard reached out to me

01:23:34.076 --> 01:23:34.310
about doing this,

01:23:36.378 --> 01:23:36.645
I thought about the line

01:23:38.547 --> 01:23:39.381
at the end of Honor and Glory.

01:23:40.983 --> 01:23:41.184
Hey...
I got the thing, here it is.

01:23:43.352 --> 01:23:46.121
You know when Reinhart says

01:23:47.823 --> 01:23:48.290
"I have been called,
I must answer, always".

01:23:52.027 --> 01:23:52.228
I thought about
Reinhart's kindness

01:23:54.330 --> 01:23:54.697
and his devotion,

01:23:57.099 --> 01:23:57.233
his sense of
being there for others.

01:23:58.501 --> 01:23:58.701
That line,

01:24:01.871 --> 01:24:02.872
that line errr,
it's very important line to me.

01:24:04.373 --> 01:24:04.874
It resonates with me,
it's a powerful line.

01:24:07.309 --> 01:24:07.576
Is it my favorite
Rhinehart line? No!

01:24:09.011 --> 01:24:09.879
People ask a lot of the cast,

01:24:11.247 --> 01:24:12.114
what's your favorite line?
(REPEATS)

01:24:13.349 --> 01:24:14.450
what's your favorite ...
character...

01:24:16.986 --> 01:24:17.453
and I've never said what mine
is. I've never said it.

01:24:18.087 --> 01:24:18.854
It's something
I've struggled with,

01:24:19.922 --> 01:24:20.389
I've put a lot of
thought into it

01:24:21.591 --> 01:24:21.857
and then it hit me.

01:24:23.425 --> 01:24:23.692
For me...

01:24:25.261 --> 01:24:26.295
there is no favorite line.

01:24:26.762 --> 01:24:27.796
There is only

01:24:29.131 --> 01:24:29.331
Overwatch.

01:24:31.433 --> 01:24:31.800
There is only Warcraft.

01:24:33.836 --> 01:24:34.336
There is only Hearthstone,

01:24:34.670 --> 01:24:34.937
Diablo,

01:24:36.272 --> 01:24:36.372
StarCraft,

01:24:37.740 --> 01:24:38.140
Heroes of the Storm.

01:24:39.041 --> 01:24:39.308
These are worlds

01:24:40.609 --> 01:24:40.876
and characters

01:24:43.479 --> 01:24:44.280
that I want to spend time with,

01:24:45.180 --> 01:24:46.081
that I want to
immerse myself in.

01:24:47.983 --> 01:24:48.918
Every time I get to
go into the recording booth.

01:24:50.719 --> 01:24:51.220
Every time I get to
become one of my now

01:24:54.356 --> 01:24:54.690
75 Blizzard characters.
How did that happen?

01:24:56.625 --> 01:24:56.959
That's my favorite time.

01:24:59.295 --> 01:24:59.562
That's what I do to hopefully

01:25:01.897 --> 01:25:02.464
give you your favorite moment.

01:25:03.866 --> 01:25:04.033
It's a little bit of joy,

01:25:05.034 --> 01:25:05.267
a little bit of madness,

01:25:06.001 --> 01:25:06.969
a little bit of whimsy.

01:25:08.637 --> 01:25:09.605
But at the heart of it,
if you think about it,

01:25:10.739 --> 01:25:11.006
that's Blizzard.

01:25:13.242 --> 01:25:13.509
That's this community.

01:25:15.411 --> 01:25:15.945
That creative spark

01:25:17.112 --> 01:25:17.980
that will inspire

01:25:19.381 --> 01:25:20.316
outrageous cosplay,

01:25:20.816 --> 01:25:21.551
beautiful art,

01:25:23.552 --> 01:25:23.886
wonderful performances.

01:25:26.555 --> 01:25:27.423
Those worlds, those characters.

01:25:29.391 --> 01:25:29.658
Hey, in Warcraft,

01:25:32.328 --> 01:25:32.528
they put a giant sword
into a planet.

01:25:35.564 --> 01:25:36.498
In Overwatch, there was a
gorilla scientist from the moon

01:25:38.267 --> 01:25:39.068
and there's a small
hamster that somehow

01:25:40.402 --> 01:25:40.703
knows how to operate
heavy machinery.

01:25:42.371 --> 01:25:42.438
And we love it.

01:25:44.473 --> 01:25:44.740
That's this community to me.

01:25:45.941 --> 01:25:46.609
That's what today is about.

01:25:47.743 --> 01:25:48.243
All the cosplayers, the artists,

01:25:48.877 --> 01:25:49.478
the short film makers,

01:25:51.113 --> 01:25:51.413
the singers, the musicians,

01:25:54.984 --> 01:25:55.117
getting their crazy, delicious,

01:25:58.454 --> 01:25:59.355
delightful, Goshallheck, "Wow!"
moment.

01:26:00.856 --> 01:26:01.390
Sharing their skill
and their passion.

01:26:03.659 --> 01:26:03.792
So that you go
"How do they do that?"

01:26:06.328 --> 01:26:06.528
Why did they do that?
Can I do that?

01:26:09.465 --> 01:26:10.299
Of course you can!
It's that creative spark.

01:26:12.968 --> 01:26:13.802
That will be shared by everyone
you're going to see tonight.

01:26:16.472 --> 01:26:16.605
So even in this time of
distance,

01:26:18.807 --> 01:26:20.275
our community
creates things that

01:26:21.677 --> 01:26:22.244
give us connection.

01:26:23.312 --> 01:26:23.512
It's that spirit

01:26:25.848 --> 01:26:26.682
that makes me so thrilled to see

01:26:28.117 --> 01:26:28.484
what everyone
has in store for us.

01:26:29.818 --> 01:26:30.085
It will be

01:26:33.222 --> 01:26:34.123
a little bit of joy,
a little bit of madness,

01:26:35.091 --> 01:26:36.258
a little bit of whimsy

01:26:37.092 --> 01:26:38.093
and also, stick around for
the end because we're gonna

01:26:39.161 --> 01:26:39.762
bring on a special guest
to help me announce

01:26:42.464 --> 01:26:43.332
Best in Show Cosplay Award.

01:26:44.867 --> 01:26:45.300
And now,
grab your favorite beverage

01:26:46.468 --> 01:26:47.036
could be iced tea,

01:26:47.937 --> 01:26:48.337
could be moon berry juice.

01:26:50.406 --> 01:26:50.639
Sit back, relax,

01:26:52.207 --> 01:26:52.474
because we are about to start.

01:26:53.108 --> 01:26:54.209
And we going to start

01:26:55.944 --> 01:26:56.412
with a segment you'll be seeing
throughout the program

01:27:00.683 --> 01:27:01.384
aptly named Talent Spotlight.

01:29:23.992 --> 01:29:24.560
We just started and
already I am so happy.

01:29:25.728 --> 01:29:26.361
What a surprise, it's me.

01:29:29.097 --> 01:29:29.732
I am always blown away by
what everyone has to offer.

01:29:30.966 --> 01:29:31.733
And there will be more talent

01:29:32.467 --> 01:29:33.468
spotlights
throughout the program.

01:29:35.204 --> 01:29:36.038
But right now,
We are going to get right into

01:29:37.372 --> 01:29:38.106
what you have
all been waiting for...

01:29:39.007 --> 01:29:39.641
the Cosplay.

01:29:42.277 --> 01:29:43.378
Our community does some of
the best cosplay out there

01:29:45.814 --> 01:29:46.949
and we are so excited to
showcase it here for you.

01:29:49.251 --> 01:29:49.585
In the cosplay contest,
the entrants were judged on:

01:29:50.686 --> 01:29:50.886
originality,

01:29:51.753 --> 01:29:52.321
design,

01:29:54.590 --> 01:29:55.257
creativity, and execution.

01:29:55.958 --> 01:29:57.025
For our first cosplay category,

01:29:59.795 --> 01:30:00.329
no one does character, armor,
weapons better than Blizzard.

01:30:01.663 --> 01:30:02.497
And this year, we're ahh

01:30:03.599 --> 01:30:04.533
doing something
a little different

01:30:05.601 --> 01:30:05.968
to introduce
some of those contest finalists.

01:30:09.571 --> 01:30:09.771
We're shining a light on the
community members from each

01:30:11.240 --> 01:30:12.374
of the six blizzard franchises,

01:30:13.175 --> 01:30:13.809
who are making a difference
within their communities

01:30:15.677 --> 01:30:15.811
by bringing people together
through gaming.

01:30:17.646 --> 01:30:17.913
To start us off here is

01:30:20.849 --> 01:30:21.416
Vitor Ravnus Silveira.

01:30:22.784 --> 01:30:23.919
Hi there, my name is
Vitor Silveira.

01:30:27.723 --> 01:30:28.290
I'm also known as Ravnus or Rav
and I'm from Brazil.

01:30:28.790 --> 01:30:29.892
For those who don't know,

01:30:32.261 --> 01:30:33.195
I am the creator of a project
called Ecopoint Brazil.

01:30:35.097 --> 01:30:35.998
This project has been
a lifesaver for me

01:30:37.332 --> 01:30:38.066
and for some members
of the community.

01:30:40.102 --> 01:30:41.003
We've been able to connect
in a whole different way.

01:30:43.639 --> 01:30:44.106
We've been doing,
like, a lot of work

01:30:46.608 --> 01:30:46.742
for the environment

01:30:50.612 --> 01:30:50.712
planting, doing reforesting,
cleaning.

01:30:52.514 --> 01:30:53.081
I want to thank everyone for

01:30:54.082 --> 01:30:54.616
helping me and allowing me

01:30:55.784 --> 01:30:56.652
to make this come true.

01:30:57.786 --> 01:30:58.620
Overwatch was a
life changer for me.

01:30:59.855 --> 01:31:00.822
I loved the universe,
I loved ...

01:31:02.391 --> 01:31:02.925
the characters,
they are amazing, I loved

01:31:04.092 --> 01:31:04.293
the soundtrack, I loved

01:31:07.663 --> 01:31:08.697
the gameplay.
I love how the game works

01:31:13.068 --> 01:31:13.635
and the lore ... was that
allowed me to create

01:31:14.903 --> 01:31:15.103
the project Ecopoint so...

01:31:17.439 --> 01:31:18.373
That changed my life forever.

01:31:20.876 --> 01:31:22.077
And now ... here are
the finalists and winner

01:31:25.447 --> 01:31:25.714
for this year's cosplay and
weapons and armor category.

01:31:29.484 --> 01:35:32.727
# UPBEAT MUSIC

01:35:33.929 --> 01:35:34.863
Another amazing spotlight.

01:35:37.432 --> 01:35:38.400
And congratulations
to all the finalists

01:35:39.267 --> 01:35:39.868
of the weapons and armor
cosplay category.

01:35:41.636 --> 01:35:42.771
The winner on hire a cosplay

01:35:45.173 --> 01:35:45.307
is now qualified for the best
in-show cosplay award

01:35:46.241 --> 01:35:46.374
at the end of the program.

01:35:46.908 --> 01:35:47.943
Moving on...

01:35:51.413 --> 01:35:51.980
Storytelling is what really
captures our attention

01:35:52.981 --> 01:35:53.882
and keeps bringing us back

01:35:55.350 --> 01:35:55.817
to the worlds and realms of
Blizzard.

01:35:57.519 --> 01:35:58.320
And this community, you guys,

01:36:00.322 --> 01:36:00.589
you're so great because
you take those stories

01:36:01.923 --> 01:36:02.123
and you make them your own.

01:36:03.792 --> 01:36:03.992
So now, let's take a look

01:36:05.794 --> 01:36:06.094
at the third place finalist

01:36:06.695 --> 01:36:08.863
for Digital Storytelling.

01:36:11.533 --> 01:36:17.572
# MUSIC IN CRESCENDO

01:36:20.008 --> 01:36:22.477
MARCHING STEPS

01:36:23.879 --> 01:36:28.016
It's over, Sylvanus.

01:36:29.718 --> 01:36:33.588
Stop this bloodshed.

01:36:34.756 --> 01:36:34.923
Jeyna.

01:36:38.193 --> 01:36:38.627
If Silvanus responds with
terms that are acceptable to me,

01:36:39.361 --> 01:36:40.528
peace is upon us.

01:36:43.265 --> 01:36:43.531
No one is better suited to
discuss the matter further.

01:36:45.433 --> 01:36:46.601
I trust in Genn Greymaine.

01:36:49.538 --> 01:36:50.939
There you are, a Lions dog.

01:36:53.241 --> 01:36:53.541
DOG PANTING

01:36:57.279 --> 01:36:57.846
The horde is now at
open war with the alliance.

01:37:01.483 --> 01:37:01.817
Has Stormwind finally
come out to play?

01:37:02.651 --> 01:37:03.218
DOG PANTING

01:37:04.586 --> 01:37:05.220
I have no time for games.

01:37:06.721 --> 01:37:06.988
Not while I reign.

01:37:11.793 --> 01:37:15.430
This war will not end
until we stand victorious.

01:37:17.299 --> 01:37:19.701
Such a feeble mind.

01:37:20.335 --> 01:37:21.002
No!

01:37:23.605 --> 01:37:25.473
Do not keep me waiting.

01:37:28.276 --> 01:37:28.410
You have no idea
what you're up against.

01:37:30.512 --> 01:37:30.779
My victory was inevitable.

01:37:34.249 --> 01:37:35.083
The forsaken will
never stop fighting.

01:37:36.518 --> 01:37:37.118
Ugh! Fool!

01:37:39.754 --> 01:37:39.921
I don't do bouncy.

01:37:41.056 --> 01:37:41.623
DOG WHIMPERS

01:37:42.991 --> 01:37:43.325
Enough of your insolence.

01:37:45.327 --> 01:37:45.661
Look up and around you.

01:37:47.896 --> 01:37:47.996
This is war.

01:37:50.799 --> 01:37:54.002
Time is a luxury
we do not possess.

01:37:55.170 --> 01:37:55.670
DOG BARKS

01:37:58.740 --> 01:38:00.442
#HEAVY DRUMMING MUSIC

01:38:00.775 --> 01:38:02.811
Nathanos

01:38:05.180 --> 01:38:05.447
give me a moment.

01:38:06.614 --> 01:38:21.529
#DRAMATIC BONE MUSIC

01:38:23.198 --> 01:38:24.032
Interesting.

01:38:26.401 --> 01:38:26.735
You truly have the
stomach for war.

01:38:30.472 --> 01:38:31.439
You, it seems have
a genuine taste for it.

01:38:34.076 --> 01:38:34.543
I require the services
of one whom I can trust.

01:38:37.679 --> 01:38:44.052
One to witness true power.

01:38:45.687 --> 01:38:46.988
BONES FALLING

01:38:48.290 --> 01:38:50.592
For you!

01:38:52.160 --> 01:38:55.230
BONE NOISES

01:38:58.233 --> 01:38:58.533
This will be a
convenient partnership.

01:38:58.733 --> 01:39:00.735
DOG WHINES

01:39:03.972 --> 01:39:07.475
I will have need of you.

01:39:09.143 --> 01:39:10.645
For the Horde!

01:39:13.047 --> 01:39:16.551
Wow! Well, I'm embarrassed.

01:39:21.990 --> 01:39:22.524
DARREN: And cue 1,342. Go!

01:39:23.224 --> 01:39:24.058
Lee, camera four.

01:39:26.194 --> 01:39:26.828
I want a slow pan in on the
host.

01:39:27.962 --> 01:39:28.663
A DePaul mover, number seven.

01:39:32.033 --> 01:39:32.634
No, Lee that's a DePaul move
number six.

01:39:33.301 --> 01:39:33.568
Are we not paying attention?

01:39:34.302 --> 01:39:34.736
Slowly.

01:39:36.738 --> 01:39:37.071
Slow! Slowly, Lee!

01:39:37.872 --> 01:39:38.406
Slowly, Lee!

01:39:41.409 --> 01:39:41.743
O aye aye!
OK, let's go to camera three.

01:39:42.210 --> 01:39:43.278
Epp! That's not working.

01:39:44.579 --> 01:39:45.613
Hi! Since no one is here,
I thought I'd take...

01:39:46.881 --> 01:39:47.449
RADIO: Someone tell Darren
there's no camera there.

01:39:48.950 --> 01:39:49.284
I've gone mad with power.

01:39:52.220 --> 01:39:52.954
(MAD LAUGH)

01:39:54.622 --> 01:39:55.256
Now, we're gonna
move right along

01:39:56.524 --> 01:39:56.991
to the next cosplay category,

01:39:57.859 --> 01:39:58.326
Blizzard character.

01:40:00.462 --> 01:40:00.595
Let's get to know Scott Levy,

01:40:02.564 --> 01:40:03.097
AKA - Bites!

01:40:04.399 --> 01:40:04.566
As he helps to
introduce the finalists

01:40:06.568 --> 01:40:06.968
OK Lee, let's go!

01:40:07.869 --> 01:40:08.203
Cue Number One.

01:40:08.970 --> 01:40:09.871
Back to one!

01:40:11.606 --> 01:40:11.739
-RADIO: Nobody tell Darren.
-Brilliant

01:40:12.674 --> 01:40:13.541
Lee, this is great.

01:40:15.310 --> 01:40:15.910
Keep going! Keep going!
Keep going!

01:40:17.245 --> 01:40:17.512
You went too far Lee! O God!

01:40:18.246 --> 01:40:19.214
Hey I'm Scott Levy,

01:40:20.482 --> 01:40:21.082
also known as Hearthstone
Innkeeper Bites,

01:40:21.983 --> 01:40:22.884
and I'm in Phoenix Arizona.

01:40:24.452 --> 01:40:25.053
Over the years I've gotten
a reputation of

01:40:26.120 --> 01:40:26.187
hosting over-the-top events.

01:40:26.788 --> 01:40:27.522
And for me

01:40:29.357 --> 01:40:30.559
first these gatherings became
a kind of creative outlet.

01:40:31.860 --> 01:40:32.494
As someone who gets lots of joy
for hosting live events,

01:40:34.362 --> 01:40:35.630
it's been an
especially difficult year.

01:40:37.966 --> 01:40:38.700
It hasn't stopped me connecting
with my Hearthstone family.

01:40:39.767 --> 01:40:40.768
Being restricted
to online events

01:40:41.936 --> 01:40:42.804
has pushed me to create
some unique tournaments

01:40:43.505 --> 01:40:44.105
like Battle Blitz and
Battle Grind.

01:40:44.806 --> 01:40:45.673
I've gotten to the point now

01:40:46.774 --> 01:40:47.742
where I've mentored
other innkeepers

01:40:49.244 --> 01:40:50.078
and provide them with
tools and resources

01:40:52.213 --> 01:40:52.614
and training to help
make their events better.

01:40:53.848 --> 01:40:54.516
I run some charity events and

01:40:55.817 --> 01:40:56.918
and created resources online
for everyone to use

01:40:58.319 --> 01:40:59.554
and giving back to the community
means a lot to me.

01:41:01.756 --> 01:41:02.390
One of the things that I miss
the most of course is Blizzcon.

01:41:04.292 --> 01:41:04.893
I miss all the people
and the live tournaments

01:41:05.593 --> 01:41:06.528
and the spectacle of it all

01:41:08.796 --> 01:41:09.230
and I even miss the
2 1/2 hours it takes

01:41:10.598 --> 01:41:11.432
of glue and make up and paint

01:41:13.568 --> 01:41:14.769
to transform me into
The Innkeeper.

01:41:16.437 --> 01:41:17.739
And as much work as it is
to transform me into this guy,

01:41:19.941 --> 01:41:20.575
I know many people who put much
more work into their cosplay.

01:41:22.043 --> 01:41:22.977
So I'm thrilled that this year

01:41:23.845 --> 01:41:24.212
we get to see some more
amazing cosplay.

01:41:26.247 --> 01:41:27.015
And now here are the finalists

01:41:28.383 --> 01:41:28.750
and winner
of this year's cosplay,

01:41:29.484 --> 01:41:30.652
Wizard characters category.

01:41:32.720 --> 01:42:27.675
# GUITAR MUSIC

01:42:29.777 --> 01:43:02.343
# MUSIC CONTINUES

01:43:05.013 --> 01:44:03.905
# ELECTRIC GUITAR MUSIC

01:44:07.809 --> 01:46:37.124
# HEAVY METAL MUSIC

01:46:40.695 --> 01:46:56.711
# MUSIC SLOWS DOWN

01:46:57.812 --> 01:46:59.046
Congratulations to Hartigan

01:47:01.382 --> 01:47:02.316
for winning the cosplay award
for best Blizzard character.

01:47:03.084 --> 01:47:03.951
Stick around, at the
end of the showcase

01:47:04.886 --> 01:47:05.486
to see if they take
home the coveted

01:47:07.955 --> 01:47:08.089
Best in show cosplay award.

01:47:09.223 --> 01:47:09.824
It's coming up

01:47:10.091 --> 01:47:10.925
at the end of the showcase.

01:47:12.860 --> 01:47:13.461
But right now,
we have the second place

01:47:14.395 --> 01:47:14.795
Digital storytelling piece.

01:47:15.429 --> 01:47:16.163
And my friends,

01:47:19.600 --> 01:47:20.434
it is a musical delight.
# CLAPS

