01:50:38.532 --> 01:50:39.200
All cosplay takes imagination,

01:50:40.868 --> 01:50:41.302
artistry, creativity, ingenuity.

01:50:44.271 --> 01:50:44.738
But for our category of
traditional creation.

01:50:46.941 --> 01:50:47.708
We wanna reward
those who displayed

01:50:48.976 --> 01:50:49.443
the highest levels
of craftsmanship

01:50:50.744 --> 01:50:51.378
through cutting,
sewing, fastening

01:50:52.913 --> 01:50:53.214
and use of classic materials.

01:50:55.716 --> 01:50:56.383
So, to announce the finalists

01:50:58.152 --> 01:50:58.652
in traditional creation cosplay,

01:51:00.688 --> 01:51:01.022
we have Diablo 3 content creator

01:51:02.490 --> 01:51:02.690
Wolfcryer.

01:51:06.060 --> 01:51:06.961
Hey ladies and gentlemen
my name is James McDermott

01:51:10.431 --> 01:51:11.365
but online
I am better known as Wolfcryer,

01:51:13.634 --> 01:51:14.268
a Diablo 3 streamer
and content creator.

01:51:16.570 --> 01:51:17.438
Also the founder of
Level With a Cause

01:51:17.972 --> 01:51:18.839
which is a
charity fundraising event

01:51:21.108 --> 01:51:21.642
that coincides
with the start of each

01:51:22.877 --> 01:51:23.244
new season in Diablo 3.

01:51:25.179 --> 01:51:26.247
We've been doing this
since season 11

01:51:28.883 --> 01:51:29.617
and thanks to a ton of
my fellow content creators

01:51:32.186 --> 01:51:33.220
and the generosity of
the Diablo 3 community

01:51:35.589 --> 01:51:36.090
this effort has managed
to raise over $80,000

01:51:36.957 --> 01:51:37.491
for various charities

01:51:38.192 --> 01:51:39.227
over the last few years.

01:51:42.029 --> 01:51:42.930
2020 brought many challenges
to our daily lives

01:51:45.399 --> 01:51:45.733
but gaming and,
in particular for me,

01:51:47.801 --> 01:51:48.402
Diablo 3 and
its fantastic community

01:51:51.539 --> 01:51:52.640
brought me at least some
sense of that normalcy

01:51:53.974 --> 01:51:54.442
that I think we were
all trying to find last year.

01:51:56.677 --> 01:51:57.211
Some of my best
memories that I have

01:51:59.313 --> 01:51:59.480
have come from Blizzcon.

01:52:03.551 --> 01:52:04.151
These are truly moments
that I can never ever forget

01:52:05.352 --> 01:52:06.187
and I personally can't wait

01:52:07.154 --> 01:52:07.821
until we all have
that opportunity

01:52:10.157 --> 01:52:10.691
to meet up in person once again.

01:52:14.094 --> 01:52:15.262
But now... here are
the finalists and winners

01:52:18.699 --> 01:52:18.833
for this year's cosplay
traditional creation category.

01:52:22.036 --> 01:52:33.614
# INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC

01:52:35.783 --> 01:54:07.775
# TECHNO MUSIC

01:54:09.543 --> 01:55:33.460
# DRUM MUSIC

01:55:33.994 --> 01:55:34.995
And now!

01:55:37.231 --> 01:55:37.798
It's time to give out
the first place award

01:55:38.899 --> 01:55:39.333
for digital storytelling.

01:55:39.867 --> 01:55:40.768
And for this piece

01:55:42.236 --> 01:55:43.103
a group of Overwatch
community members

01:55:45.105 --> 01:55:45.739
came together
from around the globe

01:55:48.675 --> 01:55:48.942
to create something
truly fantastic.

01:55:50.611 --> 01:55:50.811
Let me tell you my friends,

01:55:52.546 --> 01:55:53.013
they delivered the payload.

01:55:54.482 --> 01:56:05.726
Let's take a look.

01:56:08.796 --> 01:56:09.096
OK, let's get cracking.

01:56:10.564 --> 01:56:10.898
Oh, better get my coffee.

01:56:15.335 --> 01:56:15.836
FLASH FLASH

01:56:16.870 --> 01:56:17.204
All right, good to go

01:56:18.605 --> 01:56:19.339
and, right on time.

01:56:21.375 --> 01:56:21.675
# BING
Reinhart, how are you?

01:56:23.877 --> 01:56:24.978
(DEEP VOICE) Ughh, good I
suppose

01:56:27.781 --> 01:56:27.948
but I'm still not sure about
this Internet meeting.

01:56:30.317 --> 01:56:31.084
Ohh, you'll get used to it
big guy.

01:56:33.687 --> 01:56:34.254
Now can you screen share a plan
of attack on sector seven.

01:56:36.190 --> 01:56:36.323
What's share? Share what?

01:56:38.091 --> 01:56:38.325
What are you speaking of?

01:56:41.428 --> 01:56:41.695
Hold that thought,
Brigitte is in the waiting room.

01:56:43.230 --> 01:56:43.430
Where? What room?

01:56:45.566 --> 01:56:45.999
Where is my beloved goddaughter?

01:56:47.167 --> 01:56:47.568
I do not see her.

01:56:48.635 --> 01:56:49.136
BING CAT MEOWING

01:56:50.637 --> 01:56:51.271
Brigitte, how are y...

01:56:51.505 --> 01:56:51.638
-Uhhhh.
-#Cat miaowing

01:56:53.307 --> 01:56:54.341
Ahhh! What is that?

01:56:57.277 --> 01:56:57.644
That's just Mitsy
she hasn't had her "Linner" yet.

01:56:59.580 --> 01:57:00.247
What's a "Linner"?

01:57:01.682 --> 01:57:02.649
Half way between
lunch and dinner.

01:57:05.385 --> 01:57:05.519
She gets cranky if she
doesn't get it on time.

01:57:07.688 --> 01:57:08.522
No, Mitsy, no! Behave!

01:57:12.392 --> 01:57:12.759
-(MISY MEWING)
-Okay, well, anyway.

01:57:13.026 --> 01:57:13.260
Here's Genji.

01:57:14.528 --> 01:57:17.798
# BING

01:57:19.833 --> 01:57:20.934
Uhh, Genji,
we can't hear you.

01:57:23.737 --> 01:57:24.238
Genji, turn off mute.

01:57:26.874 --> 01:57:27.274
There you go,
what were you saying?

01:57:28.809 --> 01:57:29.276
I need healing.

01:57:29.710 --> 01:57:30.310
That's worse.

01:57:33.180 --> 01:57:33.714
Genji, we need you to focus,
all right.

01:57:34.948 --> 01:57:35.415
GENJI BATTLE CRY

01:57:37.084 --> 01:57:37.351
What just happened?

01:57:41.288 --> 01:57:41.555
OK, moving on, Mei's here.

01:57:43.423 --> 01:57:43.790
# BING
Hi, Mei.

01:57:45.225 --> 01:57:45.592
WHIRRING NOISE

01:57:48.095 --> 01:57:48.295
Oh, May, Stop!

01:57:50.130 --> 01:57:50.364
Sorry, sorry, sorry (LAUGHS)

01:57:52.266 --> 01:57:52.799
I was just making a milkshake.

01:57:54.201 --> 01:57:54.468
A little hot where I am.

01:57:56.136 --> 01:57:56.637
Don't you live in the Arctic?

01:57:59.206 --> 01:57:59.473
Yes, it's summer here.

01:58:00.107 --> 01:58:01.241
(HESITANT) OK.

01:58:04.912 --> 01:58:05.145
Nina, I did some research
on the Internet machines.

01:58:06.146 --> 01:58:06.413
I can screen share.

01:58:07.881 --> 01:58:08.215
That's wonderful.

01:58:10.217 --> 01:58:10.717
Now I can finally get
something done.

01:58:11.418 --> 01:58:11.585
# BEEPING
Oh, no.

01:58:13.720 --> 01:58:14.588
We losing connection.

01:58:15.255 --> 01:58:15.789
What is happening?
ELECTRONIC STUTTER

01:58:16.490 --> 01:58:17.057
I wish to screen share.

01:58:18.325 --> 01:58:18.725
I wish to show my skills.

01:58:20.494 --> 01:58:20.928
I live for this
(ELECTRONIC STUTTERING)

01:58:21.428 --> 01:58:22.195
ELECTRONIC BUZZING

01:58:23.130 --> 01:58:23.997
(ELECTRONIC VOICE)
Hello, Hello...

01:58:25.899 --> 01:58:26.733
REINHARDT: Hello
ELECTRONIC WHIRRING

01:58:27.968 --> 01:58:28.435
Oh bbbugggg...
ELECTRONIC EXPLOSION

01:58:31.638 --> 01:58:32.506
ELECTRONIC WHIRRING

01:58:34.274 --> 01:58:35.475
KISS NOISE

01:58:37.344 --> 01:59:02.836
# UPBEAT MUSIC

01:59:03.604 --> 01:59:04.638
Over the years,

01:59:06.540 --> 01:59:07.074
techniques for creating
costumes have evolved

01:59:07.574 --> 01:59:08.609
with current technology

01:59:10.978 --> 01:59:11.945
which has made for grander
and grander cosplay.

01:59:13.847 --> 01:59:14.915
So, right now,
we are going to award those

01:59:17.818 --> 01:59:18.018
who have used crafting
technology to its fullest

01:59:19.820 --> 01:59:19.920
to bring forth, the most...

01:59:23.924 --> 01:59:24.458
epic of modern creation cosplay.

01:59:26.226 --> 01:59:26.360
To help us introduce
the finalist,

01:59:30.330 --> 01:59:30.597
we have StarCraft Streamer
Livibee.

01:59:32.099 --> 01:59:33.133
Hi, my name's Olivia Seedo.

01:59:34.835 --> 01:59:35.436
Most people know me
by my gamer tag, Livibee.

01:59:38.338 --> 01:59:39.406
I'm a streamer and cosplayer
from Sydney, Australia,

01:59:41.441 --> 01:59:42.209
and I've been playing Blizzard
games since I was ten year's old

01:59:44.578 --> 01:59:44.678
so they hold a
special place in my heart.

01:59:47.514 --> 01:59:48.048
StarCraft is the
hardest game I've ever played

01:59:50.183 --> 01:59:51.151
and getting Grandmaster
for the first time

01:59:52.419 --> 01:59:52.786
was easily one of the
best moments of my life.

01:59:54.988 --> 01:59:55.656
I was finally able to break
through that skill ceiling.

01:59:57.991 --> 01:59:58.425
A goal I was driven
to achieve for years

02:00:00.360 --> 02:00:00.927
and something
I definitely wouldn't

02:00:01.228 --> 02:00:02.229
have been able to achieve

02:00:03.797 --> 02:00:04.164
if not for the love and
support of my community.

02:00:06.066 --> 02:00:07.067
Streaming has really
allowed for myself and

02:00:09.403 --> 02:00:09.670
others to stay connected
during the pandemic.

02:00:10.771 --> 02:00:11.805
And even if you're someone

02:00:12.939 --> 02:00:13.740
that isn't used to staying
inside all the time,

02:00:15.809 --> 02:00:16.877
there's always a place for you
to hang out with people

02:00:19.580 --> 02:00:20.147
who share the same passion
for gaming as you do.

02:00:21.214 --> 02:00:22.182
Shout out to the Beehive.

02:00:23.183 --> 02:00:24.317
For the past year or so

02:00:26.586 --> 02:00:26.920
I've also been incredibly
passionate about cosplay.

02:00:29.589 --> 02:00:29.956
My favorite character to
cosplay of course is Diva.

02:00:30.924 --> 02:00:31.491
She is definitely my video game

02:00:34.294 --> 02:00:34.594
character kindred spirit.

02:00:36.430 --> 02:00:36.830
But that's enough about me.

02:00:37.497 --> 02:00:38.598
Here are the
finalists and winners

02:00:40.667 --> 02:00:40.967
for this year's cosplay
modern creation category.

02:00:43.403 --> 02:02:39.219
# UPBEAT MUSIC

02:02:39.920 --> 02:02:41.454
There's more show to come.

02:02:43.190 --> 02:02:43.390
But before we continue

02:02:43.957 --> 02:02:44.925
we'd like to take a moment

02:02:46.159 --> 02:02:46.660
to recognize one of our
community members

02:02:48.361 --> 02:02:48.829
who passed away
earlier this year.

02:02:53.700 --> 02:02:54.434
Jarod Nandin took
the Blizzcon stage in 2013

02:02:57.070 --> 02:02:58.338
in an unforgettable Southpark
World of Warcraft cosplay.

02:02:58.705 --> 02:02:59.372
Creativity

02:03:00.774 --> 02:03:01.775
is the defining trait of what

02:03:04.344 --> 02:03:04.611
we try to put on display
during community night.

02:03:05.145 --> 02:03:05.412
And Jarod...

02:03:08.081 --> 02:03:08.748
Jarod was one
of the most creative ones

02:03:09.916 --> 02:03:10.851
to ever walk the Blizzcon stage.

02:03:12.052 --> 02:03:12.552
Our cosplay community

02:03:14.721 --> 02:03:17.691
deeply feels this loss.

02:03:19.759 --> 02:03:20.627
Jarod Nandin.

02:03:22.462 --> 02:03:23.430
How do you kill
that which has no life?

02:03:24.464 --> 02:03:59.332
# MUSIC CONTINUES

02:04:01.635 --> 02:05:42.168
# ETHEREAL MUSIC

02:05:46.506 --> 02:06:31.718
# DRUM MUSIC

02:06:34.254 --> 02:06:35.021
HUMMING

02:06:37.891 --> 02:06:37.958
Oh, hi, I didn't see you there
I'm just...

02:06:40.193 --> 02:06:40.627
Alone in an empty theatre
creating...

02:06:43.263 --> 02:06:44.030
this masterpiece.

02:06:48.435 --> 02:06:48.868
(LAUGHING) Yes and
(LOUDLY) paint brush down.

02:06:49.602 --> 02:06:49.869
(LAUGHING) Ahaha!

02:06:50.937 --> 02:06:51.438
Seriously...

02:06:51.738 --> 02:06:52.272
The Blizzard community

02:06:54.207 --> 02:06:54.841
creates some of the most

02:06:56.209 --> 02:06:56.876
impressive fan art out there.

02:06:57.911 --> 02:06:58.778
And a big thank you to all those

02:07:00.146 --> 02:07:00.580
who submitted
their fantastic work.

02:07:02.282 --> 02:07:03.249
Look, I was a little late
submitting mine

02:07:03.817 --> 02:07:04.851
so unfortunately
I could not be considered

02:07:07.554 --> 02:07:08.288
to enter the contest
but I will let all of you

02:07:10.356 --> 02:07:10.423
give me your opinion.

02:07:11.524 --> 02:07:12.125
You be the judge.

02:07:13.493 --> 02:07:13.726
It's really good, right?

02:07:15.962 --> 02:07:16.229
I'm a very fragile individual.

02:07:17.230 --> 02:07:18.398
But, come on.

02:07:19.766 --> 02:07:20.667
Let's see who the winners
of this year's art contest are.

02:07:22.869 --> 02:07:23.303
And, friends
to announce the finalists,

02:07:24.337 --> 02:07:25.238
we have Jazzalene

02:07:26.139 --> 02:07:26.272
from the Heroes of
the Storm community.

02:07:28.274 --> 02:07:28.641
(LIKE A PIRATE) Haharrgg

02:07:29.409 --> 02:07:30.310
Hi guys, my name is Brook,

02:07:31.845 --> 02:07:32.412
but most of you know me
as Jazzalene.

02:07:34.013 --> 02:07:35.181
I'm from Trenton,
Ontario, Canada

02:07:36.649 --> 02:07:37.584
but I've called California home
now for over 4 years.

02:07:38.251 --> 02:07:39.486
I stream and I cast
Heroes of the Storm

02:07:41.221 --> 02:07:41.855
but I'm also the creator and
organizer of Girls Gank Squad,

02:07:43.823 --> 02:07:44.424
an all-female community
created to highlight

02:07:45.725 --> 02:07:46.092
and support women in gaming.

02:07:46.926 --> 02:07:47.794
In 2020 alone

02:07:50.663 --> 02:07:51.264
Girls Gank Squad was
able to raise over $10,500

02:07:52.699 --> 02:07:53.600
for charities such as Rain,

02:07:54.601 --> 02:07:55.168
the Breast Cancer
Research Foundation

02:07:55.869 --> 02:07:56.436
and Marine Toys for Tots.

02:07:57.370 --> 02:07:58.371
One of my favorite things

02:07:59.506 --> 02:08:00.340
about Heroes of the Storm
is the community.

02:08:00.974 --> 02:08:01.774
I've never been
surrounded by such

02:08:03.076 --> 02:08:03.143
generous and
compassionate people

02:08:04.010 --> 02:08:04.911
They make the events

02:08:05.745 --> 02:08:06.146
Girls Gank Squad
put on so successful.

02:08:07.981 --> 02:08:08.047
But enough of that stuff.

02:08:08.848 --> 02:08:09.883
Every year at Blizzcon

02:08:11.484 --> 02:08:12.285
I'm absolutely blown away
by the talented artists

02:08:13.586 --> 02:08:14.154
that submit work for
the art contest.

02:08:14.420 --> 02:08:15.255
Here are the finalists and

02:08:16.556 --> 02:08:17.657
winner of this
year's Art contest.

02:08:20.493 --> 02:09:09.876
# EPIC MUSIC

02:09:12.445 --> 02:09:17.050
# WARBRINGERS JAINA COVER

02:09:18.751 --> 02:09:53.886
(SINGING IN CHINESE)

02:09:55.421 --> 02:11:55.875
(SINGING CONTINUES)

02:11:59.078 --> 02:11:59.946
Congratulations to Zhon Yung
for winning the art contest

02:12:01.447 --> 02:12:01.981
with that amazing
villainous piece.

02:12:03.716 --> 02:12:04.317
Well, look, I thought I
was going to introduce

02:12:05.318 --> 02:12:06.252
our special guest right now

02:12:08.421 --> 02:12:08.988
but there seems to be
a bit of a hiccup.

02:12:09.956 --> 02:12:10.590
But look I am from theatre

02:12:13.426 --> 02:12:13.626
and uh-uh the show must go on.

02:12:14.394 --> 02:12:15.362
MATTHEW: Sorry.

02:12:17.163 --> 02:12:17.764
Sorry, I had to finish
putting all this on.

02:12:19.832 --> 02:12:20.500
Gun's stuck there... I just
wanna (STRUGGLING) Oh, I got it.

02:12:22.668 --> 02:12:23.669
You look great, this is amazing.

02:12:25.705 --> 02:12:26.472
One question,
why are you dressed as McCree.

02:12:30.476 --> 02:12:31.110
You... asked me to
come in cosplay

02:12:31.344 --> 02:12:32.011
for the... community showcase

02:12:33.613 --> 02:12:34.481
It's about introducing cosplay.

02:12:36.149 --> 02:12:37.016
It's ok, it's fine
You look fantastic

02:12:38.284 --> 02:12:38.418
Well, thank you,
much obliged (LAUGHING).

02:12:39.552 --> 02:12:40.820
Figured it was

02:12:42.155 --> 02:12:43.189
this or the pajamas I've been
wearing for the past 10 months

02:12:45.525 --> 02:12:46.059
and I think this has
an air of professionalism

02:12:46.259 --> 02:12:46.459
over the previous, so...

02:12:48.895 --> 02:12:49.362
I've been wearing a suit
all the time.

02:12:49.929 --> 02:12:50.463
That's the epitome
of professional.

02:12:52.365 --> 02:12:53.366
Well... (DARREN LAUGHS)

02:12:54.601 --> 02:12:55.535
Well, thank you speaking of that
professionalism,

02:12:57.603 --> 02:12:58.271
would you help me
bring the hammer down

02:12:58.971 --> 02:12:59.906
by introducing the next segment?

02:13:02.008 --> 02:13:02.375
It would be an honor,
if you don't mind.

02:13:03.443 --> 02:13:04.243
(LAUGHS) So...

02:13:05.244 --> 02:13:05.912
The Blizzard
community as we know

02:13:07.713 --> 02:13:08.581
does cosplay better than anyone.

02:13:08.948 --> 02:13:10.149
So, thank you for the
time spent on

02:13:12.652 --> 02:13:13.653
bringing blizzard characters
to life in incredible ways.

02:13:13.986 --> 02:13:14.821
So let's take a look at
some of our entrants

02:13:16.689 --> 02:13:18.524
in this year's
cosplay exhibition.

02:13:20.760 --> 02:15:07.400
# EPIC MUSIC

02:15:10.403 --> 02:16:44.430
# MUSIC CONTINUES

02:16:45.097 --> 02:16:46.599
And we're back.

02:16:47.900 --> 02:16:48.835
Why are you
taking off your costume?

02:16:50.803 --> 02:16:51.070
I told you, I've been wearing
it as pajamas for about a year.

02:16:52.705 --> 02:16:53.773
It's getting hot.

02:16:55.875 --> 02:16:56.909
(SIGHS) However I do
want to say a huge thank you

02:16:57.777 --> 02:16:58.411
to all the amazing entrants
to our exhibition.

02:17:00.246 --> 02:17:01.213
incredible costumes
and easily one of

02:17:02.148 --> 02:17:02.315
my favorite parts every
year here at Blizzcon.

02:17:04.784 --> 02:17:04.984
And now my friends, it is time.

02:17:08.788 --> 02:17:09.455
The award for this
year's cosplay best in show

02:17:12.324 --> 02:17:12.992
will go to one of the four
cosplay category winners.

02:17:13.793 --> 02:17:14.360
And to help us present the award

02:17:16.562 --> 02:17:16.862
all the way from France...

02:17:20.433 --> 02:18:42.515
(FRENCH ACCENT) Here is...
Zeretor.

02:18:43.983 --> 02:20:03.162
#TRIUMPHANT MUSIC

02:20:07.066 --> 02:20:08.033
And that's it for our
Blizzconline Community Showcase.

02:20:09.768 --> 02:20:10.803
-Congratulations to Hartigan
-MATTHEW YELPS

02:20:12.504 --> 02:20:13.272
For winning the cosplay
Best in show contest.

02:20:15.441 --> 02:20:16.008
-Hartigan.
-Hartigan. (LAUGHS)

02:20:19.111 --> 02:20:20.045
And thank you Matt
for joining me every year.

02:20:21.280 --> 02:20:21.881
Every time that I get
to spend with you

02:20:23.015 --> 02:20:23.983
is more special
than I can possibly say.

02:20:25.651 --> 02:20:26.619
Oo, you make me blush.
Truly the honor is mine.

02:20:26.986 --> 02:20:28.087
I've been at Blizzcon
since it started and

02:20:30.790 --> 02:20:31.090
sharing this space with you is
always an absolute joy.

02:20:31.991 --> 02:20:32.958
Thank you.

02:20:35.327 --> 02:20:35.661
And, congratulations
to all our finalists.

02:20:36.228 --> 02:20:37.529
And thank you

02:20:38.731 --> 02:20:39.798
to all the community members who
participated in our showcase.

02:20:42.801 --> 02:20:43.168
And finally thanks to
all you watching at home.

02:20:45.271 --> 02:20:45.638
Look, friends,

02:20:47.172 --> 02:20:47.773
even though we're still
staying safe

02:20:49.508 --> 02:20:50.075
by playing a part together,

02:20:50.643 --> 02:20:51.310
hopefully, if we're lucky,

02:20:53.646 --> 02:20:54.146
we'll see you sooner than later

02:20:55.081 --> 02:20:55.381
at our next Blizzcon.

02:20:59.485 --> 02:21:00.219
-Until then, I'm Darren.
-And I'm Matt.

02:21:00.886 --> 02:21:01.287
Stay safe.

02:21:04.156 --> 02:21:04.590
(LOUD VOICE) We love you
MATT BLOWS A KISS

02:21:06.258 --> 02:21:42.528
BOTH LAUGH LOUDLY

02:21:44.663 --> 02:21:45.998
Welcome to Sanctuary.

02:21:46.999 --> 02:21:47.967
We here at Critical Role

02:21:49.468 --> 02:21:50.336
are thrilled
to be part of this celebration

02:21:52.037 --> 02:21:53.238
of the 30th anniversary
of Blizzard

02:21:55.641 --> 02:21:56.375
and of course the announcement
of Diablo II Resurrected.

02:21:57.076 --> 02:21:57.343
MATTHEW:
Super excited about it.

02:21:58.477 --> 02:21:59.445
As part of that we

02:21:59.878 --> 02:22:01.146
we are putting together
this very special,

02:22:05.217 --> 02:22:06.018
100% original Diablo one-shot
set in this awesome universe.

02:22:08.654 --> 02:22:09.221
I've been a fan
of Diablo since the first one.

02:22:09.488 --> 02:22:10.456
It was one of the reasons

02:22:12.157 --> 02:22:12.624
I first bought a PC
back in middle school.

02:22:13.459 --> 02:22:13.659
I'm old.

02:22:15.327 --> 02:22:16.395
Super excited to be able to play

02:22:16.962 --> 02:22:18.163
in this space today
with these wonderful people.

02:22:19.765 --> 02:22:20.499
Speaking of wonderful people,

02:22:20.799 --> 02:22:21.600
let's do a round
of introductions

02:22:22.101 --> 02:22:22.468
to our players
for this one-shot,

02:22:23.402 --> 02:22:23.602
beginning with

02:22:24.904 --> 02:22:25.604
MATTHEW: Mica Burton.

02:22:26.171 --> 02:22:26.839
Hi, I'm Mica.

02:22:27.172 --> 02:22:28.140
I'm going to be playing a Wizard

02:22:29.108 --> 02:22:30.075
and I'm super excited
to kill a lot of things,

02:22:31.810 --> 02:22:32.811
because that's
what Diablo's about, right?

02:22:33.479 --> 02:22:34.513
MATTHEW: That's kind of
what Diablo's about.

02:22:34.947 --> 02:22:36.715
-MATTHEW: You got this.
-Awesome. I got this.

02:22:37.483 --> 02:22:38.617
MATTHEW: Laura Bailey.

02:22:39.651 --> 02:22:40.719
That and looting, because
that's what I'm here for.

02:22:43.789 --> 02:22:45.791
Hi, I'm Laura Bailey
and I'm playing Druid today.

02:22:46.725 --> 02:22:47.426
MATTHEW: Brilliant.

02:22:48.127 --> 02:22:48.660
MATTHEW: Liam O'Brien.

02:22:50.029 --> 02:22:51.096
Hello, I'm Liam O'Brien

02:22:52.431 --> 02:22:52.998
and I'm going to be
the Crusader for the group.

02:22:54.366 --> 02:22:55.200
I'm excited to be the Tank

02:22:57.136 --> 02:23:00.572
in a DnD game
for the first time ever.

02:23:01.707 --> 02:23:02.207
MATTHEW: Carlos Luna.

02:23:03.242 --> 02:23:04.143
Hey, I'm Carlos Luna.

02:23:05.811 --> 02:23:06.712
I'm going to be playing
a Necromancer

02:23:09.515 --> 02:23:10.783
with a little demon worm
in his brain.

02:23:13.085 --> 02:23:14.686
-LAURA: Like you do.
-Yeah, like you do.

02:23:15.454 --> 02:23:15.921
MATTHEW: And Marisha.

02:23:16.755 --> 02:23:17.523
Hi, I'm Marisha Ray

02:23:19.625 --> 02:23:19.925
and will be playing
a Demon Hunter

02:23:21.393 --> 02:23:22.194
not voiced by Laura Bailey,

02:23:23.962 --> 02:23:26.665
even though
she's at this table.

02:23:27.666 --> 02:23:28.400
MATTHEW: Meta-awkwardness.

02:23:29.301 --> 02:23:29.435
MARISHA:
Those were my crossbows.

02:23:30.903 --> 02:23:31.870
Is that the sound they make?
I love it. Perfect.

02:23:32.237 --> 02:23:32.971
LIAM: We could find
one moment in the game

02:23:33.672 --> 02:23:34.173
where you could
throw your voice

02:23:35.641 --> 02:23:36.508
and you can just ADR.

02:23:37.576 --> 02:23:38.010
-Can you just lip-sync?
-MARISHA: Sure.

02:23:38.844 --> 02:23:39.278
Like ADR? Perfect.

02:23:40.312 --> 02:23:40.612
Watermelon, watermelon.

02:23:42.748 --> 02:23:45.885
LAURA:
Oh, that's good, Marisha.

02:23:46.819 --> 02:23:49.188
No more of that.

02:23:51.090 --> 02:23:51.990
-MICA: Squash that immediately.
-Exactly.

02:23:53.559 --> 02:23:54.693
If you wanna watch
this campaign again

02:23:56.328 --> 02:23:57.096
or check out any of the other
amazing, free content

02:23:59.431 --> 02:23:59.898
as part of
this BlizzConline event,

02:24:01.366 --> 02:24:02.034
visit BlizzCon.com.

02:24:03.368 --> 02:24:04.403
Tonight's adventure
that you'll see here shortly

02:24:06.105 --> 02:24:06.371
will be available
on our Critical YouTube channel

02:24:07.172 --> 02:24:07.473
soon enough.

02:24:08.340 --> 02:24:09.341
Thanks to Blizzard and BlizzCon

02:24:10.676 --> 02:24:11.810
for bringing us
to be a part of the celebration

02:24:14.079 --> 02:24:14.346
and to make this game possible
as part of the event.

02:24:16.148 --> 02:24:16.982
I think that's it.

02:24:18.283 --> 02:24:19.118
That all being said,
let's go ahead

02:24:20.052 --> 02:24:20.486
and jump
into this special one-shot

02:24:22.154 --> 02:24:22.521
for BlizzConline.

02:24:23.922 --> 02:25:35.327
Diablo.

02:25:38.397 --> 02:25:38.664
In the world of Sanctuary,

02:25:40.966 --> 02:25:41.266
darkness carries far.

02:25:44.503 --> 02:25:45.003
The mortal realm
between the High Heavens

02:25:45.604 --> 02:25:45.871
and the Burning Hells,

02:25:48.273 --> 02:25:48.540
life in these lands
is ever a struggle

02:25:51.877 --> 02:25:52.144
caught in the middle
of this eternal conflict.

02:25:54.713 --> 02:25:55.013
The hearts of men
fall easily to corruption

02:25:58.650 --> 02:25:59.251
and the Ancient Evil
ever seeks to spill

02:25:59.985 --> 02:26:00.619
into this world to sow chaos

02:26:04.389 --> 02:26:05.357
and blanket the realm
in fire and shadow.

02:26:07.893 --> 02:26:07.993
In a time of shallow peace,

02:26:08.627 --> 02:26:09.494
you've each set out

02:26:10.796 --> 02:26:11.230
to make your fortunes
in the world,

02:26:12.264 --> 02:26:13.031
whether to combat the evil

02:26:14.466 --> 02:26:15.534
that lurks
in every lightless space

02:26:16.702 --> 02:26:17.569
or to seek answers

02:26:18.604 --> 02:26:19.238
to the countless
forgotten mysteries

02:26:20.372 --> 02:26:21.640
that call out to the curious.

02:26:22.641 --> 02:26:22.874
You've come together

02:26:26.578 --> 02:26:26.845
in finding common purpose
against the plague of evils

02:26:29.848 --> 02:26:30.415
and made a name for yourselves
in the region of Westmarch.

02:26:31.450 --> 02:26:31.583
Here,

02:26:32.451 --> 02:26:33.418
you find yourself summoned

02:26:36.255 --> 02:26:36.888
by a Horadric scholar
called Deckard Cain.

02:26:40.359 --> 02:26:40.492
Under the dim call
of candlelight,

02:26:42.194 --> 02:26:44.796
Deckard asked for your aid.

02:26:45.897 --> 02:26:46.965
“Hello, my friends."

02:26:50.335 --> 02:26:50.802
"I have heard
of your great deeds already

02:26:53.605 --> 02:26:54.206
and find myself
in need of others

02:26:55.707 --> 02:26:56.742
with such skills as yours."

02:26:57.776 --> 02:26:57.909
"The home of my youth,

02:27:00.212 --> 02:27:01.046
the humble village of Tristram,

02:27:04.082 --> 02:27:04.483
fell to flame
and evil years ago."

02:27:05.217 --> 02:27:05.784
"Abandoned,

02:27:08.954 --> 02:27:09.454
the ruins of Tristram
have since been nothing

02:27:10.722 --> 02:27:11.723
but ash and memories,

02:27:14.860 --> 02:27:15.794
often targeted
by looters and grave robbers."

02:27:16.361 --> 02:27:16.528
"However,

02:27:20.365 --> 02:27:20.999
rumors swirl
of something dark and violent

02:27:22.134 --> 02:27:23.101
stirring beneath the cathedral

02:27:23.769 --> 02:27:24.169
and,

02:27:26.204 --> 02:27:26.838
given the history of that place,

02:27:28.540 --> 02:27:29.374
I've a foreboding worry

02:27:30.976 --> 02:27:32.311
of what
might be lingering there."

02:27:34.279 --> 02:27:35.147
"I would ask you five

02:27:36.682 --> 02:27:36.882
to journey
to the ruins of Tristram,

02:27:39.418 --> 02:27:39.551
seek the source of these rumors

02:27:41.253 --> 02:27:42.120
and cleanse the cathedral

02:27:44.423 --> 02:27:45.090
of what terrors
might reside below."

02:27:48.093 --> 02:27:48.527
"I'd like to put
the souls of those lost,

02:27:49.895 --> 02:27:50.829
finally, to rest."

02:27:54.533 --> 02:27:55.534
After braving days
of freezing wind

02:27:57.235 --> 02:27:57.736
and the persistent rain
that still haunts you...

02:27:58.236 --> 02:27:58.437
CARLOS: 10 out of 10.

02:27:58.837 --> 02:28:00.772
Indeed.

02:28:01.340 --> 02:28:02.274
Sorry, Michael Gough.

02:28:05.010 --> 02:28:05.711
...you finally reach the edge
of the surrounding hills,

02:28:08.280 --> 02:28:08.847
looking down
into the ghastly echo

02:28:09.681 --> 02:28:10.482
of the village once known

02:28:11.516 --> 02:28:12.718
as Tristram.

02:28:14.953 --> 02:28:16.021
Walking through the mud
and charred foundations

02:28:18.357 --> 02:28:19.758
of what you imagine
was once a modest township,

02:28:20.926 --> 02:28:21.993
you can't help but imagine

02:28:24.129 --> 02:28:25.364
what horrors must have fallen
upon the denizens.

02:28:26.765 --> 02:28:27.899
Slowly, your eyes fall upon

02:28:30.135 --> 02:28:30.736
the partially crumbled
stone structure to the north:

02:28:32.003 --> 02:28:33.438
the cathedral.

02:28:34.840 --> 02:28:35.741
You grasp
at your weapons tightly

02:28:39.177 --> 02:28:39.378
as you enter
the semi-fallen structure,

02:28:43.014 --> 02:28:43.215
finding solace
within here from the rain.

02:28:44.916 --> 02:28:45.350
Stepping across the stone floor,

02:28:45.617 --> 02:28:46.518
your vision skips

02:28:48.320 --> 02:28:48.620
from broken window
to fallen candelabra

02:28:49.921 --> 02:28:50.722
until you find the staircase

02:28:52.858 --> 02:28:53.258
descending
into the depths below.

02:28:55.527 --> 02:28:55.861
The shine catches your eye,

02:29:00.465 --> 02:29:02.501
seeing a single gold coin
resting atop the first stair.

02:29:04.503 --> 02:29:04.803
As you descend these steps

02:29:08.407 --> 02:29:09.107
into the first layer
of the crypt below...

02:29:12.177 --> 02:29:12.377
what do they see
as the Demon Hunter

02:29:13.612 --> 02:29:14.146
sets in?

02:29:17.649 --> 02:29:18.417
Two heavy footsteps step in

02:29:21.920 --> 02:29:22.254
and you see a big skull,
a cow skull, first.

02:29:27.259 --> 02:29:27.492
It has detail
of gold filigree emblazoning it,

02:29:32.998 --> 02:29:33.698
with a general calf-skull motif
on the rest of her armor,

02:29:35.133 --> 02:29:35.700
with little flecks of gold,

02:29:36.635 --> 02:29:39.571
and two crossbows.

02:29:40.405 --> 02:29:41.239
This is Tauro,

02:29:42.040 --> 02:29:42.374
the Demon Hunter,

02:29:45.977 --> 02:29:47.012
returning home
to her hometown of Tristram,

02:29:50.415 --> 02:29:50.949
but she hasn't been here
since she was a little girl...

02:29:52.851 --> 02:29:54.786
growing up on her cattle farm.

02:29:58.089 --> 02:29:58.723
And she is definitely
no longer recognizable

02:29:59.724 --> 02:30:00.358
to anyone who might know her.

02:30:02.928 --> 02:30:03.695
Fair enough. All righty.

02:30:04.529 --> 02:30:04.796
Laslo,

02:30:05.997 --> 02:30:06.198
get in here.

02:30:08.099 --> 02:30:09.434
"Of course, of course."

02:30:12.871 --> 02:30:13.305
You see Laslo... step in.

02:30:14.406 --> 02:30:15.273
He's a young man.

02:30:19.144 --> 02:30:19.811
His forearms
are missing flesh and skin.

02:30:20.712 --> 02:30:21.746
It's just bone that you can see.

02:30:25.450 --> 02:30:26.351
It's surrounded
by this purple glow around it.

02:30:28.453 --> 02:30:29.454
Same thing
with his left calf as well.

02:30:31.990 --> 02:30:32.290
He has two scythes.

02:30:33.625 --> 02:30:34.926
They look like...

02:30:36.862 --> 02:30:37.496
barber blades, shaving blades.

02:30:40.298 --> 02:30:41.333
That's how they're shaped,
almost L shaped.

02:30:44.135 --> 02:30:44.970
He's very wide-eyed,
but at the same time

02:30:47.672 --> 02:30:48.473
you would notice that
his body language

02:30:50.642 --> 02:30:50.742
and his eyes
kind of change sometimes

02:30:51.209 --> 02:30:51.843
and he starts hunching

02:30:53.245 --> 02:30:54.813
and smirking.

02:30:56.248 --> 02:30:56.748
And then back
to wide-eyed again.

02:30:58.450 --> 02:30:59.251
"Oh yes, right away."

02:31:00.018 --> 02:31:00.252
Alright.

02:31:02.687 --> 02:31:03.588
As you tumble down the stairway

02:31:03.855 --> 02:31:04.689
to follow
the Demon Hunter companion.

02:31:05.957 --> 02:31:06.258
Mordred, if you don't mind.

02:31:10.996 --> 02:31:12.430
"Shining in the darkness
is Mordred, The Gaunt."

02:31:15.166 --> 02:31:15.433
"Not a hair on my head."

02:31:17.269 --> 02:31:17.702
"Bald and pale

02:31:19.337 --> 02:31:19.738
and dark of eye."

02:31:20.372 --> 02:31:21.006
"Sallow-cheeked,

02:31:24.009 --> 02:31:24.543
in golden armor of latticework

02:31:26.811 --> 02:31:27.479
shining with my Zakara."

02:31:30.181 --> 02:31:31.449
"A word I looked up on Wikipedia
earlier today."

02:31:32.717 --> 02:31:33.151
"I carry a...

02:31:37.255 --> 02:31:39.024
a Morningstar
and a tall, slender shield."

02:31:43.461 --> 02:31:44.396
"And I look with a lean
and hungry gaze,

02:31:46.364 --> 02:31:47.332
wanting to eliminate
corruption."

02:31:48.300 --> 02:31:48.900
"Stay close."

02:31:54.272 --> 02:31:55.006
As Mordred steps into
the central landing chamber,

02:31:55.740 --> 02:31:57.208
if you wouldn't mind.

02:31:58.009 --> 02:31:58.643
Well,

02:32:00.979 --> 02:32:01.580
before you even see Remuil,

02:32:04.783 --> 02:32:05.083
you hear the swarm of insects
that follows her.

02:32:06.151 --> 02:32:06.351
A buzzing

02:32:09.321 --> 02:32:10.055
that enters the room
before she does.

02:32:11.489 --> 02:32:11.890
She steps in,

02:32:13.191 --> 02:32:14.593
hair over one eye,

02:32:15.160 --> 02:32:17.495
a bit of a mess.

02:32:19.698 --> 02:32:20.198
Green and black armor.

02:32:21.499 --> 02:32:21.700
It's more like

02:32:25.670 --> 02:32:26.304
vines and reptile skin.

02:32:28.473 --> 02:32:28.673
Two snakes

02:32:30.108 --> 02:32:30.709
encircle her arms.

02:32:32.410 --> 02:32:32.777
They look around.

02:32:35.180 --> 02:32:36.081
Her fingernails very long.

02:32:37.983 --> 02:32:41.419
She seems happy to be here.

02:32:42.487 --> 02:32:43.154
And following in,

02:32:44.255 --> 02:32:44.456
the final member of this troupe.

02:32:48.193 --> 02:32:48.960
At first, Indra walks in
and she fixes her hair

02:32:51.329 --> 02:32:51.730
as it's been messy
on the ride in.

02:32:53.999 --> 02:32:54.933
She immediately picks up
the gold off the floor

02:32:56.668 --> 02:32:57.335
and scoffs at everyone
who didn't realize

02:32:57.902 --> 02:32:58.937
there was treasure lying there.

02:33:04.342 --> 02:33:04.709
You see these beautiful raven
feathers encircling her neck,

02:33:04.776 --> 02:33:05.910
like a collar.

02:33:09.280 --> 02:33:10.115
Very beautiful cleavage
on display

02:33:14.352 --> 02:33:15.553
in a tiny,
raven-feathered bra top.

02:33:17.889 --> 02:33:20.091
I also saw on Wikipedia that
this is the Wizard couture.

02:33:24.629 --> 02:33:25.263
Just one blue swathe of fabric
going across,

02:33:26.665 --> 02:33:27.365
making this very skimpy dress.

02:33:29.668 --> 02:33:30.568
Interestingly, her right arm

02:33:31.269 --> 02:33:31.903
is completely burnt
up to her forearm

02:33:34.739 --> 02:33:35.640
and she has gold fingernails.

02:33:37.509 --> 02:33:38.610
Probably smelted
from all of her loot.

02:33:41.079 --> 02:33:41.513
She has a large staff
that swirls with dark magic

02:33:42.013 --> 02:33:43.982
at the end of it.

02:33:44.849 --> 02:33:45.016
She says nothing,

02:33:47.252 --> 02:33:47.585
but she pockets the gold
into her cleavage.

02:33:47.652 --> 02:33:48.053
You got it.

02:33:52.323 --> 02:33:53.391
As you all finally descend
the last bit of stairs,

02:33:57.362 --> 02:33:57.562
you finally land in the crypt
entryway chambers.

02:33:59.831 --> 02:34:00.765
You can see immediately
in the torchlight

02:34:01.866 --> 02:34:02.133
that you carry
into this lightless space,

02:34:04.569 --> 02:34:04.836
glistening sparkles.

02:34:07.105 --> 02:34:07.572
And other smattering
of scattered gold coins,

02:34:08.440 --> 02:34:09.641
maybe a dozen or so,

02:34:13.044 --> 02:34:13.545
that spill out in the middle
of the old, dusty stonework

02:34:13.845 --> 02:34:14.279
that greets you here.

02:34:21.186 --> 02:34:22.020
Smell of decay and old, musty,
stale air catches your nose.

02:34:23.855 --> 02:34:24.522
You can see
alcove displays nearby

02:34:24.989 --> 02:34:25.457
in the sides of the stone walls

02:34:27.025 --> 02:34:27.559
and the low ceiling.

02:34:30.562 --> 02:34:31.463
Angelic statues
sit within these little alcoves,

02:34:32.297 --> 02:34:32.797
though in various states
of disrepair.

02:34:34.432 --> 02:34:35.533
While numerous puddles of wax

02:34:38.236 --> 02:34:39.070
form at the corners
of various elements of decor,

02:34:39.971 --> 02:34:40.805
where candles
once lit these chambers

02:34:41.973 --> 02:34:43.274
before they burnt
down to nothing.

02:34:45.944 --> 02:34:46.978
A faint growl
echoes in the shadow,

02:34:47.746 --> 02:34:49.748
beyond your sight.

02:34:51.750 --> 02:34:52.117
As you all continue on a bit,

02:34:53.251 --> 02:34:54.219
keeping your eyes peeled,

02:34:56.888 --> 02:34:57.322
the pathway
splits into three directions,

02:34:58.089 --> 02:34:58.423
a T-intersection.

02:35:00.325 --> 02:35:05.196
So (indistinct) in this crypt.

02:35:07.699 --> 02:35:08.266
Any indication
of which direction

02:35:08.466 --> 02:35:09.000
the growl is coming from?

02:35:09.667 --> 02:35:09.868
Make a perception check.

02:35:12.837 --> 02:35:13.538
Are there any clay pots around?

02:35:15.273 --> 02:35:19.210
Make a perception check.

02:35:20.545 --> 02:35:21.379
Seventeen.

02:35:21.746 --> 02:35:23.448
Seventeen.

02:35:24.549 --> 02:35:25.016
Very good, actually.

02:35:26.751 --> 02:35:27.585
The growl,
while the echo seems to be

02:35:28.787 --> 02:35:29.854
somewhat
amorphous in the distance,

02:35:31.923 --> 02:35:32.457
you listen closely
and can hear a faint bit of...

02:35:35.727 --> 02:35:36.995
grinding and another low,
guttural rumble,

02:35:39.030 --> 02:35:40.532
similar to that initial growl,
from the path directly ahead.

02:35:41.399 --> 02:35:41.666
You rolled a...

02:35:42.267 --> 02:35:42.400
Thirteen.

02:35:43.468 --> 02:35:44.002
Thirteen.

02:35:44.636 --> 02:35:47.672
Yeah, there's a pot
right to the left of you.

02:35:49.040 --> 02:35:49.774
It smashes
and breaks to the ground,

02:35:51.176 --> 02:35:52.377
-leaving 4 gold pieces.
-Yes

02:35:54.445 --> 02:35:55.446
Because why wouldn't there be
gold in a pot in a crypt.

02:35:56.781 --> 02:35:59.884
Diablo.

02:36:00.351 --> 02:36:01.486
Alright

02:36:03.755 --> 02:36:04.489
"It seems as if trouble
might be awaiting us ahead."

02:36:05.690 --> 02:36:05.890
"Do we wanna start there or...

02:36:07.692 --> 02:36:08.059
pick one of the sides?"

02:36:09.627 --> 02:36:10.562
"Straight ahead, I say."

02:36:12.463 --> 02:36:13.264
"We're here
to eradicate the darkness."

02:36:15.166 --> 02:36:15.667
"No point in wasting time,
let's go."

02:36:20.538 --> 02:36:21.172
"Bag of bones
so scared on the inside."

02:36:25.210 --> 02:36:27.111
"Bag of bones
does not want to go."

02:36:28.613 --> 02:36:32.116
"Onyx does."

02:36:33.551 --> 02:36:33.751
And he scurries off.

02:36:35.753 --> 02:36:36.354
-"He creeps me out every time."
-"Every time."

02:36:38.356 --> 02:36:39.123
"Laslo is in a mood today."

02:36:41.092 --> 02:36:43.161
-"Alright."
-"Follow him."

02:36:43.828 --> 02:36:44.762
Moving forward.

02:36:46.130 --> 02:36:48.066
Laslo, you are taking point
on this one.

02:36:49.200 --> 02:36:50.101
Creeping forward,

02:36:50.301 --> 02:36:51.569
you initially step through
the stone arches

02:36:53.171 --> 02:36:53.371
and you can see they're deep-set
with cracks all around you.

02:36:57.542 --> 02:36:58.710
The crunch of shale and bones
breaks beneath you as you step,

02:37:00.879 --> 02:37:01.379
loud in your ears amongst
the silence that surrounds you.

02:37:03.348 --> 02:37:04.415
The hall carries on
for quite a bit forward

02:37:06.050 --> 02:37:07.285
but the walls begin to narrow,
ever so slightly,

02:37:09.587 --> 02:37:10.655
before finally coming to an end
where you can subtly see,

02:37:12.657 --> 02:37:13.558
with the torchlight
as it approaches behind you,

02:37:15.593 --> 02:37:16.661
a pile of corpses
lying on the ground.

02:37:17.295 --> 02:37:18.329
Human at one point,
but even just at a quick glance,

02:37:20.164 --> 02:37:23.701
you can see that
they're bloody and torn apart.

02:37:27.972 --> 02:37:28.573
You guys wouldn't notice that
the back of Laslo has changed

02:37:30.909 --> 02:37:31.709
from hunching to up straight

02:37:34.012 --> 02:37:35.146
and darting his head
left and right.

02:37:36.180 --> 02:37:38.416
"There are...

02:37:39.784 --> 02:37:39.851
There are corpses."

02:37:41.653 --> 02:37:42.186
-"Yeah."
-"Everywhere."

02:37:43.121 --> 02:37:43.254
"We're in a cathedral."

02:37:44.222 --> 02:37:45.323
"There's a tomb down here."

02:37:47.525 --> 02:37:48.426
"Are you surprised by the fact
that people are..?"

02:37:48.993 --> 02:37:49.494
"We knew people
were dead down here."

02:37:51.629 --> 02:37:51.896
"I know. I just meant,

02:37:54.699 --> 02:37:55.166
yay for us,
we picked the right way."

02:37:56.367 --> 02:37:56.634
-"Okay?"
-"Yeah."

02:37:57.869 --> 02:37:58.202
"You're not wrong."

02:37:59.337 --> 02:38:00.071
How fresh do the bodies look?

02:38:01.940 --> 02:38:03.508
You'll have to make a medicine
check to go and inspect.

02:38:04.042 --> 02:38:05.677
Do I have medicine?

02:38:06.577 --> 02:38:07.412
There should be a skill there.

02:38:08.346 --> 02:38:08.479
Doesn't mean
you're any good at it.

02:38:11.382 --> 02:38:11.616
There's no medicine.
There's survival.

02:38:12.784 --> 02:38:13.084
Sorry.

02:38:13.518 --> 02:38:14.018
Medicine.

02:38:14.285 --> 02:38:14.652
I did remove that one.

02:38:15.320 --> 02:38:15.920
Nature, then.

02:38:16.154 --> 02:38:16.554
-Nature.
-Sorry, my bad.

02:38:19.057 --> 02:38:19.457
That's not good.

02:38:20.558 --> 02:38:20.692
Which is weird,

02:38:23.361 --> 02:38:23.661
but seeing how I grew up
in a swamp and all.

02:38:24.729 --> 02:38:25.330
Seventeen.

02:38:26.331 --> 02:38:26.664
Seventeen?

02:38:27.332 --> 02:38:27.598
Not too bad.

02:38:30.501 --> 02:38:31.102
Inspecting the bodies,
as you lean down

02:38:32.270 --> 02:38:32.403
and look across the corpses.

02:38:34.572 --> 02:38:35.573
They... the blood is congealed.

02:38:37.041 --> 02:38:37.475
They've been dead
for a little bit of time.

02:38:39.277 --> 02:38:40.511
Some of them look fresh,
some of them look old,

02:38:43.081 --> 02:38:44.282
almost like something keeps
coming back to feed at times.

02:38:45.350 --> 02:38:46.617
But some of them are very fresh

02:38:47.952 --> 02:38:48.820
and you can see where then bone
has been splintered and broken.

02:38:50.121 --> 02:38:51.022
There are gouges
in the exposed elements

02:38:54.559 --> 02:38:55.093
of the heavier white bone
that peaks out.

02:38:56.194 --> 02:38:58.429
Teeth marks, claw marks.

02:39:00.398 --> 02:39:01.232
"An animal did this."

02:39:02.066 --> 02:39:06.704
"I would know."

02:39:08.539 --> 02:39:09.207
That growl creeps back in

02:39:11.209 --> 02:39:12.310
and you hear it and glance up

02:39:13.611 --> 02:39:14.645
and just as you catch
the edge of the torchlight,

02:39:15.546 --> 02:39:16.647
the height of the building,
your eyes now see,

02:39:20.818 --> 02:39:21.285
lining the upper roof
and ceiling of this chamber

02:39:24.288 --> 02:39:25.390
a dozen or so of these
grey-skinned humanoid beings

02:39:28.226 --> 02:39:29.227
with elongated limbs,
all hanging, quietly waiting

02:39:30.795 --> 02:39:31.195
as the torchlight
glistens past their eyes,

02:39:32.096 --> 02:39:33.297
reflecting once.

02:39:35.366 --> 02:39:36.267
And in that brief moment of
tension as you hear that growl,

02:39:37.468 --> 02:39:37.935
they all begin to leap down
towards you.

02:39:38.269 --> 02:39:38.569
Everybody roll an 8.

02:39:39.570 --> 02:39:40.004
Oh my god!

02:39:44.709 --> 02:39:45.143
As it begins, you see swarming
down 10 of these creatures

02:39:48.246 --> 02:39:48.746
begin to surround,
and tear and gnash.

02:39:50.815 --> 02:39:51.082
Three of them
are going after you.

02:39:53.017 --> 02:39:53.584
Three of them
are gonna be swarming you.

02:39:55.286 --> 02:39:55.420
And then it's gonna be...

02:39:57.588 --> 02:39:59.857
We'll do yours first.
So, 3 against you.

02:40:00.758 --> 02:40:01.559
It's a miss.

02:40:02.026 --> 02:40:02.293
It's a 12 hit.

02:40:02.927 --> 02:40:03.361
A miss.

02:40:04.829 --> 02:40:05.797
And that does hit.

02:40:06.864 --> 02:40:07.298
So, 2 of them
go streaking up towards you,

02:40:07.565 --> 02:40:08.666
claws towards you.

02:40:10.735 --> 02:40:11.536
One of them holding a giant,
hooked, rusted blade,

02:40:12.036 --> 02:40:12.837
swings it wide
and cuts into you

02:40:13.704 --> 02:40:14.272
for 3 points
of physical damage.

02:40:15.473 --> 02:40:16.340
So, the 3 on you,
not much of an effect.

02:40:17.075 --> 02:40:18.076
The 3 that are
storming you, Laslo...

02:40:21.145 --> 02:40:21.546
That's gonna be a 10,
which I believe misses.

02:40:23.514 --> 02:40:23.781
Eighteen, which does hit.

02:40:24.048 --> 02:40:24.315
Better.

02:40:25.850 --> 02:40:26.717
Twenty-one.

02:40:29.720 --> 02:40:30.721
So, as you're backing away
you have

02:40:30.922 --> 02:40:31.923
a swarm of these creatures
rush towards you.

02:40:34.025 --> 02:40:34.325
Their jaws open
with horrible, spiked teeth

02:40:36.961 --> 02:40:38.062
almost like thick, greenish,
phlegm-like liquid

02:40:39.464 --> 02:40:39.797
pouring out of the inside
as they run towards you,

02:40:39.964 --> 02:40:41.265
claws out...

02:40:43.067 --> 02:40:44.135
as they slash, you take
6 points of physical damage

02:40:45.536 --> 02:40:46.304
from 2 who managed
to break through your defense.

02:40:48.840 --> 02:40:49.240
These points are not very high.

02:40:51.109 --> 02:40:52.477
Two end up swarming
towards you, Tauro.

02:40:53.177 --> 02:40:53.578
Twenty-one.

02:40:53.878 --> 02:40:54.412
Hits.

02:40:56.280 --> 02:40:56.514
And an 11.

02:40:56.714 --> 02:40:56.981
Miss.

02:40:57.248 --> 02:40:57.882
Alright.

02:40:58.683 --> 02:40:59.951
As they both come
swarming towards you,

02:41:01.486 --> 02:41:02.320
one jumps up and you catch it
with the side of your forearms

02:41:03.621 --> 02:41:04.155
and shove it off
but at that point

02:41:04.355 --> 02:41:05.623
the other one crawls up

02:41:06.224 --> 02:41:07.125
and starts biting at the side of
your shoulder and clavicle area.

02:41:07.825 --> 02:41:08.693
You take 3 points
of physical damage.

02:41:13.397 --> 02:41:13.998
And the last 2 would be
1 against each of you.

02:41:17.435 --> 02:41:17.768
That is a 24 versus Mordred.

02:41:19.704 --> 02:41:19.904
-Hits.
-And a 9 versus Indra.

02:41:20.171 --> 02:41:21.272
Hit.

02:41:21.539 --> 02:41:22.340
Soo you take 3 points
of physical damage, Mordred,

02:41:23.474 --> 02:41:23.908
as 1 of them jumps up
on your shield

02:41:24.775 --> 02:41:25.042
and claws over it.

02:41:26.277 --> 02:41:27.478
Catches the side
of your forehead,

02:41:28.846 --> 02:41:29.914
you can feel the blood begin to
roll down into your eye.

02:41:32.617 --> 02:41:33.651
Top of the round now,
Indra, you're up first.

02:41:35.253 --> 02:41:36.154
