onto 1 of these creatures.

02:49:40.004 --> 02:49:40.871
Screams from the inside,

02:49:41.071 --> 02:49:41.972
muffled once enclosed
in the mouth,

02:49:43.741 --> 02:49:45.075
and as the jaw tightens
it goes limp.

02:49:45.809 --> 02:49:46.110
Spitting it on to the ground.

02:49:47.511 --> 02:49:48.012
Nice.

02:49:49.113 --> 02:49:50.280
So, you are currently
transformed

02:49:52.783 --> 02:49:53.417
which means you get your AC
while you're shapeshifted.

02:49:54.385 --> 02:49:55.319
-Oh, sweet.
-Alright.

02:49:56.787 --> 02:49:57.921
That did generate spirit

02:49:59.690 --> 02:50:00.057
so you could also swam
now that you have that to use.

02:50:03.427 --> 02:50:03.627
Well, I'll do that too.

02:50:05.129 --> 02:50:05.462
So, I'll roll for attack
on that 1.

02:50:05.996 --> 02:50:06.897
You got it.

02:50:09.199 --> 02:50:10.134
That definitely hit,
that's a 21.

02:50:12.069 --> 02:50:16.440
Alright, roll damage
for the swarm, now.

02:50:17.074 --> 02:50:17.441
Ten.

02:50:18.709 --> 02:50:19.610
Ten, that'll do it.

02:50:21.512 --> 02:50:21.779
So, after that 1 falls,
you pull back

02:50:23.247 --> 02:50:24.481
angry in your gator form.

02:50:25.249 --> 02:50:26.150
You watch as the insects swarm
around 1 of the second ones

02:50:27.685 --> 02:50:28.285
that was still recoiling
from the shock

02:50:28.552 --> 02:50:29.453
that was delivered by Indra,

02:50:29.653 --> 02:50:30.888
at the beginning
of this combat round.

02:50:32.289 --> 02:50:33.524
As the insects swarm around it,
it begins to screech loudly...

02:50:35.559 --> 02:50:36.393
before the silence hit
and the insects pull away.

02:50:38.195 --> 02:50:38.862
You see mostly
skeletal upper torso

02:50:39.463 --> 02:50:40.397
as it falls to its knees and...

02:50:42.332 --> 02:50:42.599
splats to the ground dead.

02:50:43.701 --> 02:50:44.101
-Alright.
-Nice.

02:50:45.969 --> 02:50:46.236
Are you finishing your round?

02:50:47.237 --> 02:50:48.172
Yeah.

02:50:49.740 --> 02:50:49.973
Laslo, you're up.
Tauro, you're on deck

02:50:51.008 --> 02:50:51.675
Okay.

02:50:54.278 --> 02:50:54.545
Actually, sorry,
the creatures have to go first.

02:50:57.414 --> 02:50:57.781
So of the swarm that's there,
2 of them have fallen.

02:50:58.749 --> 02:50:59.383
There's still 1 against you.

02:51:02.453 --> 02:51:02.820
That's gonna be an 11 to hit

02:51:03.654 --> 02:51:04.088
which misses.

02:51:04.354 --> 02:51:04.455
Goes against you.

02:51:08.692 --> 02:51:09.193
Three still up against you,
but actually now

02:51:10.194 --> 02:51:10.728
the 3 against you
are going after you.

02:51:12.096 --> 02:51:12.362
They begin to rush away

02:51:13.831 --> 02:51:17.968
in your direction.

02:51:22.039 --> 02:51:23.640
That's a 24 roll (indistinct).

02:51:25.809 --> 02:51:26.610
Do you get
an attack of opportunity

02:51:27.211 --> 02:51:29.046
against the
ones that ran away?

02:51:29.980 --> 02:51:30.614
Yeah.

02:51:32.049 --> 02:51:32.983
You can take a singular strike

02:51:34.651 --> 02:51:34.785
against one of them
with your Siphon Blood.

02:51:36.120 --> 02:51:38.388
Let's do that.

02:51:40.190 --> 02:51:40.657
-Fourteen.
-Fourteen does hit.

02:51:41.725 --> 02:51:44.928
Roll damage on that.

02:51:47.731 --> 02:51:48.699
-Thirteen.
-Thirteen, all right.

02:51:48.966 --> 02:51:49.833
The one that's
rushing away from you,

02:51:50.367 --> 02:51:50.968
which would have
first attacked him,

02:51:52.236 --> 02:51:52.336
so that one's nullified

02:51:53.504 --> 02:51:54.638
tries to scoot away.

02:51:56.273 --> 02:51:57.207
As it does, you manage
to slam it your Siphon Blood.

02:51:58.909 --> 02:51:59.943
As you do, you pull the last bit
of its undead life force out.

02:52:00.978 --> 02:52:01.812
It crumples to the ground
and withers on the spot

02:52:02.613 --> 02:52:02.913
like a spider
curling its legs in.

02:52:04.081 --> 02:52:04.348
(SHUDDERS)

02:52:07.017 --> 02:52:08.185
So that first attack
does not actually come at you.

02:52:10.420 --> 02:52:11.955
That's my Necromancer!

02:52:13.690 --> 02:52:14.158
So, one miss.

02:52:16.693 --> 02:52:19.029
And a second miss. They both
come at you, rolling terribly.

02:52:21.732 --> 02:52:22.166
The other two
that are coming at you,

02:52:22.432 --> 02:52:23.300
one of them stays.

02:52:24.501 --> 02:52:25.803
-Okay.
-The other one that succeeded.

02:52:27.838 --> 02:52:28.272
That one's gonna be against you.
That is gonna be an 11 to hit.

02:52:28.472 --> 02:52:29.006
-Miss.
-Misses.

02:52:30.440 --> 02:52:31.375
The other one runs towards you.
You do get an attack.

02:52:33.510 --> 02:52:34.478
Although,
you are ranged at this point.

02:52:36.180 --> 02:52:38.115
So, I will say
you don't necessarily have that.

02:52:40.184 --> 02:52:40.384
That is a 12 against you.

02:52:42.986 --> 02:52:44.588
All right. Then there's
the 2 that were already on you.

02:52:47.457 --> 02:52:47.724
Twelve and 14.

02:52:48.225 --> 02:52:48.559
-No.
-Does not hit.

02:52:50.294 --> 02:52:51.261
The last one that's against you

02:52:52.162 --> 02:52:52.663
rushes past
and heads towards you as well

02:52:52.963 --> 02:52:54.031
That's gonna be a 12.

02:52:55.666 --> 02:52:57.334
-They're rolling real bad.
-Back to the darkness.

02:53:00.437 --> 02:53:01.305
Now there is a mighty swarm
of these surviving ghouls

02:53:03.540 --> 02:53:03.807
that are all scrambling
over and around

02:53:05.509 --> 02:53:06.276
the proximity of Mordred,

02:53:06.643 --> 02:53:07.477
who's pushing back
with the shield,

02:53:08.946 --> 02:53:09.379
flail spinning
in the air angrily,

02:53:10.414 --> 02:53:10.614
getting amped up.

02:53:12.716 --> 02:53:13.183
That finishes their go,
now we're back to Indra

02:53:14.318 --> 02:53:14.852
and then it's Laslo.

02:53:17.020 --> 02:53:17.788
I'm gonna electrocute
in the middle,

02:53:19.690 --> 02:53:20.023
if they're all piling round him,
just to hit 3 again.

02:53:21.358 --> 02:53:22.059
Sure, you can do that.

02:53:23.961 --> 02:53:25.028
-Go ahead and roll for attack.
-All right.

02:53:26.897 --> 02:53:27.030
Wait, no, it's a DC16.

02:53:28.398 --> 02:53:30.234
That's right. (indistinct)

02:53:32.236 --> 02:53:33.437
That's a success.

02:53:35.105 --> 02:53:36.039
Success.
Wow, they're rolling high.

02:53:37.608 --> 02:53:38.342
-And a fail.
-All right.

02:53:39.176 --> 02:53:39.376
-Roll damage on that.
-Ten.

02:53:40.878 --> 02:53:41.345
Ten damage, so that's 5.

02:53:43.247 --> 02:53:43.814
Still takes out one
who was damaged

02:53:44.448 --> 02:53:44.915
by the Electrocute before.

02:53:45.916 --> 02:53:48.051
Then the other two...

02:53:48.852 --> 02:53:49.353
take half damage.

02:53:50.988 --> 02:53:52.122
The energy sparks off.

02:53:55.659 --> 02:53:55.926
The first one pops from
the pulse of electrical energy.

02:53:56.860 --> 02:53:57.928
The other 2 get shaken by it,

02:53:59.263 --> 02:53:59.596
but still continue to focus
their attention angrily

02:54:00.163 --> 02:54:01.298
on Mordred.

02:54:02.699 --> 02:54:03.700
Though some of them are starting
to lose their luster

02:54:05.269 --> 02:54:06.770
fighting against
this iron wall of a person.

02:54:09.573 --> 02:54:10.507
-Anything else you want to do?
-Yes.

02:54:12.209 --> 02:54:13.010
Since Mordred
brought all of them to me,

02:54:15.946 --> 02:54:16.713
I'm going to teleport again
on the other side.

02:54:17.915 --> 02:54:18.248
Okay, go for it.

02:54:18.949 --> 02:54:19.449
(indistinct)

02:54:20.484 --> 02:54:21.919
Thanks a lot, Mordred

02:54:24.888 --> 02:54:25.088
Indra's playing a teleporting...

02:54:28.191 --> 02:54:29.126
chess piece over there,
finishing your turn.

02:54:30.861 --> 02:54:31.228
Laslo, you're up,
Tauro, you're on deck.

02:54:35.399 --> 02:54:35.832
As soon as
the other guy hits the floor,

02:54:37.167 --> 02:54:37.734
Laslo's demeanor changes again.

02:54:40.904 --> 02:54:41.905
Now he's kind of
near the ground,

02:54:43.740 --> 02:54:44.441
pushing corpses aside

02:54:47.144 --> 02:54:47.577
to look for one
that looks just about right.

02:54:49.246 --> 02:54:49.579
And Onyx is like,

02:54:51.315 --> 02:54:51.715
"Second chance, friend, yes."

02:54:52.883 --> 02:54:53.383
"Second chance."

02:54:54.885 --> 02:54:55.485
And I'm gonna cast
Command Skeletons

02:54:57.487 --> 02:54:58.088
and bring one of them back.

02:55:01.325 --> 02:55:02.426
So, you're currently in the
process of this harried combat.

02:55:04.261 --> 02:55:04.594
You reach over to find
one of the corpses mostly eaten

02:55:08.632 --> 02:55:08.799
and as you draw forth
the undeath from within,

02:55:10.834 --> 02:55:11.668
you watch this body.

02:55:14.404 --> 02:55:14.738
Suddenly, a skeletal hand
pushes through its own flesh.

02:55:16.740 --> 02:55:17.607
It's like watching
a skeleton claw its way

02:55:19.109 --> 02:55:19.409
out of the body
that once contained it.

02:55:21.545 --> 02:55:22.212
Bones that were broken
and pulled apart...

02:55:22.913 --> 02:55:23.814
...snap together.

02:55:25.749 --> 02:55:26.917
Until eventually,
you watch this skeleton,

02:55:29.586 --> 02:55:30.487
in all of it's still gashed
and clawed glory, stand...

02:55:32.022 --> 02:55:32.322
right next to you.

02:55:35.092 --> 02:55:36.126
Gruesome. I also love
how you have a spot.

02:55:37.694 --> 02:55:38.261
-I can name this skeleton.
-You can if you want to.

02:55:40.097 --> 02:55:40.664
It's a pet of some sorts.

02:55:44.234 --> 02:55:44.668
-That would be great.
-What's his name?

02:55:46.703 --> 02:55:47.337
God. What do you think
would be good?

02:55:48.572 --> 02:55:48.972
Spell Slots, that's his name.

02:55:51.241 --> 02:55:52.075
-Spell Slots?
-Yeah, Spell Slots.

02:55:53.710 --> 02:55:55.078
Because I will be
out of him soon.

02:55:57.781 --> 02:55:58.648
You trying to find the right one
gave me a vision

02:55:58.915 --> 02:55:59.549
of being
at the grocery store going,

02:56:00.384 --> 02:56:01.218
"Which is the right avocado?"

02:56:03.320 --> 02:56:03.887
No. No.
Squeeze, squeeze, squeeze.

02:56:04.988 --> 02:56:05.789
That skeleton right there.

02:56:07.257 --> 02:56:07.958
This has got some good bones.

02:56:10.160 --> 02:56:10.427
Skeleton can take a turn
if he wants.

02:56:11.895 --> 02:56:12.262
-Really? On this turn?
-Yeah.

02:56:14.931 --> 02:56:15.966
I'll send him out to go

02:56:17.334 --> 02:56:18.201
hit one of those bad guys
that's running after...

02:56:20.937 --> 02:56:22.339
So the skeleton,
immediately after forming up...

02:56:25.742 --> 02:56:25.809
lunges forward and takes
a swing at one of the ghouls.

02:56:29.279 --> 02:56:30.881
-Fourteen.
-Fourteen does hit. Roll damage.

02:56:33.750 --> 02:56:34.384
-Three.
-Three damage.

02:56:36.353 --> 02:56:36.853
Not a whole lot,
but doesn't hurt either.

02:56:38.688 --> 02:56:39.056
Spell Slots, come on.

02:56:39.122 --> 02:56:40.657
He's so cute.

02:56:43.427 --> 02:56:43.627
-You can't blame him.
-Spell Slots.

02:56:46.096 --> 02:56:46.163
Spell Slots is smaller
than the other skeletons.

02:56:49.299 --> 02:56:51.001
-But he's trying his best.
-He's just really tiny.

02:56:52.769 --> 02:56:53.970
Perfect.
That finishes your turn?

02:56:55.038 --> 02:56:56.573
As a bonus action,

02:56:57.641 --> 02:56:58.675
I want to,

02:57:00.911 --> 02:57:01.244
while I'm still down there
looking for corpses,

02:57:03.013 --> 02:57:03.413
I want to cast Bone Armor.

02:57:04.981 --> 02:57:06.450
Okay, go for it.

02:57:09.352 --> 02:57:09.953
From the other corpses
you did not choose from,

02:57:10.220 --> 02:57:11.321
2 of the other nearby ones,

02:57:13.723 --> 02:57:14.391
you watch as sections
of their bone begins to also...

02:57:15.592 --> 02:57:16.693
pull out of the flesh,

02:57:18.128 --> 02:57:19.229
the soft, easy to tear through
flesh and they begin...

02:57:22.399 --> 02:57:22.899
to assemble around you
like this suit of white, pale,

02:57:23.166 --> 02:57:23.467
somewhat bloody armor.

02:57:24.267 --> 02:57:25.969
I love it.

02:57:27.604 --> 02:57:27.871
Six.

02:57:29.973 --> 02:57:30.407
So you have 6 temporary hit
points from that.

02:57:31.108 --> 02:57:31.975
Awesome,
finishing Laslo's turn,

02:57:33.009 --> 02:57:33.343
Tauro you're up,
Mordred you're on deck.

02:57:36.513 --> 02:57:37.447
I'm gonna really piss off
at these ones here.

02:57:39.182 --> 02:57:40.183
I'm gonna push
the one that's one me off.

02:57:42.819 --> 02:57:44.054
I'm gonna spend 12 hatred
to do Rapid Fire.

02:57:45.422 --> 02:57:45.689
You got it.

02:57:48.625 --> 02:57:49.159
Just full on
every moving body I can see.

02:57:52.295 --> 02:57:52.496
So the one that's one me,
the first one...

02:57:53.830 --> 02:57:54.965
that was cocked.

02:57:57.100 --> 02:57:57.400
Okay, that is 13.

02:57:58.535 --> 02:57:59.236
Thirteen to hit?

02:58:00.637 --> 02:58:00.770
-Yeah, to hit.
-That hits.

02:58:03.140 --> 02:58:03.240
Let's see. These are D6 plus 2.

02:58:05.909 --> 02:58:06.443
-Three damage on that one.
-Three damage.

02:58:10.147 --> 02:58:10.680
He's still standing. This is
the same one you shot earlier.

02:58:12.149 --> 02:58:12.883
He's riddled with holes.

02:58:13.383 --> 02:58:14.117
-Fifteen to hit.
-That hits.

02:58:17.254 --> 02:58:17.687
Okay, that should do it.
Eight damage.

02:58:19.222 --> 02:58:19.923
Takes him out.
Falls to the ground.

02:58:21.591 --> 02:58:22.058
-That was 2 shots.
-Four more attacks.

02:58:23.226 --> 02:58:24.361
To the one that's...

02:58:26.263 --> 02:58:28.098
Actually, I'm gonna go
to the ones that are on Laslo.

02:58:29.366 --> 02:58:30.500
Okay.

02:58:32.636 --> 02:58:33.470
-Eighteen to hit.
-There's only one left on Laslo.

02:58:33.970 --> 02:58:34.271
The other one's
rushed towards...

02:58:35.505 --> 02:58:36.506
I think all of them
rushed towards Mordred.

02:58:37.207 --> 02:58:38.241
Their backs are
probably turned towards me.

02:58:40.043 --> 02:58:41.011
Okay, so the ones that are
rushing away from Laslo.

02:58:42.746 --> 02:58:43.713
-Eighteen to hit on that one.
-That hits.

02:58:45.048 --> 02:58:46.116
-Seven damage.
-All right. It's still standing.

02:58:48.185 --> 02:58:49.553
-But it's real rough.
-I'm gonna hit him again.

02:58:51.888 --> 02:58:52.522
-Yikes, 11.
-Eleven does not hit.

02:58:53.924 --> 02:58:54.891
I'm gonna shoot at him again.

02:58:57.027 --> 02:58:57.861
-That should do it, 18 to hit.
-That hits.

02:58:59.029 --> 02:59:00.197
-That's 8 damage.
-That one falls.

02:59:03.099 --> 02:59:03.233
And I've got one more shot,

02:59:04.668 --> 02:59:04.968
to the next one I can see.

02:59:06.870 --> 02:59:07.237
(MUMBLING)

02:59:08.772 --> 02:59:08.838
Twelve to hit.

02:59:10.974 --> 02:59:11.641
-Twelve just hits.
-Great.

02:59:13.977 --> 02:59:14.578
One? Three damage.

02:59:17.847 --> 02:59:19.216
You angrily turn around,
channeling your hatred...

02:59:22.852 --> 02:59:23.620
and unleash this barrage
of shots in their direction.

02:59:25.255 --> 02:59:25.522
You watch
as 3 of these creatures

02:59:26.957 --> 02:59:27.224
fall to the ground,
no longer moving.

02:59:28.491 --> 02:59:29.292
(PANTS)

02:59:29.793 --> 02:59:32.796
-You steady yourself.
-"Filth."

02:59:34.097 --> 02:59:35.065
-That finishes your turn?
-That finishes my turn.

02:59:36.600 --> 02:59:37.834
Mordred, you're up.
Remy, you're on deck.

02:59:41.705 --> 02:59:42.305
I heft my shield and it begins
to emit white, radiant fire

02:59:45.809 --> 02:59:46.943
and I will use Shield Bash.

02:59:48.545 --> 02:59:49.512
I will charge one of them,

02:59:51.348 --> 02:59:52.415
and any of the others
within 5 feet of it

02:59:55.051 --> 02:59:55.819
must all make a deck save
and take Holy Damage.

02:59:57.454 --> 02:59:57.754
-You've got it.
-"By the Light, be damned!"

03:00:01.625 --> 03:00:02.792
You watch as the shield begins
to fill with radiant energy

03:00:05.228 --> 03:00:05.729
and with a sudden impacting
blast, like iron on stone,

03:00:05.795 --> 03:00:06.029
this echoing explosion

03:00:09.332 --> 03:00:10.000
across the inside of this crypt
catches your ears

03:00:11.101 --> 03:00:11.668
as you see this flash of energy.

03:00:14.704 --> 03:00:15.005
-What's the damage?
-Twenty points if they fail.

03:00:16.039 --> 03:00:16.306
Good roll.

03:00:17.707 --> 03:00:19.542
That's a fail.

03:00:20.844 --> 03:00:24.114
Fail.

03:00:24.648 --> 03:00:26.116
Fail.

03:00:26.983 --> 03:00:27.484
And fail.

03:00:28.218 --> 03:00:28.985
With that final flash,

03:00:30.620 --> 03:00:31.454
you watch
as the bodies go flying

03:00:32.489 --> 03:00:32.689
and the few
still standing ghouls

03:00:35.191 --> 03:00:35.458
are scattered in pieces

03:00:37.527 --> 03:00:37.927
across
the far end of this chamber

03:00:40.330 --> 03:00:40.530
as silence
once more takes the interior

03:00:41.665 --> 03:00:43.466
of this dungeon.

03:00:43.733 --> 03:00:44.434
I...

03:00:47.103 --> 03:00:50.340
and turn back
into my human form.

03:00:51.875 --> 03:00:54.577
"That was a nice warm-up."

03:00:56.880 --> 03:00:57.414
"I think it's agreed, next time
we walk into a hallway,

03:00:58.815 --> 03:00:59.215
we check the ceilings."

03:01:02.285 --> 03:01:02.719
-"That was unnecessary."
-"But it was fun!"

03:01:04.621 --> 03:01:04.888
"I know.
Feeling really good, actually."

03:01:07.924 --> 03:01:08.191
"You're not the one
covered in goblin parts."

03:01:10.427 --> 03:01:14.464
"No, I actually look
pretty damn good."

03:01:16.866 --> 03:01:17.167
"All right.
Shall we continue on?"

03:01:20.737 --> 03:01:21.404
This is the end of the hall.
It ends here, at the bodies.

03:01:22.439 --> 03:01:23.239
It narrowed and came to an end.

03:01:24.708 --> 03:01:26.409
"Well (BLEEP), we went
the wrong way. Turn around."

03:01:27.444 --> 03:01:28.144
Is there anything else?

03:01:29.679 --> 03:01:30.814
-Any clay pots?
-Any pots?

03:01:32.182 --> 03:01:33.149
There are 3 pots, no chests.

03:01:34.951 --> 03:01:35.418
There are the tattered corpses
and 3 pots.

03:01:36.686 --> 03:01:36.953
I wreck one of them.

03:01:40.156 --> 03:01:40.423
Is nobody else claim the other
pots? I'm going for it.

03:01:41.925 --> 03:01:42.592
LAUGHTER

03:01:45.495 --> 03:01:45.929
All right, you have to teleport.
I'm just saying.

03:01:46.196 --> 03:01:47.297
Because right now,

03:01:49.265 --> 03:01:49.933
there's a weregator
that is just wading into them.

03:01:52.802 --> 03:01:53.303
Can I use my maul action

03:01:53.570 --> 03:01:54.838
to maul the clay pot?

03:01:56.673 --> 03:01:57.841
I'll allow it. You don't need
spirit for that, but you can.

03:01:59.576 --> 03:02:00.443
I've got a sheath of unpuffed
bubble wrap before I go.

03:02:01.144 --> 03:02:02.245
-Okay, you do that.
-I want one pot.

03:02:03.980 --> 03:02:04.948
One pot bursts with arc energy
from your magic missile,

03:02:06.816 --> 03:02:07.684
causing it to scatter
across the chamber.

03:02:07.951 --> 03:02:09.018
-Four gold drops on that one.
-Yes!

03:02:12.989 --> 03:02:13.590
The two are the ones
that you tear into, Remi...

03:02:17.060 --> 03:02:17.594
One of them
contains 40 gold pieces.

03:02:18.628 --> 03:02:18.828
Oh, s***!

03:02:20.263 --> 03:02:20.897
And the other is empty.

03:02:21.531 --> 03:02:22.031
Okay, well, that was worth it.

03:02:22.932 --> 03:02:23.767
It is strange, though.

03:02:24.601 --> 03:02:25.335
Most things
you hit in this world

03:02:28.171 --> 03:02:28.438
do tend to erupt
into gold coins.

03:02:29.739 --> 03:02:30.840
-I agree.
-Strange? How's that strange?

03:02:33.076 --> 03:02:33.576
I try not to question it.
Where do they come from?

03:02:37.747 --> 03:02:38.681
I once hit a waffle and
it turned into three gold coins.

03:02:40.817 --> 03:02:42.619
We're one act away
from the Truman Show.

03:02:44.320 --> 03:02:46.289
Videogame.

03:02:48.658 --> 03:02:49.492
Maybe there's another realm,

03:02:52.695 --> 03:02:53.129
where there's
just piles of gold.

03:02:53.363 --> 03:02:54.197
Pocket dimension.

03:02:55.965 --> 03:02:57.200
A distant echo
of some distant screech

03:03:01.771 --> 03:03:02.071
suddenly cuts you off this deep,
metaphysical conversation.

03:03:03.873 --> 03:03:04.808
(indistinct)
LAUGHTER

03:03:05.241 --> 03:03:06.376
Did it come
from the left or the right?

03:03:09.446 --> 03:03:12.248
Did you hear that? The narrative
structure is calling us.

03:03:13.917 --> 03:03:14.951
I feel a deep calling.

03:03:16.252 --> 03:03:17.420
-Nice.
-(indistinct)

03:03:19.689 --> 03:03:20.190
It sounded pretty muffled,
but nothing beyond that, really.

03:03:20.723 --> 03:03:22.125
Did you hear the call?

03:03:24.093 --> 03:03:24.861
Something's around.

03:03:25.528 --> 03:03:26.496
Which direction?

03:03:28.064 --> 03:03:28.598
I don't know. I couldn't tell.
It was muffled.

03:03:29.399 --> 03:03:30.233
Did anyone else hear it?

03:03:30.967 --> 03:03:31.868
No, you were
having conversations.

03:03:33.903 --> 03:03:35.038
Oh. We were talking
about metaphysics.

03:03:37.507 --> 03:03:38.107
I'm going to go back to
where the three branches start.

03:03:38.641 --> 03:03:39.476
Back yourself out a little.

03:03:40.877 --> 03:03:41.411
You're back
at the T-intersection

03:03:42.212 --> 03:03:42.745
facing in the direction.

03:03:43.012 --> 03:03:43.913
You have right and left.

03:03:46.382 --> 03:03:47.584
I'm gonna hold my wrist up
and let my snake

03:03:49.018 --> 03:03:49.419
lick the air and see if it
points in a certain direction.

03:03:50.753 --> 03:03:50.987
Oh, that's cool.

03:03:51.287 --> 03:03:54.891
Okay.

03:03:55.959 --> 03:03:56.793
The snake

03:03:59.762 --> 03:04:00.864
is unfamiliar
with crypt environments

03:04:02.899 --> 03:04:03.900
and is uncertain how
to tell which direction to go.

03:04:05.468 --> 03:04:06.402
It's all right, baby.
You'll get it someday.

03:04:07.804 --> 03:04:08.304
It slithers sadly
back onto your wrist.

03:04:09.873 --> 03:04:10.740
Familiars can sometimes
be disappointing.

03:04:12.675 --> 03:04:13.843
I went to press
my ear to the ground

03:04:17.080 --> 03:04:17.814
to see if I can hear where
the calling is coming from.

03:04:19.382 --> 03:04:20.950
-Make a perception check.
-Okay.

03:04:24.521 --> 03:04:24.621
-Nineteen.
--Nineteen. Not bad.

03:04:26.556 --> 03:04:27.690
As you put your ear against
the stone of the ground,

03:04:32.362 --> 03:04:33.830
you hear faint scraping noises
from both directions.

03:04:36.299 --> 03:04:36.733
Which scraping sounds eviler?

03:04:38.768 --> 03:04:39.502
There's more of them
to the right.

03:04:44.440 --> 03:04:44.674
A more independent
and fainter one to the left.

03:04:44.874 --> 03:04:46.509
Okay/

03:04:47.744 --> 03:04:48.378
The right seems dangerous.

03:04:50.079 --> 03:04:50.847
The left also seems dangerous.

03:04:53.182 --> 03:04:53.883
-Take your pick.
-What are you feeling?

03:04:54.884 --> 03:04:55.985
I'm feeling...

03:04:57.053 --> 03:04:58.121
If we're looking for some fun,
we go to the right.

03:04:59.522 --> 03:05:00.356
If we're looking to stay safe,
we go to the left.

03:05:01.024 --> 03:05:01.824
-Right, it is.
-Let's go to the right.

03:05:02.992 --> 03:05:03.293
-You guys are psychopaths.
-Yeah.

03:05:03.760 --> 03:05:03.893
All right.

03:05:05.962 --> 03:05:07.196
You all travelled to the right,

03:05:09.499 --> 03:05:10.667
for about 15 feet, as you all
have your weapons at the ready.

03:05:13.503 --> 03:05:14.470
Eyes peeled, you come upon
a massive, solid, iron door.

03:05:15.605 --> 03:05:16.239
There are chains pulled
across the front of it

03:05:18.408 --> 03:05:18.675
and a heavy lock fixed to it.

03:05:21.244 --> 03:05:22.011
Hmm, I actually might
be able to handle this.

03:05:22.812 --> 03:05:23.947
-I'm gonna try and pick it.
-Okay.

03:05:26.282 --> 03:05:26.516
Go ahead and roll a D20.
Add your dexterity modifier.

03:05:27.784 --> 03:05:28.952
Okay.

03:05:30.053 --> 03:05:30.920
Ew. My dex... Just--

03:05:32.755 --> 03:05:33.056
-Just your dex.
-Straight dex. Okay.

03:05:36.426 --> 03:05:36.559
Oh, poop! That was almost great.

03:05:37.460 --> 03:05:38.361
Fifteen total.

03:05:38.828 --> 03:05:39.362
-Oh, sorry. Thirteen total.
-Thirteen.

03:05:40.430 --> 03:05:41.431
Okay, with the thirteen,

03:05:42.932 --> 03:05:43.766
you watch
as your awesome bad***,

03:05:44.734 --> 03:05:45.735
down in
her home turf Demon Hunter

03:05:47.503 --> 03:05:47.704
gets down and takes out
her thieves' tools.

03:05:48.137 --> 03:05:48.771
Yes.

03:05:50.773 --> 03:05:51.074
And with a whip of the wrist,

03:05:52.275 --> 03:05:53.009
you achieve nothing.

03:05:55.211 --> 03:05:56.179
It was not budging.

03:05:57.981 --> 03:05:58.514
Do we need to get a key?

03:05:59.716 --> 03:06:00.583
What about your horns?

03:06:03.119 --> 03:06:03.519
No. I just...
Just give me a moment.

03:06:03.987 --> 03:06:04.821
I just punch it.

03:06:06.022 --> 03:06:06.756
I just try and punch it
like The Fonz.

03:06:08.057 --> 03:06:08.424
Make a strength check.

03:06:09.759 --> 03:06:10.226
Tauro, Tauro.

03:06:14.464 --> 03:06:14.797
Why couldn't that
be my lockpicking check?

03:06:18.635 --> 03:06:19.102
What's my strength?
I have no... 18.

03:06:20.136 --> 03:06:21.738
Eighteen? Good roll.

03:06:23.439 --> 03:06:25.241
Your knuckles are bleeding.

03:06:26.342 --> 03:06:26.976
Blast!

03:06:28.211 --> 03:06:29.178
Yeah, we need to find a key.

03:06:30.813 --> 03:06:31.447
With a heavy impact
against an iron door,

03:06:31.814 --> 03:06:32.048
the echo on the other side...

03:06:33.583 --> 03:06:33.683
Boom!

03:06:35.718 --> 03:06:36.252
Definitely reverberates
through the nearby chambers.

03:06:36.519 --> 03:06:37.687
You get the sense that,

03:06:39.922 --> 03:06:40.657
with any sense of surprise
you may have had at this point,

03:06:42.759 --> 03:06:43.393
you've definitely made
your presence known

03:06:43.693 --> 03:06:44.861
in the proximity of this door.

03:06:46.562 --> 03:06:47.697
It was the door's fault.

03:06:50.066 --> 03:06:50.900
Well, the surprise is ruined.

03:06:52.168 --> 03:06:52.735
I'll just magic missile
the lock.

03:06:53.803 --> 03:06:54.437
Okay.

03:06:55.605 --> 03:06:56.773
Go ahead and roll some damage.

03:06:57.440 --> 03:06:58.207
All right. Just damage?
I don't need to roll the hit?

03:06:59.275 --> 03:06:59.809
-Roll the hit just in case.
-Okay.

03:07:01.277 --> 03:07:01.577
-I like ones.
-Okay.

03:07:02.178 --> 03:07:03.012
Seventeen.

03:07:04.480 --> 03:07:05.348
-Does that hit the door?
-It hits.

03:07:05.982 --> 03:07:07.684
-Go ahead and roll damage.
-I shall.

03:07:11.888 --> 03:07:12.321
-Four plus two. Six.
-Okay.

03:07:14.290 --> 03:07:15.258
You blast it once.

03:07:17.326 --> 03:07:17.860
Glancing at it,
this is a very heavy door.

03:07:18.561 --> 03:07:19.095
With the magic missile,

03:07:19.729 --> 03:07:20.930
the arcane blast from it

03:07:23.866 --> 03:07:24.500
is generally pretty powerful
against softer, fleshier things.

03:07:25.601 --> 03:07:26.469
It's not gaining any purchase

03:07:27.537 --> 03:07:28.137
against this door's lock,
unfortunately.

03:07:29.205 --> 03:07:29.739
Yes, it's the door's fault.

03:07:31.474 --> 03:07:31.607
Find another way around.

03:07:33.342 --> 03:07:33.676
Maybe there's a key
down the other hallway.

03:07:35.278 --> 03:07:35.912
To the left.

03:07:38.347 --> 03:07:38.581
Look for keys, all the while.

03:07:39.716 --> 03:07:40.650
Yeah.

03:07:42.018 --> 03:07:42.285
Place my hand on the door
before we go.

03:07:43.586 --> 03:07:45.822
We'll play later.

03:07:48.758 --> 03:07:51.527
-F*** doors.
-Spell Slots goes like...

03:07:53.563 --> 03:07:54.363
Spell Slot.

03:07:56.532 --> 03:07:56.733
Glad you're with us, buddy.

03:07:58.234 --> 03:07:59.235
Spell Slots is the best.

03:08:01.571 --> 03:08:02.138
He's my favorite character
in this adventure.

03:08:03.606 --> 03:08:04.407
Continuing onward
in the other path,

03:08:05.475 --> 03:08:06.075
there's a relatively
lengthy hallway

03:08:06.776 --> 03:08:07.844
that continues on for a bit.

03:08:10.379 --> 03:08:10.847
There are pots here,
but they're already broken.

03:08:12.715 --> 03:08:12.949
-Oh...
-What?

03:08:13.015 --> 03:08:13.950
What?

03:08:16.819 --> 03:08:17.420
You do eventually, quietly,

03:08:18.521 --> 03:08:19.622
come upon a left-hand turn,

03:08:21.457 --> 03:08:21.791
and in the next hall,
you can just faintly hear...

03:08:23.493 --> 03:08:23.826
movement,

03:08:24.093 --> 03:08:24.560
scrambling,

03:08:27.764 --> 03:08:27.897
footfalls and shifting scrapes
against the stone.

03:08:28.898 --> 03:08:29.632
Is there anything
on the ceiling?

03:08:30.299 --> 03:08:31.200
-Make a perception check.
-Okay.

03:08:33.469 --> 03:08:34.036
Someone knows the secrets
of the pots.

03:08:38.241 --> 03:08:39.075
-It's a very competent four.
-Gosh.

03:08:39.542 --> 03:08:40.376
Glancing up
at the ceiling above,

03:08:42.645 --> 03:08:43.279
which is only
about a 10-foot ceiling

03:08:43.479 --> 03:08:44.380
at this portion of the tunnel,

03:08:44.947 --> 03:08:46.149
and with the torchlight,
you do carry,

03:08:49.118 --> 03:08:49.385
you're pretty sure there's
nothing on the ceiling, but...

03:08:50.787 --> 03:08:51.287
who knows.

03:08:52.688 --> 03:08:52.822
We're absolutely safe.

03:08:55.124 --> 03:08:56.359
-I'm gonna scurry ahead.
-Yeah, peek around.

03:08:58.528 --> 03:08:58.828
Yeah. Can we see what's making
that scurrying noise ahead?

03:08:59.328 --> 03:08:59.896
Can we...?

03:09:00.963 --> 03:09:01.764
-Scooby-Doo?
-Yeah.

03:09:02.799 --> 03:09:03.332
One by one,
the heads go boop, boop!

03:09:05.535 --> 03:09:06.369
They appear in a totem.

03:09:07.537 --> 03:09:08.371
You can see,
in this next chamber,

03:09:10.740 --> 03:09:11.607
a cluster of pots
and small cases,

03:09:12.742 --> 03:09:13.409
all open or broken
in various states,

03:09:16.579 --> 03:09:17.547
and there is a dressed humanoid.

03:09:18.548 --> 03:09:19.448
You see from the back
that it's currently

03:09:19.715 --> 03:09:20.683
rummaging
through one of these right now.

03:09:22.718 --> 03:09:23.953
You can see some coins
spill out of its grasp.

03:09:25.321 --> 03:09:25.955
It reaches in and snatches them
and puts them in a pocket

03:09:27.356 --> 03:09:28.357
and is just talking to itself.

03:09:29.458 --> 03:09:29.792
-Is it a goblin?
-Oh my God. Is it a goblin?

03:09:33.262 --> 03:09:34.764
-Is it a treasure goblin?
-It's hard to see from the side.

03:09:36.799 --> 03:09:37.066
"Kill him!" I just yell.

03:09:38.067 --> 03:09:38.367
(indistinct)

03:09:39.101 --> 03:09:39.435
MIMICS GUN

03:09:40.469 --> 03:09:40.770
Roll attack.

03:09:42.572 --> 03:09:42.772
Roll attack.

03:09:43.639 --> 03:09:44.674
(indistinct)

03:09:45.708 --> 03:09:46.209
Get away!

03:09:47.476 --> 03:09:48.377
I've blocked the door,

03:09:48.878 --> 03:09:49.378
blocked the hallways,
so it can't run.

03:09:50.012 --> 03:09:50.446
Roll to attack twice.

03:09:50.913 --> 03:09:51.414
Actually, do I...?

03:09:54.350 --> 03:09:54.550
Will I get hatred for this?

03:09:55.651 --> 03:09:56.853
This is the first round
of combat.

03:09:58.487 --> 03:09:58.888
Actually, I can't. I wouldn't
have enough hatred, so no.

03:09:59.689 --> 03:10:00.923
Hungering Arrow.

03:10:03.492 --> 03:10:04.093
Okay. Two... Those are both.
That's a natural 20 and an 18.

03:10:05.127 --> 03:10:05.728
-A natural 20?
-Yeah.

03:10:06.462 --> 03:10:06.929
That's a critical hit. Yeah.

03:10:07.597 --> 03:10:08.564
Roll damage on both,

03:10:09.699 --> 03:10:09.932
doubling the dice damage
on the first one.

03:10:10.566 --> 03:10:11.133
Okay.

03:10:13.035 --> 03:10:13.369
What do I roll? New class.

03:10:18.574 --> 03:10:19.008
Okay. First one. That's a 4,
so 8 doubled, plus 5.

03:10:21.310 --> 03:10:21.844
So, 13. Wait, no.

03:10:23.512 --> 03:10:23.946
-Yes.
-Eight doubled, plus five.

03:10:24.380 --> 03:10:25.481
No, no. 4 doubled.

03:10:27.283 --> 03:10:28.417
Oh, got you. Got you.
So, 4 doubled is 8. So 8 plus 5.

03:10:30.486 --> 03:10:31.087
-That brings it to 13.
-Thirteen damage on the crit.

03:10:32.655 --> 03:10:33.556
And then, for the other one,

03:10:35.625 --> 03:10:35.925
I rolled a one on damage,
so 6 total.

03:10:38.160 --> 03:10:38.761
Gotcha. Okay.
So, 19 damage total.

03:10:39.896 --> 03:10:40.329
So, as you close the door...

03:10:40.529 --> 03:10:41.797
Fire above these.

03:10:43.900 --> 03:10:44.166
The individual turns around and
you see, for a brief second,

03:10:45.635 --> 03:10:46.669
just a dude

03:10:49.472 --> 03:10:49.739
in normal clothes,

03:10:53.276 --> 03:10:53.509
with a small package,
who just goes,

03:10:54.744 --> 03:10:54.977
"What?

03:10:55.778 --> 03:10:56.178
Argh!"

03:10:56.846 --> 03:10:57.513
Treasure goblin!

03:10:58.014 --> 03:10:59.315
He spits blood out of his mouth,

03:11:01.050 --> 03:11:01.384
and there are two crossbow bolts
on his chest and he's like...

03:11:03.753 --> 03:11:04.287
-Oh!
-"Argh!"

03:11:05.755 --> 03:11:06.022
Who?

03:11:07.189 --> 03:11:07.690
Was I not...?

03:11:08.591 --> 03:11:09.725
Was I not supposed to?

03:11:12.295 --> 03:11:12.895
He falls onto the ground
and he's like bleeding out.

03:11:13.829 --> 03:11:14.230
-Ooh.
-Ah! Run away.

03:11:18.534 --> 03:11:22.772
Run to him. "Do you have a key
to the lock on the other side?"

03:11:24.774 --> 03:11:25.408
"Who are you?"

03:11:26.575 --> 03:11:27.476
-Oh.
-Splitting blood.

03:11:29.145 --> 03:11:30.012
-Like...
-Just let him die and Laslo--

03:11:30.780 --> 03:11:31.414
...consecrate the ground
under this man.

03:11:33.449 --> 03:11:34.617
-Oh!
-Oh, really? Okay.

03:11:39.188 --> 03:11:39.622
He starts to heal. So does
everyone standing around him.

03:11:40.656 --> 03:11:40.923
Ooh, really? Okay.

03:11:44.794 --> 03:11:45.761
Four rounds of one D6 plus 2.

03:11:47.163 --> 03:11:48.030
What were you saying, Indra?

03:11:48.297 --> 03:11:49.565
I was gonna say
if you let him die,

03:11:51.734 --> 03:11:52.034
Laslo would have talked to him
and it have been much easier.

03:11:54.637 --> 03:11:55.104
He begins to heal up
a little bit of his wounds.

03:11:56.739 --> 03:11:57.606
Take the arrows out.

03:12:01.410 --> 03:12:01.677
He sits up and says,
"No, no. What do you want?

03:12:03.980 --> 03:12:04.380
Okay, stop.
I have to get to him."

03:12:05.614 --> 03:12:06.716
He grabs the bag

03:12:07.083 --> 03:12:08.284
and ignores you until he goes
back into the boxes,

03:12:11.020 --> 03:12:11.287
and takes whatever he can find
and throws it in the sack.

03:12:13.456 --> 03:12:13.656
"Give what for whom?"

03:12:15.958 --> 03:12:16.058
"For the child."

03:12:20.863 --> 03:12:22.198
It needs me. It needs
all the treasure and valuables."

03:12:23.666 --> 03:12:24.934
"Don't think about it."

03:12:27.670 --> 03:12:27.803
The eyes glance past all of you
as his wounds heal back to full.

03:12:28.771 --> 03:12:29.939
Whoa, whoa.

03:12:34.010 --> 03:12:37.279
I just transformed my arm
into a crocodile arm.

03:12:39.749 --> 03:12:40.149
I'm a werecrocodile.
That means my arms--

03:12:41.384 --> 03:12:42.284
I know, I know.

03:12:43.686 --> 03:12:44.754
-Just like a crocodile.
-Fair enough.

03:12:46.288 --> 03:12:46.555
I was picturing the crocodile
with fur, though.

03:12:47.390 --> 03:12:47.957
Me too!

03:12:49.158 --> 03:12:50.426
(indistinct)

03:12:52.628 --> 03:12:53.195
Sanctuary ecology is a little
different than earth ecology.

03:12:54.530 --> 03:12:55.364
Crocodiles here, be furry.

03:12:57.066 --> 03:12:57.333
-Okay.
-However you wanna picture it.

03:12:58.034 --> 03:12:59.135
Wild look in his eyes,

03:13:02.571 --> 03:13:03.572
he's surrounded by 5
well armored dungeon delvers.

03:13:05.141 --> 03:13:06.308
At this point,
he is wearing normal clothing

03:13:08.477 --> 03:13:09.578
and is currently holding,
in one hand, this half-open bag

03:13:10.679 --> 03:13:10.946
and with the other,
pulls out a dagger and goes...

03:13:14.216 --> 03:13:15.184
"Give me your belongings!
Give me your valuables!"

03:13:16.952 --> 03:13:17.920
I pull out my crossbows
and point them at him.

03:13:21.157 --> 03:13:21.290
Annex is very happy
at all of this.

03:13:24.126 --> 03:13:24.727
"Kill him again. Do it again."

03:13:25.795 --> 03:13:27.797
See, Annex knows what's up.

03:13:28.230 --> 03:13:28.664
"Honestly...

03:13:31.967 --> 03:13:33.069
you're about 5 seconds
from that being your reality,

03:13:35.171 --> 03:13:35.371
if you don't stop and tell us
what you're doing."

03:13:39.108 --> 03:13:39.742
"He'll kill me if I don't bring
enough back for him."

03:13:42.711 --> 03:13:44.213
-"Who's the child?"
-"The child below."

03:13:45.781 --> 03:13:46.882
"Through the door, with a lock?"

03:13:48.617 --> 03:13:49.085
"Beyond that, aye!"

03:13:50.119 --> 03:13:52.421
"So you have a key?"

03:13:54.323 --> 03:13:54.590
"Maybe."

03:13:55.291 --> 03:13:56.358
"Tell you what...

03:13:59.662 --> 03:13:59.795
We'll bring all your treasure
to the child for you."

03:14:02.531 --> 03:14:03.432
"No, no. I have to do it.

03:14:03.833 --> 03:14:04.100
l have to."

03:14:06.669 --> 03:14:07.169
"All right,
how about an exchange?

03:14:07.970 --> 03:14:09.205
You can come with us."

03:14:11.006 --> 03:14:11.207
"Okay.

03:14:13.142 --> 03:14:15.144
When we get there,
you'll give me your belongings?"

03:14:15.744 --> 03:14:16.011
"Sure.

03:14:17.146 --> 03:14:17.446
What's your name?"

03:14:18.681 --> 03:14:19.582
"Johnny."

03:14:21.016 --> 03:14:21.617
-"Johnny?"
-"Johnny."

03:14:23.219 --> 03:14:24.954
"Nice to meet you, Johnny."

03:14:27.356 --> 03:14:27.857
-"Yeah. Give them to me."
-"Not now."

03:14:28.057 --> 03:14:28.157
"I'll keep it, then."

03:14:29.425 --> 03:14:29.725
-"Sure."
-"Okay."

03:14:33.562 --> 03:14:33.829
And he lifts the bag up
over one shoulder like this.

03:14:35.731 --> 03:14:36.365
Half-crazed...

03:14:38.134 --> 03:14:38.501
Santa-gnome figure...

03:14:39.068 --> 03:14:39.869
blinks a lot in front.

03:14:40.936 --> 03:14:41.937
"So, go on. Follow him."

03:14:43.105 --> 03:14:43.439
I really did think
he was a treasure goblin.

03:14:44.673 --> 03:14:45.341
I did, too.

03:14:47.409 --> 03:14:48.144
I was about to confirm
all of my theories

03:14:48.744 --> 03:14:49.612
for this
other dimensional realm,

03:14:50.846 --> 03:14:51.280
which is filled
with gold and treasure.

03:14:52.848 --> 03:14:53.282
I was this close.

03:14:54.316 --> 03:14:55.284
I know it's real.

03:14:56.218 --> 03:14:57.052
I'm regretting my choice

03:14:58.854 --> 03:14:59.388
to bring this man back
from the brink.

03:15:02.791 --> 03:15:03.292
Looks over you
with this mostly gum-filled,

03:15:03.959 --> 03:15:04.193
occasional tooth grin.

03:15:05.461 --> 03:15:05.661
GROWLS

03:15:07.229 --> 03:15:07.363
-Well...
-"Oh, oh, wait."

03:15:08.063 --> 03:15:09.064
He reaches into his pocket

03:15:10.633 --> 03:15:10.900
and pulls out
this long rusty key and goes,

03:15:11.200 --> 03:15:14.270
"Here."

03:15:14.837 --> 03:15:15.271
He pulls a dagger out.

03:15:16.138 --> 03:15:16.739
"There you go."

03:15:18.374 --> 03:15:18.507
You know what? Have a seat.

03:15:21.610 --> 03:15:22.111
If you want me
to help you all...

03:15:24.480 --> 03:15:24.947
I need to meditate for a while.

03:15:26.282 --> 03:15:29.185
How long?

03:15:30.452 --> 03:15:30.786
Thirty to sixty minutes.

03:15:31.086 --> 03:15:31.854
(indistinct)

03:15:32.821 --> 03:15:34.757
-We just got started.
-I know.

03:15:36.492 --> 03:15:37.893
We'll just do a montage.
It's fine.

03:15:39.428 --> 03:15:41.330
What's a montage?

03:15:41.864 --> 03:15:43.265
It's a great hotel.

03:15:47.536 --> 03:15:48.537
It's with a bunch of activities
that have taken a long time

03:15:51.173 --> 03:15:52.074
and shortened
to an easy-to-grasp scenario.

03:15:52.875 --> 03:15:53.275
Let Johnny and Spell Slots
put arrows in--

03:15:54.810 --> 03:15:55.811
Oh, I love him.

03:15:57.913 --> 03:15:58.180
-Tauro does push-ups.
-Yeah.

03:15:58.781 --> 03:15:59.715
Are you taking a rest here?

03:16:02.284 --> 03:16:02.484
If the game
and the group will allow it.

03:16:02.885 --> 03:16:03.886
That's up to you, guys.

03:16:05.454 --> 03:16:06.689
I'll just mark it here.

03:16:07.556 --> 03:16:08.157
-Mark it.
-Good.

03:16:09.992 --> 03:16:10.292
Things are happening below.

03:16:11.727 --> 03:16:12.561
It's up to you.

03:16:14.296 --> 03:16:16.131
It's skin off your backs,
not mine.

03:16:18.968 --> 03:16:21.270
All right, I guess. Fine.

03:16:23.172 --> 03:16:24.240
-Okay.
-I think it's a good idea.

03:16:26.375 --> 03:16:26.775
We could ask our little friend
a little bit more

03:16:28.344 --> 03:16:30.879
about "Johnny"?

03:16:32.348 --> 03:16:34.717
"We're not going?

03:16:35.351 --> 03:16:35.484
We're not moving."

03:16:36.118 --> 03:16:36.785
"Well..."

03:16:38.687 --> 03:16:39.221
-"Thirty--"
-"You were hurt.

03:16:39.488 --> 03:16:40.055
And he had to heal you.

03:16:41.257 --> 03:16:41.957
So, now he needs to rest."

03:16:43.959 --> 03:16:44.326
Could have been avoided
if we'd let him die like I said,

03:16:45.361 --> 03:16:45.894
but whatever.

03:16:48.497 --> 03:16:49.431
-Well--
-He's looking through his bag.

03:16:50.032 --> 03:16:50.833
He's ignoring the questions
for the moment.

03:16:51.100 --> 03:16:51.567
He's checking,
counting things...

03:16:53.435 --> 03:16:53.702
"What is it? Okay."

03:16:55.170 --> 03:16:55.237
Spell Slots,

03:16:57.339 --> 03:17:00.776
do you know
any good musical routines?

03:17:04.913 --> 03:17:07.449
Lazlo is not excited
about Spell Slots.

03:17:10.552 --> 03:17:13.422
He has become
a stepdad overnight.

03:17:15.958 --> 03:17:17.960
He's (indistinct)
all the attention.

03:17:20.429 --> 03:17:21.363
Laslo's not very happy
about Spell Slots.

03:17:22.731 --> 03:17:23.632
But what did you ask? I'm sorry.

03:17:24.199 --> 03:17:26.101
If he knows
any good musical numbers.

03:17:27.469 --> 03:17:32.041
Hey, buddy.

03:17:36.145 --> 03:17:36.578
Can you play those things,
like a xylophone or something?

03:17:37.479 --> 03:17:38.380
Do you know any...

03:17:40.282 --> 03:17:40.649
Kanye or do you know...?

03:17:42.117 --> 03:17:42.685
What can you do?

03:17:44.787 --> 03:17:45.120
What is... What is his...?

03:17:45.988 --> 03:17:46.355
(indistinct)

03:17:48.991 --> 03:17:49.325
The Soca Room is a well-known
travelling bar.

03:17:49.992 --> 03:17:50.259
(indistinct)

03:17:51.293 --> 03:17:53.996
I was...

03:17:56.865 --> 03:17:58.567
Oh, just deep tracks?
God, Spell Slots!

03:17:59.068 --> 03:18:01.537
Give me some hits.

03:18:05.140 --> 03:18:06.342
This skeleton mainly sits
in a dark house vicinity.

03:18:07.209 --> 03:18:08.344
Not quite hitting the right
vibe for you, unfortunately.

03:18:10.479 --> 03:18:10.779
But it's the only skeleton
you've got at the moment.

03:18:14.116 --> 03:18:14.683
Well, say, you finish
your 30-minute period of rest.

03:18:15.751 --> 03:18:16.352
When it comes to an image,

03:18:16.552 --> 03:18:17.653
you all stand at the ready.

03:18:19.388 --> 03:18:20.356
You can see that Johnny
is looking very impatient,

03:18:21.824 --> 03:18:22.791
pacing, going,
"Come on, come on," to himself,

03:18:23.759 --> 03:18:24.626
his eyes looking
at nothing in particular.

03:18:26.762 --> 03:18:27.196
Then you hear
this distant shriek...

03:18:29.064 --> 03:18:29.264
down the hallway, just like...

03:18:31.033 --> 03:18:31.367
MATT SHRIEKS

03:18:32.935 --> 03:18:33.569
Oh, come on.

03:18:35.404 --> 03:18:36.105
A ghoul...

03:18:36.638 --> 03:18:38.207
-That was really cool.
-Creep.

03:18:40.609 --> 03:18:41.143
-So, what are you gonna do?
-All right.

03:18:41.410 --> 03:18:42.010
Are you feeling better?

03:18:43.212 --> 03:18:44.947
Come on, autotune skeleton.

03:18:45.714 --> 03:18:46.315
Let's go.

03:18:48.617 --> 03:18:54.723
That's not even early Kanye.

03:18:58.227 --> 03:18:58.861
All right. As you head back
towards the large iron door,

03:19:01.363 --> 03:19:01.630
indeed, the key does open it.

03:19:03.031 --> 03:19:03.298
As the door...

03:19:04.233 --> 03:19:04.566
.opens to the side,

03:19:04.833 --> 03:19:05.734
you can see

03:19:07.102 --> 03:19:08.303
there's an annexed portion
of the chamber.

03:19:10.005 --> 03:19:10.639
The hallways curves
to the right slightly.

03:19:11.073 --> 03:19:12.007
And following with the light,

03:19:13.842 --> 03:19:14.610
eventually, that opens
into wide archways

03:19:17.713 --> 03:19:18.614
and this faint glow
of candlelight

03:19:18.814 --> 03:19:19.882
that greets you
on the opposite side.

03:19:22.785 --> 03:19:23.352
You can see a beautiful display
of large statues

03:19:24.386 --> 03:19:25.220
depicting angelic figures,

03:19:27.456 --> 03:19:28.323
a central one
in heavy armor and hood,

03:19:29.324 --> 03:19:30.159
that's looming
over a wide staircase,

03:19:32.327 --> 03:19:32.394
the hood itself empty,
sword in front.

03:19:35.397 --> 03:19:36.331
You can see
this staircase descends below,

03:19:36.832 --> 03:19:37.399
but standing
before this armored figure,

03:19:40.402 --> 03:19:40.602
you see a humanoid shape,

03:19:43.372 --> 03:19:43.872
wearing its own haphazard armor,

03:19:44.506 --> 03:19:44.940
turned away from you.

03:19:45.374 --> 03:19:48.110
And as it spins...

03:19:49.778 --> 03:19:49.978
you see this...

03:19:52.214 --> 03:19:53.182
skeletal entity

03:19:58.654 --> 03:19:59.188
wearing old rusted,
dusty Horadric armor.

03:20:00.189 --> 03:20:01.023
As it looks back
towards you all,

03:20:02.291 --> 03:20:04.693
as you spin
around the edge, it...

03:20:05.894 --> 03:20:06.695
And as it races its hands,

03:20:06.962 --> 03:20:08.197
you can hear
the sound of scratches,

03:20:11.667 --> 03:20:12.534
as the walls you now notice
are filled, ceiling to floor,

03:20:14.169 --> 03:20:14.736
with stone tombs
that begin to spill.

03:20:15.337 --> 03:20:15.838
MATT MIMICS TOMBS CRASHING

03:20:16.104 --> 03:20:17.105
The lid spilling open

03:20:19.341 --> 03:20:19.875
as skeletons scramble out
in your direction.

03:20:20.409 --> 03:20:21.009
They swarm towards you,

03:20:21.577 --> 03:20:22.444
as the one-armored skeleton

03:20:22.978 --> 03:20:24.213
begins to curl
its hands in the air.

03:20:26.849 --> 03:20:27.549
And you see arcane runes swirl
on the floor in front of it.

03:20:28.650 --> 03:20:28.951
I need all of you
to roll.

03:20:29.418 --> 03:20:30.285
Oh boy...

03:20:30.919 --> 03:20:32.488
Whatever.
We've got a skeleton, too.

03:20:32.855 --> 03:20:33.255
It's true.

03:20:35.524 --> 03:20:36.158
All right. Top of the run.

03:20:36.725 --> 03:20:37.926
Remi, Laslo, you can see now,

03:20:39.328 --> 03:20:39.995
one central armored skeleton
that stands taller than the rest

03:20:41.530 --> 03:20:42.464
that is currently in the process

03:20:44.666 --> 03:20:45.300
of some sort
of dark purple incantation.

03:20:45.767 --> 03:20:46.668
The energy is swirling off it

03:20:47.035 --> 03:20:47.436
and the rune on the ground
begins to break.

03:20:48.303 --> 03:20:49.505
You can see now

03:20:52.608 --> 03:20:52.741
four other skeletons that
have crawled out of the tombs,

03:20:53.375 --> 03:20:54.409
drawing rusted weapons

03:20:55.077 --> 03:20:55.677
and beginning to scatter
their way towards you.

03:20:55.878 --> 03:20:57.079
And in the back of the room,

03:20:59.515 --> 03:20:59.982
two of the skeletons that fell,
bringing a total of six,

03:21:00.315 --> 03:21:01.283
have bows and arrows

03:21:03.018 --> 03:21:03.886
and begin to reach back,
pulling them taut.

03:21:07.422 --> 03:21:10.692
So, here we go.
8 D8s and heartbreak.

03:21:12.227 --> 03:21:12.861
-What are you two doing?
-I'm gonna whip my arm up.

03:21:15.764 --> 03:21:16.265
And my snake's gonna shoot
forward from my arm,

03:21:17.666 --> 03:21:18.800
and a spiritual blade

03:21:20.802 --> 03:21:21.737
is gonna shoot forward
towards the armored creature.

03:21:22.538 --> 03:21:23.071
-Oh, cool.
-And I'm gonna cast Windshear.

03:21:23.739 --> 03:21:25.007
You've got it. Okay.

03:21:26.642 --> 03:21:27.109
Go ahead. Roll an attack for it.
Which one? The one in the armor?

03:21:28.510 --> 03:21:32.648
-Yes.
-Okay.

03:21:34.416 --> 03:21:35.083
Seventeen to hit.

03:21:35.918 --> 03:21:36.685
-That indeed hits.
-Yes!

03:21:38.954 --> 03:21:42.357
So, that's 3D 8.

03:21:43.926 --> 03:21:44.560
Matt, you said there was...

03:21:46.128 --> 03:21:46.328
one big baddie and two...?

03:21:49.865 --> 03:21:50.432
Two archers
and four melee skeletons.

03:21:50.899 --> 03:21:51.500
Okay. And one big baddie?

03:21:52.467 --> 03:21:52.834
-Yeah.
-That's okay.

03:21:53.902 --> 03:21:54.636
So, 11 damage.

03:21:55.304 --> 03:21:56.171
Eleven points of damage.
Not bad.

03:21:58.373 --> 03:21:59.007
But my movement
has increased by 10 feet

03:21:59.274 --> 03:22:00.409
until the end of my next turn.

03:22:02.644 --> 03:22:02.844
Indeed. Don't forget to generate
eight spirit from that.

03:22:02.911 --> 03:22:04.313
Yes.

03:22:05.047 --> 03:22:05.714
All righty.

03:22:09.051 --> 03:22:10.052
As the blast of razor-sharp wind

03:22:11.086 --> 03:22:12.054
arcs off your hand
and strikes the creature,

03:22:13.288 --> 03:22:14.423
it shears off
part of its shoulder armor.

03:22:15.357 --> 03:22:16.592
It cracks in the bone.

03:22:17.726 --> 03:22:17.993
You see his thing damaged from
the impact, but it stands there,

03:22:19.328 --> 03:22:20.162
continuing to cast,

03:22:21.663 --> 03:22:22.331
its arm
still undulating in space.

03:22:23.465 --> 03:22:24.099
How far away is it from me now?

03:22:24.566 --> 03:22:25.400
You guys are at the entrance,

03:22:25.834 --> 03:22:26.234
so that's about
15 feet from you.

03:22:29.271 --> 03:22:29.705
And the melee skeletons
quickly rushing in

03:22:29.972 --> 03:22:31.173
at the same plain.

03:22:32.074 --> 03:22:32.441
The archers are about 30 feet
from you in the distance.

03:22:33.909 --> 03:22:34.776
I'm gonna run forwards

03:22:37.379 --> 03:22:37.879
since I've got
extra movement speed.

03:22:38.180 --> 03:22:41.249
I'm gonna run forward.

03:22:43.085 --> 03:22:43.719
I'm gonna run towards
the armored guy,

03:22:44.252 --> 03:22:44.620
just straight into the middle.

03:22:44.820 --> 03:22:45.921
Easily enough.

03:22:48.724 --> 03:22:49.191
Then I'm gonna throw a
bonus action cast swarm at him.

03:22:49.958 --> 03:22:50.659
You've got it.

03:22:52.894 --> 03:22:53.428
All right, as you rush forward
towards the front,

03:22:55.130 --> 03:22:55.464
in your awesome druid...

03:22:57.366 --> 03:22:57.599
swamp druid form.

03:22:59.267 --> 03:23:00.435
Dart towards him. As you do,
you bring your arm up.

03:23:03.138 --> 03:23:03.772
And out of the inside of
your outfit, insects crawl out

03:23:04.206 --> 03:23:05.173
and whip around this creature.

03:23:06.441 --> 03:23:07.042
-Which roll to attack?
-Fifteen plus seven.

03:23:09.578 --> 03:23:15.117
Fifteen plus seven hits.
Roll damage for that.

03:23:18.286 --> 03:23:19.287
-Six points of damage.
-Six points of damage.

03:23:20.255 --> 03:23:21.123
It's swirling around inside.

03:23:22.424 --> 03:23:22.691
Since this is not
a fleshy creature,

03:23:23.625 --> 03:23:24.459
you can hear them buzzing

03:23:25.060 --> 03:23:25.661
and hitting the inside
of the rib cage.

03:23:26.561 --> 03:23:27.062
The armor from the interior

03:23:27.829 --> 03:23:28.664
is sustaining damage,

03:23:29.931 --> 03:23:30.465
but not as much
as you would hope

03:23:30.766 --> 03:23:31.667
given the circumstances.

03:23:32.668 --> 03:23:33.802
But you are now
right in front of it.

03:23:34.770 --> 03:23:35.671
You can see, within its
deep, sunken, dark sockets,

03:23:37.572 --> 03:23:37.906
these faint points
of glowing purple energy

03:23:40.475 --> 03:23:41.276
matching the same arcane force

03:23:42.544 --> 03:23:42.744
that its currently
calling to it.

03:23:43.478 --> 03:23:44.780
That finishes your turn.

03:23:46.682 --> 03:23:47.315
You are right in the center now.
All eyes are currently on you.

03:23:48.316 --> 03:23:48.950
Laslo, what are you doing?

03:23:51.620 --> 03:23:52.220
As Remi starts to run forward,

03:23:54.022 --> 03:23:54.690
Laslo gets down on one knee

03:23:56.258 --> 03:23:56.892
and starts punching the cement.

03:23:58.293 --> 03:23:59.361
And I'm gonna cast Death Nova.

03:24:02.364 --> 03:24:02.898
So, all this smoke
is coming up... above him.

03:24:04.199 --> 03:24:04.700
But below him, I guess.

03:24:05.233 --> 03:24:05.300
You got it.

03:24:07.669 --> 03:24:08.770
So, it's a DC 15
constitution save.

03:24:10.539 --> 03:24:11.406
It is. It's also all creatures,
just so you know.

03:24:12.441 --> 03:24:13.341
That does include
your friends too.

03:24:14.576 --> 03:24:14.810
So, you're gonna
wanna try to maneuver.

03:24:17.045 --> 03:24:17.879
Yeah, so, if he's 15 feet...

03:24:21.116 --> 03:24:21.717
Is she right at 15 feet
or at 10 feet?

03:24:22.084 --> 03:24:23.318
She's 15 feet ahead of you.

03:24:25.787 --> 03:24:26.455
You'd have to go far to one side
of the other to avoid her.

03:24:26.888 --> 03:24:29.491
-Yeah, let's do that.
-Okay.

03:24:30.158 --> 03:24:31.293
Right or left corner?

03:24:33.862 --> 03:24:34.196
Left. We've avoided left
this entire game.

03:24:35.263 --> 03:24:35.597
You got it.

03:24:35.864 --> 03:24:36.765
To the left.

03:24:39.134 --> 03:24:39.534
You Zoolander over
to the left-hand corner,

03:24:42.637 --> 03:24:43.472
punch the ground
and this green energy swirls up

03:24:44.740 --> 03:24:45.674
and with the impact,
darts outward.

03:24:47.676 --> 03:24:48.877
All this toxic, poisonous,
magical energy

03:24:51.113 --> 03:24:51.680
radiates outward and swarms
into and hits the two skeletons

03:24:52.280 --> 03:24:53.815
and the central skeleton.

03:24:56.485 --> 03:24:59.287
It's a minimal effect.
Go ahead and roll damage.

03:25:00.622 --> 03:25:00.756
Twelve.

03:25:01.957 --> 03:25:02.224
-Twelve damage.
-All right.

03:25:03.625 --> 03:25:04.126
You've got it.

03:25:04.793 --> 03:25:05.694
It hits them.

03:25:07.596 --> 03:25:12.000
You watch
as they withdraw from this.

03:25:14.236 --> 03:25:14.302
They do all fail their saves,
but even so,

03:25:17.305 --> 03:25:17.873
poison doesn't seem
to have the same impact

03:25:18.940 --> 03:25:19.841
on the skeletal entities.

03:25:21.576 --> 03:25:21.777
You realize that moment,
like, "Damn!"

03:25:24.312 --> 03:25:24.479
Did some damage, but not as much
as you'd have hoped.

03:25:26.748 --> 03:25:29.317
And Spell Slots can take
his turn as well, if he'd like.

03:25:30.385 --> 03:25:31.186
Go, Spell Slots!

03:25:32.053 --> 03:25:33.155
Getting ready for it. Yeah.

03:25:34.723 --> 03:25:35.624
He's gonna make a melee attack
at the closest one.

03:25:37.159 --> 03:25:40.362
You got it. All right.

03:25:43.799 --> 03:25:44.132
-Eleven.
-Eleven does not hit.

03:25:44.399 --> 03:25:45.534
Spell Slots.

03:25:47.702 --> 03:25:48.603
He goes... and arcs wide
and hits off the bones now.

03:25:49.304 --> 03:25:49.938
It's just skeleton
and skeleton slap fight.

03:25:50.839 --> 03:25:53.308
He's a college drop-out.

03:25:56.278 --> 03:25:57.646
Hey, game in the room
for a little bit.

03:25:59.281 --> 03:26:01.049
That finishes you turn, Laslo?

03:26:03.618 --> 03:26:03.819
-Yes.
-All right. Mordred, you're up.

03:26:04.085 --> 03:26:05.220
Yes.

03:26:09.224 --> 03:26:10.358
I'm going to charge in
and run up alongside Remallia.

03:26:13.028 --> 03:26:13.128
And as I do, I'm going
to recite the Laws of Justice,

03:26:13.929 --> 03:26:15.130
so that I and my companions

03:26:19.367 --> 03:26:20.001
are resistant to cold, fire
and lightning damage for a bit.

03:26:25.307 --> 03:26:25.507
Takes away 4 points of wrath and
I will punish the big baddie.

03:26:28.243 --> 03:26:28.610
with two swings
of my Morning Star.

03:26:29.644 --> 03:26:29.911
You've got it.

03:26:32.347 --> 03:26:32.781
As a note for you as well,
which I just recalled,

03:26:33.982 --> 03:26:34.783
after you strike,

03:26:36.151 --> 03:26:37.052
the creature insects
swarm around it.

03:26:37.485 --> 03:26:38.386
And this pulse of energy
comes off it.

03:26:39.888 --> 03:26:40.322
You watch as these
arcane needles shoot out

03:26:41.456 --> 03:26:41.523
in your direction.

03:26:43.592 --> 03:26:43.925
And you did on that one.

03:26:44.960 --> 03:26:46.795
You took...

03:26:49.798 --> 03:26:50.065
five points of fire damage
as they blast on you.

03:26:52.133 --> 03:26:52.567
It seemed to almost reflect
some of the damage back at you.

03:26:54.769 --> 03:26:55.604
-What do you do on your turn?
-I...

03:26:56.304 --> 03:26:56.838
Bonus action
from Laws of Justice,

03:26:57.272 --> 03:26:57.939
which gives resistance.

03:26:58.573 --> 03:26:59.574
I don't know if it was in time.

03:27:00.408 --> 03:27:01.543
Not for her, but it will
for the next round.

03:27:03.945 --> 03:27:05.080
Cold fire and lightning
till the start of my next turn.

03:27:07.215 --> 03:27:08.083
And then I used Punish,
so I got two attack actions,

03:27:10.018 --> 03:27:10.452
and when I rolled,
I got 22 on both.

03:27:10.952 --> 03:27:11.152
Both of those hit.

03:27:14.322 --> 03:27:15.624
Perfect. That is one D8.

03:27:16.925 --> 03:27:17.893
Five plus seven.

03:27:19.895 --> 03:27:20.562
Six is thirteen.

03:27:20.795 --> 03:27:21.496
This is against the armored one?

03:27:22.764 --> 03:27:23.598
-Hm-hmm.
-The armored one--

03:27:25.400 --> 03:27:25.467
-Against the... cast.
-You've got it.

03:27:29.271 --> 03:27:29.537
That buffs up my own AC a bit

03:27:33.041 --> 03:27:33.541
and charges my wrath again,
and that's the end of my turn.

03:27:35.277 --> 03:27:35.810
That was 13 damage
for both of those.

03:27:37.479 --> 03:27:38.046
All told.

03:27:38.346 --> 03:27:39.447
You've got it. All righty.

03:27:40.582 --> 03:27:41.850
So, as you go ahead and strike
with both of those,

03:27:43.318 --> 03:27:43.418
your flail hitting at the side,
once again over the shield.

03:27:46.154 --> 03:27:46.554
Each impact blasts into you and
you can see it from the impact.

03:27:47.589 --> 03:27:48.156
And that same...

03:27:48.790 --> 03:27:49.391
arcane energy seems to...

03:27:50.525 --> 03:27:51.593
fire that damage back out at you

03:27:55.363 --> 03:27:55.697
as these two spears
of burning white hot magic.

03:27:58.366 --> 03:27:58.833
That is a 13 that misses you.

03:28:00.969 --> 03:28:01.269
But a 24 does hit you.

03:28:02.203 --> 03:28:02.704
You take...

03:28:03.638 --> 03:28:04.773
It would be 7 points
of fire damage,

03:28:07.542 --> 03:28:07.642
but because of your resistance,
it reduces it to 3.

03:28:08.510 --> 03:28:09.411
Nice. Good call.

03:28:11.446 --> 03:28:11.980
All right,
finishing up Mordred's turn

03:28:14.482 --> 03:28:14.683
is now Kresh
the Unforgiven's turn.

03:28:16.017 --> 03:28:16.418
-Kresh?
-Kresh?

03:28:16.718 --> 03:28:17.953
The Unforgiven?

03:28:20.021 --> 03:28:21.056
The armored skeleton you can see
now finishes its casting,

03:28:22.524 --> 03:28:23.425
and as it does,
in the center of the floor...

03:28:24.392 --> 03:28:24.726
a new skeleton appears.

03:28:28.897 --> 03:28:30.832
You get the sense this one can
just bring more skeletons.

03:28:33.335 --> 03:28:34.135
-That's a sense we get, guys.
-You get a sense of that.

03:28:35.704 --> 03:28:36.104
It's a weird thing
about that one

03:28:37.439 --> 03:28:38.974
See if that recharges.

03:28:40.475 --> 03:28:41.643
Yeah, it recharges.

03:28:43.678 --> 03:28:44.312
It is going to then
do a burning dart,

03:28:44.579 --> 03:28:45.613
as it's standing right there.

03:28:45.880 --> 03:28:46.848
It's gonna go ahead
and fling the dart at you

03:28:48.650 --> 03:28:49.150
since you're the one
who first came at it.

03:28:49.818 --> 03:28:51.653
And you're the one...

03:28:52.554 --> 03:28:53.655
actually it's gonna go for you

03:28:53.955 --> 03:28:55.223
since you're the one
who did the most damage to it.

03:28:56.224 --> 03:28:56.858
Natural 19.

03:29:00.462 --> 03:29:00.962
That's put it at a 23 to hit.

03:29:03.565 --> 03:29:04.165
So you take 10 fire damage
reduced to 5

03:29:05.633 --> 03:29:06.267
as it blasts into your face.

03:29:06.534 --> 03:29:07.702
The shield catches part of it

03:29:10.972 --> 03:29:11.373
and the rest of you lawful
defense manages to shrug it off.

03:29:13.141 --> 03:29:13.408
That feels good.

03:29:17.278 --> 03:29:18.446
Finishing its turn, that brings
us to Tauro and Indra.

03:29:19.381 --> 03:29:20.215
Do you want me to go first or..?

03:29:21.683 --> 03:29:22.517
What is the new scales
and holding?

03:29:23.151 --> 03:29:23.284
Is it a melee
or is it an archer?

03:29:24.552 --> 03:29:25.220
-That is a melee.
-Okay.

03:29:26.021 --> 03:29:27.655
Try executioner's axe actually.

03:29:29.024 --> 03:29:29.557
-Why did I ask?
-Charming.

03:29:30.291 --> 03:29:31.393
-You can go first.
-Okay.

03:29:34.596 --> 03:29:35.196
I'm just gonna slowly walk up,
drawing my crossbows

03:29:37.465 --> 03:29:38.233
I'm gonna say
"if it bleeds, you can kill it."

03:29:40.301 --> 03:29:44.706
And I'm gonna cast
Mark for Death.

03:29:46.307 --> 03:29:47.275
"Well,
the big vein bleeds a little."

03:29:47.776 --> 03:29:48.376
Right?

03:29:48.777 --> 03:29:51.546
"It bleeds a little, guys."

03:29:53.114 --> 03:29:55.517
You all go "yeah".

03:29:58.286 --> 03:29:58.787
I don't wanna do
hungering arrow.

03:29:59.554 --> 03:30:00.789
We got there.

03:30:03.892 --> 03:30:06.127
The whole group is like
"yes, and..."

03:30:06.895 --> 03:30:07.896
Don't stop for improv.

03:30:08.797 --> 03:30:08.997
You know that I don't want
to jack your job.

03:30:10.598 --> 03:30:11.566
Don't worry.

03:30:13.101 --> 03:30:13.768
It's not my fault
this is the line

03:30:15.403 --> 03:30:15.970
that they've set for disability.

03:30:16.471 --> 03:30:17.372
Alright.

03:30:18.373 --> 03:30:19.207
So what are the rules?

03:30:19.707 --> 03:30:20.775
And you're respecting
which ones?

03:30:22.243 --> 03:30:22.577
I'm gonna attack,
just 2 hits of the big baddie.

03:30:23.511 --> 03:30:24.079
You got it.

03:30:26.381 --> 03:30:27.015
Okay, so that first 1 is a 17

03:30:28.983 --> 03:30:29.851
and the second attack is a 23.

03:30:30.919 --> 03:30:31.119
Both hit.
Go ahead and roll damage.

03:30:32.921 --> 03:30:33.421
And these are extra-D6's,

03:30:35.390 --> 03:30:36.024
because he is marked.

03:30:37.025 --> 03:30:38.359
So, for the first 1...

03:30:39.861 --> 03:30:42.063
Okay, lets...

03:30:42.697 --> 03:30:43.198
11 damage total.

03:30:44.365 --> 03:30:44.833
11 damage, you got it.

03:30:46.067 --> 03:30:47.268
For the second 1...

03:30:48.570 --> 03:30:49.070
Go ahead.

03:30:50.338 --> 03:30:50.772
...is a...

03:30:52.440 --> 03:30:52.707
13 damage total.

03:30:53.208 --> 03:30:53.441
Nice.

03:30:54.442 --> 03:30:54.642
So, as you come around and...

03:30:56.511 --> 03:30:57.645
You fired twice out
of the arrows

03:30:58.847 --> 03:30:59.013
Hit the arm and you can see
another chunk falls off.

03:31:00.582 --> 03:31:01.249
The bones are
now splintering

03:31:01.516 --> 03:31:02.584
from the impact they have taken.

03:31:04.519 --> 03:31:05.420
It's having a hard
time holding itself together.

03:31:05.687 --> 03:31:06.788
And all the other skeletons
around it

03:31:08.857 --> 03:31:09.657
are eager to rush in
and try and offer protection.

03:31:10.592 --> 03:31:10.859
You also notice...

03:31:11.593 --> 03:31:14.062
Not bleeding.

03:31:14.496 --> 03:31:14.696
Not yet.

03:31:16.831 --> 03:31:18.199
-Yet, exactly.
-Go back to the writers.

03:31:20.301 --> 03:31:20.568
Systemic dialogue.

03:31:21.669 --> 03:31:23.238
Roll with it.

03:31:25.406 --> 03:31:25.940
Alright, finishing your go.
Indra.

03:31:26.274 --> 03:31:26.541
-Question.
-Yes.

03:31:28.076 --> 03:31:28.877
-Big baddie is here.
-Yeah.

03:31:30.745 --> 03:31:30.912
My friends are in front of him.

03:31:31.946 --> 03:31:32.814
-Directly?
-Directly in front of him.

03:31:33.681 --> 03:31:33.848
However,
the archers are behind him.

03:31:35.450 --> 03:31:35.984
How close
would you say they are?

03:31:36.251 --> 03:31:36.551
They'd be about 15 feet.

03:31:37.152 --> 03:31:38.052
Wonderful!

03:31:39.320 --> 03:31:39.454
As in a 15 feet diameter
could catch...

03:31:42.023 --> 03:31:42.724
both this big baddie
and these archers.

03:31:44.359 --> 03:31:45.560
Cool.
Then I'm going to...

03:31:46.394 --> 03:31:47.462
Flick my hair behind my...

03:31:48.196 --> 03:31:49.330
get it caught on my lip-gloss
like a cool person

03:31:49.964 --> 03:31:50.198
and then I'm gonna cast a meteor
right in the middle.

03:31:50.865 --> 03:31:51.266
Okay.

03:31:52.600 --> 03:31:53.902
-Okay.
-Yes.

03:31:55.270 --> 03:31:56.171
Hoping to end this quickly.

03:31:58.506 --> 03:31:58.773
Indra is just gonna
scoff as she...

03:32:00.542 --> 03:32:00.808
summons a giant meteor from...

03:32:01.776 --> 03:32:01.910
-...above?
-Yeah.

03:32:02.544 --> 03:32:03.545
-So...
-No?

03:32:05.346 --> 03:32:05.947
As you watch,
Idra pulls the staff forward.

03:32:08.483 --> 03:32:09.651
(indistinct) kinda spins
her staff in the air.

03:32:10.885 --> 03:32:11.586
You're all engaged in this
skeleton until you hear this...

03:32:12.854 --> 03:32:13.721
This horrible, tearing sound

03:32:14.656 --> 03:32:15.023
and you all can't
help but glance up

03:32:16.724 --> 03:32:17.392
As in the air above
this staircase,

03:32:17.926 --> 03:32:19.127
and where this battle has taken,

03:32:21.462 --> 03:32:22.263
you see a slither of reality
is suddenly carved and open.

03:32:24.632 --> 03:32:24.832
And you see
a dark expanse of stars.

03:32:26.334 --> 03:32:27.035
And purplish-blue mist.

03:32:29.337 --> 03:32:31.472
And from that, a bright light
as a flaming rock...

03:32:32.173 --> 03:32:33.341
appears out of it

03:32:34.943 --> 03:32:35.410
and slams into the top of
the staircase and explodes.

03:32:35.877 --> 03:32:36.344
You can see flames.

03:32:37.045 --> 03:32:38.279
Just spirals around

03:32:40.448 --> 03:32:41.316
and almost engulfs both of you
at the front of this battle

03:32:42.750 --> 03:32:43.751
but just manages
to singe your eyebrows.

03:32:44.018 --> 03:32:44.986
You don't have any
so you don't have to worry

03:32:45.253 --> 03:32:46.087
But it does catch you
a little off guard.

03:32:47.822 --> 03:32:48.489
This thing called
hair on my body.

03:32:49.857 --> 03:32:50.124
Go ahead,
roll damage on that.

03:32:53.328 --> 03:32:53.761
I had to bring out
extra D6's for this one.

03:32:54.562 --> 03:32:58.533
Good lord.

03:32:58.866 --> 03:32:59.067
Twelve.

03:33:00.468 --> 03:33:02.103
Who's good at math here?

03:33:02.904 --> 03:33:03.504
-No.
-Best luck.

03:33:04.272 --> 03:33:04.706
-Just say it.
-Okay

03:33:06.674 --> 03:33:07.475
Twelve plus eight.

03:33:08.243 --> 03:33:08.943
Plus 5

03:33:10.311 --> 03:33:10.511
Plus 5.

03:33:11.346 --> 03:33:12.180
Plus 7.

03:33:12.814 --> 03:33:13.648
Thirty-seven
points of fire damage.

03:33:14.182 --> 03:33:14.816
Thirty-seven
points of fire damage.

03:33:15.083 --> 03:33:15.717
And you spell DC on that one?

03:33:17.318 --> 03:33:18.653
-Sixteen dex.
-Got it.

03:33:19.887 --> 03:33:20.822
Failure to crush the unforgiven.

03:33:23.258 --> 03:33:23.858
-Failure on the archer.
-Love hearing it.

03:33:24.425 --> 03:33:24.959
Failure on the other archer.

03:33:28.529 --> 03:33:28.796
As the flames and explosion
die down for a second,

03:33:29.530 --> 03:33:30.398
the sound you hear

03:33:31.733 --> 03:33:32.834
is the clattering
of scattered bones

03:33:34.702 --> 03:33:35.136
raining down from the opposite
side of the chamber.

03:33:36.070 --> 03:33:36.938
As the 2 archer skeletons
are blown apart

03:33:39.507 --> 03:33:39.674
and thrown
across the opposite side.

03:33:42.310 --> 03:33:43.244
The central skeleton armor
you now see as it looks out

03:33:44.746 --> 03:33:45.013
the purple light in its eye
blinks out,

03:33:45.713 --> 03:33:46.047
and the bones...

03:33:48.716 --> 03:33:49.784
scatter on the inside
and hitting the ground.

03:33:50.752 --> 03:33:50.852
Destroyed.

03:33:52.954 --> 03:33:53.488
Indra brushes off
some dust of her shoulder

03:33:53.955 --> 03:33:54.222
and is like "Pathetic."

03:33:55.023 --> 03:33:55.857
The big guy?

03:33:56.858 --> 03:33:57.759
Yeah,
he just fell to the ground,

03:33:59.027 --> 03:33:59.527
but there are still
4 other skeletons.

03:34:00.695 --> 03:34:01.429
Five technically,
one with a giant axe.

03:34:03.064 --> 03:34:03.264
And it's now their turn.

03:34:05.266 --> 03:34:05.733
Where's the dude
we came in here with?

03:34:05.933 --> 03:34:06.467
Is he hanging back?

03:34:07.135 --> 03:34:08.069
He's not in this battle.

03:34:08.336 --> 03:34:08.836
-He's in the hallway.
-He's back there?

03:34:09.671 --> 03:34:11.606
Yeah, with his dagger.

03:34:13.908 --> 03:34:14.108
"I'm Johnny,
what do you want from me!"

03:34:17.712 --> 03:34:18.046
-And the one-liner: I'm Johnny!
-"I'm Johnny!"

03:34:18.813 --> 03:34:19.080
He is hisown movie
right now.

03:34:20.315 --> 03:34:20.815
Exactly.

03:34:21.582 --> 03:34:22.183
With the proper NPC,

03:34:22.450 --> 03:34:23.284
once you cycle the dialogue,

03:34:23.951 --> 03:34:24.319
he just has
the one thing to say.

03:34:25.753 --> 03:34:28.956
"I'm Johnny!"

03:34:32.026 --> 03:34:33.428
Two skeletons
rushing up towards you.

03:34:34.028 --> 03:34:34.162
Remy?

03:34:35.430 --> 03:34:36.297
Going to strike.
That's a natural 20.

03:34:37.432 --> 03:34:37.865
That's 8 points
of physical damage.

03:34:41.803 --> 03:34:42.003
And the other 1
is gonna be a 20 to hit.

03:34:45.006 --> 03:34:45.273
Four points physical damage.
A total of twelve against you.

03:34:46.574 --> 03:34:46.774
Cool.

03:34:47.775 --> 03:34:48.443
Other 2
are rushing up against you,

03:34:48.943 --> 03:34:49.844
since you're right in the front.

03:34:51.746 --> 03:34:52.814
That's a 1, which misses.

03:34:53.348 --> 03:34:54.182
Another natural 20.

03:34:55.316 --> 03:34:55.917
You take 8 points
of physical damage

03:34:57.051 --> 03:34:57.285
from that secondary strike.

03:34:57.552 --> 03:34:58.619
Okay.

03:34:59.220 --> 03:34:59.721
And they're just swarming
at you, hacking away.

03:35:00.855 --> 03:35:01.222
And the 1 with the...

03:35:03.157 --> 03:35:03.424
executioner's axe...

03:35:05.226 --> 03:35:07.395
let's roll to see
which 1 of you it goes after.

03:35:07.895 --> 03:35:10.698
You.

03:35:12.633 --> 03:35:13.968
I'm sitting there going.

03:35:16.704 --> 03:35:17.472
Just looking over at him
suggestively.

03:35:19.807 --> 03:35:20.808
-So, here's the thing.
-If it bleeds, you can kill it.

03:35:22.276 --> 03:35:22.477
They're aware.

03:35:24.512 --> 03:35:25.380
As the 2 skeletons rush
and you're fighting them off

03:35:25.747 --> 03:35:26.614
you can't help
but in the background

03:35:27.548 --> 03:35:28.182
see the 1 skeleton
glance up at you.

03:35:29.717 --> 03:35:30.485
It's head cocked to one side,

03:35:30.985 --> 03:35:31.586
as it slowly lifts
this massive axe

03:35:34.856 --> 03:35:35.456
that weighs immense amounts.

03:35:36.057 --> 03:35:36.391
-Oh no.
-'Sup buddy.

03:35:37.458 --> 03:35:38.159
Large swing,

03:35:40.361 --> 03:35:40.461
right into the ground,
about a foot from you.

03:35:41.996 --> 03:35:42.630
Not a great aim
on this skeleton.

03:35:43.598 --> 03:35:44.465
Probably used to using an axe

03:35:45.299 --> 03:35:45.833
and just completely
misses entirely.

03:35:45.900 --> 03:35:48.636
Kind of looks at you...

03:35:50.238 --> 03:35:51.773
"This is awkward,
I feel bad for you."

03:35:52.874 --> 03:35:53.875
And it's now wedging
out of the ground

03:35:54.742 --> 03:35:58.279
which brings us back to
Remy and Laslo's go.

03:36:00.114 --> 03:36:01.349
Wait, are they in a line?

03:36:03.618 --> 03:36:05.353
They are pretty close to a line.

03:36:06.954 --> 03:36:07.455
Actually, 3 of them
are in a line.

03:36:09.891 --> 03:36:10.158
Doesn't matter,
can't do it anyway.

03:36:11.426 --> 03:36:13.694
Hold on.

03:36:15.763 --> 03:36:16.597
"But they're close
to each other?"

03:36:17.131 --> 03:36:17.665
"They're within 5 feet
of each other."

03:36:18.733 --> 03:36:19.400
Three of them are, yes.

03:36:20.067 --> 03:36:20.435
Yes, screw it.

03:36:21.569 --> 03:36:22.737
"I'm gonna...

03:36:24.105 --> 03:36:24.472
...look up...

03:36:26.741 --> 03:36:27.642
and find a big piece of rock

03:36:29.811 --> 03:36:30.077
from the pile of meteorite
that fell down."

03:36:30.711 --> 03:36:31.646
You got it.

03:36:33.381 --> 03:36:34.282
"I'm gonna lift it up
and cast Landslide

03:36:36.451 --> 03:36:37.718
on 3 of the creatures
in front of me."

03:36:39.387 --> 03:36:39.720
Hopefully including the one with
the giant executioner's axe.

03:36:42.023 --> 03:36:42.957
Go ahead and roll attack
for all 3 of them.

03:36:43.991 --> 03:36:45.793
Executioner's axe
and the 2 next to him.

03:36:48.162 --> 03:36:48.796
-Get it Stevie Nicks.
-Ah, he beat me to it.

03:36:52.333 --> 03:36:52.600
 And if you see my reflection...

03:36:54.802 --> 03:36:56.437
The first one is...

03:36:58.072 --> 03:36:58.339
-Who was singing there?
-Oh no, damn.

03:37:01.175 --> 03:37:01.476
The first one is 17.

03:37:02.009 --> 03:37:02.810
That hits.

03:37:03.544 --> 03:37:04.011
Do I add anything?
Oh, yes I do.

03:37:04.512 --> 03:37:05.012
The first one is 24.

03:37:05.713 --> 03:37:06.214
That definitely hits.

03:37:08.316 --> 03:37:08.616
The second one is 13.

03:37:08.950 --> 03:37:09.584
Just hits.

03:37:09.851 --> 03:37:10.852
Why do you still have your...

03:37:11.686 --> 03:37:12.920
And the last one
definitely hits, it's a 23.

03:37:16.224 --> 03:37:16.924
**** natural damage
for each of them.

03:37:17.725 --> 03:37:18.359
-Okay.
-This is individual.

03:37:20.328 --> 03:37:20.461
Three D10.

03:37:20.928 --> 03:37:22.196
Executioner first.

03:37:26.200 --> 03:37:26.667
Three plus nine is twelve
plus six is eighteen.

03:37:29.337 --> 03:37:30.438
Eighteen, other two?

03:37:32.907 --> 03:37:33.307
Nine, fifteen...

03:37:34.208 --> 03:37:34.442
Seventeen.

03:37:35.476 --> 03:37:37.044
Okay.

03:37:39.947 --> 03:37:40.548
Five plus six
is eleven on the last one.

03:37:42.149 --> 03:37:42.216
Got it.

03:37:45.253 --> 03:37:46.120
So, as you pull up
a chuck of the meteor

03:37:48.155 --> 03:37:48.789
that was summed
through space by Indra,

03:37:49.790 --> 03:37:50.157
you lift it up to the ceiling

03:37:51.859 --> 03:37:52.760
with a crack impact
that brings elements

03:37:54.128 --> 03:37:55.029
of dirt and earth
and rock from above.

03:37:56.230 --> 03:37:57.131
As it slams down
to the central space,

03:37:58.666 --> 03:37:59.734
broken apart
from the multiple impacts,

03:38:02.203 --> 03:38:03.104
it cause a shower
of sharp shards of rock, stone

03:38:04.805 --> 03:38:05.439
and whatever piece
of the nearby structure

03:38:06.173 --> 03:38:06.574
that was carved free from it,

03:38:07.441 --> 03:38:08.609
and as it does,

03:38:11.145 --> 03:38:12.179
you watch the executioner
skeleton axe high in the air

03:38:13.247 --> 03:38:14.315
for a secondary
strike is smashed beneath it,

03:38:15.816 --> 03:38:16.817
flattened into a bunch
of broken pieces of bone.

03:38:18.519 --> 03:38:18.920
The 2 other skeletons
to its side look up...

03:38:20.521 --> 03:38:21.722
and are simultaneously
smashed as well.

03:38:23.558 --> 03:38:24.258
We're down to 2 skeletons,
that brings us to you, Laslo.

03:38:25.326 --> 03:38:26.193
Are they in a row?

03:38:29.130 --> 03:38:29.697
They're in a row,
but distant from each other.

03:38:31.332 --> 03:38:31.999
They're on opposite ends.

03:38:33.234 --> 03:38:33.834
I'd say 30 feet from each other.

03:38:35.770 --> 03:38:36.704
I'm just gonna run up to 1,

03:38:38.172 --> 03:38:38.873
place my hands on its head
and Siphon it.

03:38:40.408 --> 03:38:40.741
Can it Siphon its blood?
Does it have blood?

03:38:41.008 --> 03:38:41.309
Siphon life.

03:38:42.543 --> 03:38:43.344
Life, yes.

03:38:43.511 --> 03:38:43.945
It's a little more
of an essence.

03:38:45.813 --> 03:38:50.418
-Exactly.
-'Cause video game.

03:38:50.985 --> 03:38:51.986
Nineteen.

03:38:52.053 --> 03:38:57.358
Nineteen does hit.
Go ahead and roll damage.

03:38:59.193 --> 03:39:01.829
Mordred, you're on deck.

03:39:03.931 --> 03:39:04.632
-Ten.
-Ten damage, that does it.

03:39:07.401 --> 03:39:08.302
As you reach out
and extend your hand towards it,

03:39:09.570 --> 03:39:10.171
you watch as it
(indistinct) and shake

03:39:11.005 --> 03:39:12.006
and what faint bit of magic

03:39:14.041 --> 03:39:15.209
still remains holding it
animate is pulled away.

03:39:15.977 --> 03:39:17.111
The skeleton almost seems
to implode in your direction

03:39:19.447 --> 03:39:19.714
sending bones scattering
to the ground by your feet.

03:39:20.581 --> 03:39:21.215
And you heal up on D4.

03:39:22.550 --> 03:39:22.817
Awesome.

03:39:23.618 --> 03:39:24.919
-Four.
-There you go.

03:39:27.822 --> 03:39:28.823
While I'm doing this Spell Slot
is running to the other side.

03:39:30.625 --> 03:39:31.325
-To hit the other dude?
-To hit the other dude.

03:39:31.525 --> 03:39:32.660
-You got it.
-It's so sad.

03:39:33.828 --> 03:39:38.332
I'm picturing him a lot smaller
than the other guy.

03:39:39.100 --> 03:39:39.367
Let's see what he does.

03:39:40.167 --> 03:39:40.635
He's trying so hard.

03:39:40.868 --> 03:39:42.003
He's trying so hard.

03:39:45.206 --> 03:39:46.207
The way you keep describing him,
I imagine him in Yeezys.

03:39:48.442 --> 03:39:51.212
-Yeezys and joggers.
-Yeah!

03:39:52.013 --> 03:39:52.613
Fourteen.

03:39:53.581 --> 03:39:53.848
Fourteen does hit.

03:39:56.350 --> 03:39:56.751
What's the collateral damage
for the last standing skeleton.

03:39:57.284 --> 03:39:57.952
Three.

03:39:58.619 --> 03:40:00.087
Three damage.

03:40:01.756 --> 03:40:02.189
Big old heavy fist fall

03:40:04.392 --> 03:40:05.326
into the skeleton, which takes
the hit but it's still standing.

03:40:06.661 --> 03:40:07.895
It's looking damaged
but it's still standing.

03:40:08.696 --> 03:40:09.563
That finishes...

03:40:10.364 --> 03:40:11.465
what else have you got?

03:40:13.300 --> 03:40:13.834
I'm gonna cast Devour again,
if there's a bunch...

03:40:15.503 --> 03:40:15.803
oh, they're not corpses

03:40:16.671 --> 03:40:17.571
they're skeletons

03:40:18.139 --> 03:40:18.205
-They're...
-Do they could as corpses?

03:40:20.708 --> 03:40:22.243
They technically
would not count as corpses.

03:40:23.044 --> 03:40:24.011
-Then that's it.
-Sorry.

03:40:27.081 --> 03:40:27.415
Philosophical question,
are skeletons corpses?

03:40:29.250 --> 03:40:29.350
So, 2 are upright?

03:40:30.685 --> 03:40:31.152
-One is up.
-Just one?

03:40:31.552 --> 03:40:32.420
Yes.

03:40:35.322 --> 03:40:35.523
I just hoist up
my Morningstar and say,

03:40:36.791 --> 03:40:37.058
"I hate to do it

03:40:37.792 --> 03:40:42.396
No I don't"

03:40:42.930 --> 03:40:43.197
So, it's pulverized?

03:40:45.466 --> 03:40:46.267
-First this is...
-A punishment.

03:40:48.502 --> 03:40:48.836
Very low role-reversed.
That's a 10.

03:40:50.137 --> 03:40:50.304
Ten misses.

03:40:53.307 --> 03:40:53.808
And a very low roll for
the second so I hate to do it,

03:40:54.075 --> 03:40:54.809
so I don't do it. 12.

03:40:56.243 --> 03:40:57.178
-Twelve does hit.
-Does hit?

03:40:59.447 --> 03:41:00.715
Skeletons don't have
huge AC necessarily.

03:41:03.417 --> 03:41:04.351
Oh, but it's a 1 on the damage,
so 4 points of physical damage.

03:41:05.986 --> 03:41:08.355
Four points physical damage.
Still standing.

03:41:10.524 --> 03:41:10.791
You do about
as much damage as...

03:41:12.326 --> 03:41:12.593
(indistinct)

03:41:13.427 --> 03:41:14.428
The skeleton looks mad at you.

03:41:14.862 --> 03:41:16.063
Trying to blow it over the rest
of the way.

03:41:18.966 --> 03:41:20.601
It's mad-dogging you
from its eye-less sockets.

03:41:22.870 --> 03:41:24.805
Cresh is gone
so now it's Tauro and Indra.

03:41:25.973 --> 03:41:26.207
Alright, I...

03:41:28.909 --> 03:41:29.710
I'll just look at Indra and say
"Mind if I do the honors?"

03:41:32.279 --> 03:41:36.383
-Go for it.
-Just pull out a dagger.

03:41:38.085 --> 03:41:38.385
I'm gonna do my impale.

03:41:38.719 --> 03:41:40.187
Go for it.

03:41:41.355 --> 03:41:42.022
Come on, 17 or 20!

03:41:43.591 --> 03:41:43.891
I got a 19!

03:41:44.225 --> 03:41:44.959
Or an 18!

03:41:45.426 --> 03:41:45.726
-That's a crypt!
-That's a crypt.

03:41:48.996 --> 03:41:49.196
You can't see it but
we're not far from each other.

03:41:49.930 --> 03:41:50.798
Expression says it all.

03:41:54.335 --> 03:41:55.002
That get a critical hit
on 17 or 20.

03:41:56.737 --> 03:41:56.871
-Yeah.
-Or 17 through 20.

03:41:57.671 --> 03:41:59.306
And it's 2 D12 damage.

03:42:00.941 --> 03:42:01.142
Wait, let me get another D12.

03:42:02.777 --> 03:42:03.344
I never get to do this.

03:42:04.145 --> 03:42:04.712
...one hit point left is.

03:42:05.813 --> 03:42:08.783
Just wait for it.

03:42:10.484 --> 03:42:11.018
Socially distant DnD.

03:42:12.153 --> 03:42:12.520
Here we go.

03:42:15.489 --> 03:42:16.590
I never get to roll D12s,
this is awesome.

03:42:17.258 --> 03:42:17.858
Okay.

03:42:22.096 --> 03:42:22.363
So, that's 9 damage, so 18,

03:42:25.666 --> 03:42:25.866
plus 5.

03:42:28.002 --> 03:42:28.869
-Twenty-three points.
-Twenty-three points of damage.

03:42:30.070 --> 03:42:30.971
This skeleton is taking
blow-after-blow

03:42:31.238 --> 03:42:32.339
and it's standing
resolute against you

03:42:33.874 --> 03:42:34.775
and your companions around you
as it turns towards you.

03:42:36.110 --> 03:42:37.077
The dagger comes towards it
as time slows,

03:42:40.114 --> 03:42:40.481
sit there contemplates
in those final moments.

03:42:45.085 --> 03:42:46.620
Gary Jules playing
 Mad World right now.

03:42:48.055 --> 03:42:48.689
It considers...

03:42:50.624 --> 03:42:51.725
nothing as it's a skeleton,
it has no mind.

03:42:54.395 --> 03:42:55.229
Whereas the other skeletons
exploded into chunks of bone,

03:42:56.397 --> 03:42:57.464
the dagger impacts,

03:42:58.265 --> 03:43:00.601
and as it hits the grounds
and it turns to dust.

03:43:01.368 --> 03:43:01.936
The sheer force of it

03:43:04.772 --> 03:43:05.973
causing whatever possible

03:43:07.374 --> 03:43:07.441
undead willpower that held it
together to just atomize.

03:43:09.276 --> 03:43:11.078
You just hear my dagger go...

03:43:12.213 --> 03:43:13.480
"I think that's all of them."

03:43:15.049 --> 03:43:16.851
"That wasn't too bad."

03:43:17.818 --> 03:43:18.886
-Technical question?
-Yes.

03:43:19.520 --> 03:43:20.321
Since it was both of our turns
at the same time,

03:43:22.189 --> 03:43:22.857
do I still get that
6 arcane power?

03:43:25.159 --> 03:43:25.459
You get it back regardless
outside of the combat.

03:43:26.260 --> 03:43:27.094
You're one of the few
that generates,

03:43:28.362 --> 03:43:28.996
you're usually
at full arcane power

03:43:29.196 --> 03:43:29.797
at the beginning of the fight.

03:43:33.133 --> 03:43:33.267
The problem is,
a lot of you things cost a lot.

03:43:34.935 --> 03:43:35.870
So what we're saying
is that by the next round

03:43:37.104 --> 03:43:37.404
-I'll have full arcane power?
-You will.

03:43:38.472 --> 03:43:39.440
-I didn't know that.
-Lucky.

03:43:39.874 --> 03:43:40.474
There you go.
The fun thing about wizards.

03:43:43.244 --> 03:43:43.911
They don't have to build up
their resources, you start full.

03:43:44.445 --> 03:43:45.613
But you've got to be careful
what you use.

03:43:46.714 --> 03:43:47.314
Yeah, it's meteors ****,
whatever.

03:43:47.848 --> 03:43:47.982
-Meteors.
-Alrighty.

03:43:52.920 --> 03:43:53.554
So, checking the body of Cresh
amongst the armor

03:43:54.521 --> 03:43:55.756
you do find a couple of items,

03:43:56.991 --> 03:43:57.858
because it's Diablo and that's
one of the cool parts about it.

03:44:03.297 --> 03:44:03.864
You find a magical ring
of silver and gold inlay

03:44:08.836 --> 03:44:09.770
and beneath its helmet
you can see this burial shawl

03:44:11.839 --> 03:44:13.207
that seems to shimmer
in the torchlight.

03:44:15.509 --> 03:44:16.143
The shawl is considered
The Shawl Of The Forsaken,

03:44:16.343 --> 03:44:17.611
and it gives whoever wears it

03:44:19.513 --> 03:44:20.648
a plus 1 to hit on any of their
abilities that rolled a hit.

03:44:21.715 --> 03:44:22.650
The ring is
The Ring Of The Zakarum,

03:44:23.550 --> 03:44:24.151
which gives
a plus 1 to your armor class

03:44:26.053 --> 03:44:26.353
and saves whilst it's worn.

03:44:30.891 --> 03:44:32.059
As the one who casted the meteor
that took out this **** here,

03:44:33.093 --> 03:44:34.094
can I lay claim to the ring?

03:44:35.462 --> 03:44:35.729
Sure.

03:44:36.397 --> 03:44:37.264
Thank you,

03:44:38.198 --> 03:44:38.465
So, AC and (indistinct)
go up by 1.

03:44:40.534 --> 03:44:42.036
Who would like
The Shall Of The Forsaken?

03:44:45.472 --> 03:44:48.275
-I mean.
-"I'm good, with faith."

03:44:51.545 --> 03:44:52.012
Any one feel like they need a
little boost to their attacks?

03:44:52.813 --> 03:44:53.180
We are good as well.

03:44:55.249 --> 03:44:57.151
Onyx is so polite.

03:44:59.286 --> 03:45:03.991
"What about you, Spell Slots?"

03:45:05.993 --> 03:45:06.360
-Goes to Remy.
-You got it.

03:45:08.729 --> 03:45:08.963
Plus 1 to hit
on all your abilities.

03:45:09.997 --> 03:45:10.864
Sweet.

03:45:15.035 --> 03:45:15.536
Descending the stairway beyond
this encounter with Cresh,

03:45:17.738 --> 03:45:18.639
the air grows slightly warmer

03:45:19.573 --> 03:45:20.074
and carries a hint
of putrescence upon it.

03:45:22.843 --> 03:45:23.811
While the architecture remains a
continuation of the crypt above,

03:45:25.713 --> 03:45:26.046
these walls have seen
more wear and tear.

03:45:28.515 --> 03:45:29.516
Odd, black iron chains
dangle in places,

03:45:30.784 --> 03:45:31.585
some of them finishing
in large metal hooks.

03:45:34.121 --> 03:45:35.089
The recurring chair beliefs
and holy iconography you see

03:45:36.724 --> 03:45:37.291
are often scratched out
or gauged entirely

03:45:37.358 --> 03:45:38.092
from the walls around you.

03:45:38.993 --> 03:45:39.893
When the steps come to an end

03:45:41.061 --> 03:45:42.129
you can see
this much larger chamber,

03:45:44.765 --> 03:45:45.733
maybe 100 or so feet across,
but there are 4 smaller,

03:45:48.369 --> 03:45:50.537
almost mausoleum-like
doored chambers within.

03:45:52.339 --> 03:45:53.540
What would you like to do?

03:45:54.074 --> 03:45:55.109
Four...

03:45:56.243 --> 03:45:56.343
And they're closed?
The doors are all closed?

03:45:58.178 --> 03:45:58.445
Seems to be, yeah.

03:46:01.248 --> 03:46:02.049
Do we hear any noise?

03:46:02.483 --> 03:46:03.017
"Does Johnny
have any inclination

03:46:05.519 --> 03:46:05.786
of where this child is?"

03:46:06.387 --> 03:46:07.521
Johnny goes

03:46:09.023 --> 03:46:09.790
"Oh yeah, across the way
this door on the other side,

03:46:10.858 --> 03:46:11.525
that's where we're
supposed to be."

03:46:12.693 --> 03:46:13.193
"What's behind the other doors?"

03:46:14.762 --> 03:46:14.962
"The room
where the child is, come on."

03:46:16.797 --> 03:46:18.365
And you see him walking ahead.

03:46:21.335 --> 03:46:21.869
"Just let him go first,
like 15-20 feet."

03:46:22.069 --> 03:46:23.103
"Let's see what happens"

03:46:25.572 --> 03:46:25.973
"Also, he didn't answer
our question at all."

03:46:27.341 --> 03:46:27.608
"No, he didn't."

03:46:31.278 --> 03:46:31.578
We're gonna let him go
and see what happens.

03:46:32.479 --> 03:46:33.447
He walks along,

03:46:35.616 --> 03:46:35.816
picks up a gold piece
and put it in his sack.

03:46:36.216 --> 03:46:36.984
Takes a few more steps,

03:46:37.718 --> 03:46:38.719
"Oh, that's nice."

03:46:41.522 --> 03:46:43.690
Picks up a candleholder
and puts it in the bag.

03:46:44.391 --> 03:46:45.292
I run ahead of him

03:46:46.960 --> 03:46:48.829
and kick any pots
that are in the way.

03:46:50.130 --> 03:46:51.799
LAUGHTER

03:46:53.801 --> 03:46:54.401
He's like, "No, wait!"

03:46:54.835 --> 03:46:55.969
These pots are mostly empty.

03:46:56.837 --> 03:46:57.704
He does rush off into one
chamber with an open door.

03:46:59.039 --> 03:47:00.107
He goes, "Ooh,"
and darts in there.

03:47:01.241 --> 03:47:02.176
He's easily distracted
by his particular interest

03:47:05.312 --> 03:47:06.613
in finding worthwhile things
in the vicinity.

03:47:07.247 --> 03:47:08.315
He rushes in.

03:47:09.817 --> 03:47:11.085
There are the 4 chambers.
You pass the first 2.

03:47:12.886 --> 03:47:14.021
The one on the right is open,
the one on the right is ajar.

03:47:15.389 --> 03:47:15.489
He rushes to the left
and begins to push his way in.

03:47:18.058 --> 03:47:18.759
You see him disappear
inside that chamber.

03:47:20.794 --> 03:47:22.529
Are there any screams
coming from that chamber?

03:47:23.063 --> 03:47:24.064
You don't hear any.

03:47:26.166 --> 03:47:26.600
What about the one to the right?

03:47:27.301 --> 03:47:28.335
To the right?

03:47:29.503 --> 03:47:30.370
You don't hear anything
coming from that one.

03:47:31.405 --> 03:47:34.708
You want to make
a perception check?

03:47:35.609 --> 03:47:36.376
(GRUNTS)

03:47:37.678 --> 03:47:38.579
Twenty.

03:47:41.548 --> 03:47:41.982
As you glance through
and look into this open doorway,

03:47:43.383 --> 03:47:44.551
this next room...

03:47:47.354 --> 03:47:48.188
it's far more grotesque
than you were expecting.

03:47:48.455 --> 03:47:49.523
You can see,
all across the floor,

03:47:51.792 --> 03:47:52.192
there are dozens and dozens
of long-rotted corpses,

03:47:53.393 --> 03:47:54.428
mostly skeletal,

03:47:56.463 --> 03:47:57.664
bits of putrid flesh
still hanging on the bone.

03:48:00.200 --> 03:48:01.301
There are many chains
hanging from this room

03:48:04.705 --> 03:48:05.205
and bodies on hooks
all the meat has sloughed off.

03:48:07.741 --> 03:48:08.675
This has been here
for quite some time.

03:48:10.677 --> 03:48:11.311
It's been left still
and filled with rot.

03:48:12.880 --> 03:48:13.647
Glancing inside
in the middle of it,

03:48:16.049 --> 03:48:16.950
you see this squat,
tubby-looking,

03:48:18.685 --> 03:48:19.753
red and black skinned
demonic creature

03:48:21.588 --> 03:48:22.256
that is sitting with tiny,
scrawny legs and arms

03:48:24.258 --> 03:48:24.391
and this very wide mid section.

03:48:25.759 --> 03:48:26.727
It's horns are curled inwards.

03:48:28.295 --> 03:48:32.399
It's just sitting there,
chewing on a bone.

03:48:34.301 --> 03:48:35.402
-Does it see me?
-It does not see you.

03:48:37.538 --> 03:48:44.077
Make a stealth check,
actually, if you don't mind.

03:48:45.379 --> 03:48:47.514
Twelve.

03:48:48.182 --> 03:48:49.049
It looks up at you

03:48:51.084 --> 03:48:54.154
and darts off
into the shadow nearby.

03:48:55.389 --> 03:48:55.856
"Friend or foe?"

03:48:57.324 --> 03:48:57.925
There's a brief pause

03:48:59.626 --> 03:49:00.260
and a voice rings out
from the shadow that says,

03:49:04.298 --> 03:49:04.498
"You step into the realm of
Damershaal,

03:49:06.366 --> 03:49:06.900
the great Eater of Storms,

03:49:11.038 --> 03:49:11.338
Lord of Annihilation and
demon master of this dominion!"

03:49:11.705 --> 03:49:12.806
"Leave now

03:49:16.009 --> 03:49:16.643
or become devoured by
his immense and terrible form!"

03:49:17.211 --> 03:49:18.212
Does he sound full of (BLEEP)?

03:49:18.779 --> 03:49:24.418
Make an insight check.

03:49:25.652 --> 03:49:26.987
Great. Fourteen.

03:49:29.790 --> 03:49:32.759
It's easy to notice.
Yeah, he's full of (BLEEP).

03:49:34.928 --> 03:49:36.363
"Do we waste our time here?"

03:49:39.967 --> 03:49:40.234
"Are we supposed
to eradicate all of the evil?"

03:49:41.335 --> 03:49:44.004
"I am."

03:49:46.540 --> 03:49:47.174
I'm going to try
and drag him out

03:49:48.141 --> 03:49:49.243
of whatever cubbyhole he's in.

03:49:50.877 --> 03:49:51.311
Make a perception check
as you enter this chamber

03:49:52.846 --> 03:49:53.313
filled with bones.

03:49:55.082 --> 03:49:55.916
Not good. Four.

03:49:57.818 --> 03:49:58.151
You look in the room. You have
no idea where this thing is.

03:49:59.186 --> 03:49:59.853
You heard
the voice boom from it,

03:50:01.255 --> 03:50:01.788
but you push through the chains.

03:50:02.923 --> 03:50:02.990
The voice says, "I said

03:50:05.392 --> 03:50:06.560
run away before it's too late!"

03:50:07.894 --> 03:50:08.161
"Please!"

03:50:09.496 --> 03:50:10.664
"Please."

03:50:11.732 --> 03:50:12.699
"How long have you been here?"

03:50:14.935 --> 03:50:15.302
"Since time eternal,

03:50:16.470 --> 03:50:19.706
about a year."

03:50:21.675 --> 03:50:21.942
"We're hearing
about a child here."

03:50:24.244 --> 03:50:24.811
"Do you know
anything about that?"

03:50:25.779 --> 03:50:28.115
Make a persuasion check.

03:50:29.816 --> 03:50:30.083
That's much better.

03:50:32.152 --> 03:50:33.954
Twenty-one.

03:50:36.890 --> 03:50:37.457
Stepping out
from this cluster of bones

03:50:38.392 --> 03:50:39.526
that have melted together

03:50:41.428 --> 03:50:41.895
as the fats of the bodies
have solidified around it,

03:50:42.095 --> 03:50:42.763
he pokes out at you.

03:50:45.399 --> 03:50:46.466
This sad-looking demon creature,

03:50:49.002 --> 03:50:49.970
maybe about 3 feet
off the ground, scutters out.

03:50:51.238 --> 03:50:52.306
"Hi."

03:50:54.408 --> 03:50:56.276
"I'm Damershaal,
Eater of Storms."

03:50:57.778 --> 03:50:58.712
"Avatar form."

03:50:59.946 --> 03:51:01.214
"Much bigger
and dangerous in true form."

03:51:03.617 --> 03:51:04.384
"You're looking
for the child, right?"

03:51:05.018 --> 03:51:05.686
"Seem to be."

03:51:07.921 --> 03:51:08.188
"He's below, but the doors
are closed and locked."

03:51:09.923 --> 03:51:10.057
"You need..."

03:51:11.458 --> 03:51:12.025
He reaches behind the bodies
and pulls out

03:51:13.660 --> 03:51:15.062
this stone, circular seal.

03:51:16.496 --> 03:51:17.731
"You need this."

03:51:18.365 --> 03:51:18.498
"So give it."

03:51:20.334 --> 03:51:21.201
"How about we trade?"

03:51:23.503 --> 03:51:23.770
"I'm very hungry."

03:51:24.905 --> 03:51:25.972
"Not a lot...

03:51:28.709 --> 03:51:29.476
around here to eat any more."

03:51:31.144 --> 03:51:33.046
"Any fresh flesh?"

03:51:34.381 --> 03:51:36.249
"Johnny?"

03:51:38.752 --> 03:51:39.519
He comes out around the way
with a small box.

03:51:41.555 --> 03:51:42.189
He's like, "I found some...
Yeah?"

03:51:43.690 --> 03:51:47.027
Puts it in the satchel, "Yes?"

03:51:50.297 --> 03:51:50.897
"Someone in the room
is asking for you."

03:51:54.134 --> 03:51:59.106
He pulls a blade out.
Make a deception check.

03:52:00.374 --> 03:52:02.175
Nine.

03:52:03.243 --> 03:52:09.116
"What aren't you telling me?"

03:52:11.685 --> 03:52:15.622
-"Go in the room."
-Make an intimidation check.

03:52:17.357 --> 03:52:18.258
Come on, big money.

03:52:19.126 --> 03:52:19.626
Seventeen?

03:52:21.428 --> 03:52:21.728
Seventeen. He goes...

03:52:21.962 --> 03:52:22.229
(STUTTERS)

03:52:26.166 --> 03:52:27.701
"Of course, of course. Yeah.
Got to keep you all safe."

03:52:29.736 --> 03:52:30.203
He creeps in
with his dagger out.

03:52:32.072 --> 03:52:33.039
Walks into the room and sees...

03:52:35.308 --> 03:52:35.876
the creature and goes...

03:52:38.779 --> 03:52:40.080
"Kill it, kill it! There's
another one of them demons."

03:52:42.682 --> 03:52:44.651
I nod and smile
at our demon friend.

03:52:46.219 --> 03:52:46.353
"Make friends."

03:52:47.654 --> 03:52:48.722
-"Be nice."
-"For me?"

03:52:49.756 --> 03:52:52.793
"Don't be rude."

03:52:55.262 --> 03:52:56.797
-The demon walks forward.
-We're terrible.

03:52:57.531 --> 03:52:58.498
"What do you mean?"

03:53:01.401 --> 03:53:01.535
-I close the door behind me.
-"No, no, no!"

03:53:03.737 --> 03:53:04.070
As the door closes, you hear...

03:53:05.071 --> 03:53:05.372
(SCREAMING)

03:53:06.673 --> 03:53:07.207
(SNARLING)

03:53:08.041 --> 03:53:08.675
...the screams.

03:53:10.610 --> 03:53:11.178
And a section of the upper...

03:53:11.812 --> 03:53:12.746
What you didn't notice
on the walls,

03:53:14.514 --> 03:53:15.515
there are these faint,
remaining elements

03:53:17.217 --> 03:53:17.818
of stained glass reliefs
that are on the top.

03:53:18.018 --> 03:53:18.285
You see a bloody hand go...

03:53:19.186 --> 03:53:20.053
(SPLAT)

03:53:22.689 --> 03:53:23.356
...like a terrible twist
on the Titanic scene

03:53:24.958 --> 03:53:25.325
as blood smears down the glass.

03:53:25.959 --> 03:53:26.526
"Hey, buddy."

03:53:27.394 --> 03:53:28.161
"What you saw back there,

03:53:30.363 --> 03:53:32.265
that's not
how people usually act."

03:53:34.601 --> 03:53:35.202
"We were gonna get ice cream
later. It's gonna be fine."

03:53:36.169 --> 03:53:37.771
Spell Slots is just crying.

03:53:39.306 --> 03:53:39.973
"It started as a joke

03:53:42.476 --> 03:53:42.742
and then we just let it happen."

03:53:43.443 --> 03:53:43.910
"I'm proud of us."

03:53:44.110 --> 03:53:45.111
A few moments pass.

03:53:47.214 --> 03:53:47.514
It grows quiet
and the door opens once more.

03:53:48.548 --> 03:53:48.748
(SQUEAKS)

03:53:50.584 --> 03:53:51.518
You see the squat demon come out

03:53:54.287 --> 03:53:54.554
picking elements of muscle
from a freshly

03:53:55.822 --> 03:53:56.957
exposed bone.

03:54:00.527 --> 03:54:01.161
He goes, "Thank you very much.
That's a fine trade."

03:54:02.229 --> 03:54:02.996
"Good luck with the child."

03:54:04.631 --> 03:54:05.332
He tosses
the stone relief to you.

03:54:06.266 --> 03:54:07.467
"I'm gonna have leftovers
for a little bit."

03:54:10.804 --> 03:54:11.304
"Hey, do you have any use
for that bag of gold he had?"

03:54:11.404 --> 03:54:11.705
"Could we take that?"

03:54:13.340 --> 03:54:14.674
-"Go ahead."
-"Thank you."

03:54:16.042 --> 03:54:16.943
"All right."

03:54:19.379 --> 03:54:19.746
I believe Mordred
was in that room.

03:54:19.813 --> 03:54:20.313
He walks out,

03:54:22.883 --> 03:54:23.717
blood spattered across his face,
and says,

03:54:25.519 --> 03:54:27.087
"That was really
something to see."

03:54:28.455 --> 03:54:28.855
"Let's go."

03:54:29.723 --> 03:54:30.790
All right, we go downstairs.

03:54:32.359 --> 03:54:32.626
"We need to take care of him
on the way out, though."

03:54:34.494 --> 03:54:35.729
-"For sure."
-"Yeah."

03:54:37.564 --> 03:54:38.999
"Let him enjoy his last meal."

03:54:42.202 --> 03:54:43.069
Making your way to the doors
on the opposite side,

03:54:43.670 --> 03:54:44.571
there it is,

03:54:45.939 --> 03:54:47.040
you can see
the large, angelic reliefs

03:54:48.408 --> 03:54:48.975
both facing each other,
arms meeting in the center

03:54:50.510 --> 03:54:50.810
where the circular imprint

03:54:52.412 --> 03:54:52.612
currently awaits
the seal that you were given.

03:54:53.713 --> 03:54:54.881
Placing it in, the doors...

03:54:58.585 --> 03:54:59.152
open and lead you into a large,
stone, spiral staircase

03:54:59.786 --> 03:55:02.289
that descends out of view.

03:55:03.990 --> 03:55:05.725
"I feel so bad about Johnny."

03:55:07.594 --> 03:55:08.728
"You're having guilt now?"

03:55:09.796 --> 03:55:10.764
-"Too late."
-"I know it's too late."

03:55:12.699 --> 03:55:13.166
"You want to go back and kill
him? Would you feel better?"

03:55:14.100 --> 03:55:14.501
"No, no, it's fine."

03:55:17.003 --> 03:55:17.470
-"Let's take care of the child."
-"Okay."

03:55:20.507 --> 03:55:21.608
"We've got some reverse healing
to do, let's go."

03:55:24.611 --> 03:55:24.811
Partway down the stairs,
you find an alcove

03:55:28.114 --> 03:55:29.149
with a stone fountain of
some kind situated in the side.

03:55:30.717 --> 03:55:31.618
The water's still running
after all this time.

03:55:33.787 --> 03:55:34.154
As you pass by it,
a quick glance.

03:55:34.621 --> 03:55:35.188
The waters are

03:55:36.189 --> 03:55:36.656
red

03:55:38.258 --> 03:55:38.692
and thicker
than the average liquid.

03:55:40.694 --> 03:55:40.961
-Wine.
-Totally.

03:55:42.429 --> 03:55:42.996
Can I...

03:55:45.231 --> 03:55:45.932
touch it and feel it
with my fingers?

03:55:47.334 --> 03:55:47.934
-Sure.
-"What's it taste like?"

03:55:49.736 --> 03:55:50.537
-"I'm feeling it first."
-"Make sure you taste it."

03:55:52.038 --> 03:55:52.238
"Yeah, taste it."

03:55:52.973 --> 03:55:53.206
Somewhat viscous.

03:55:55.442 --> 03:55:55.709
The smell is somewhat iron-like.

03:55:56.676 --> 03:55:57.143
"What does it taste like,
though?"

03:55:58.678 --> 03:55:59.079
"I can't believe you tasted it."

03:55:59.512 --> 03:56:00.447
"That's gross."

03:56:02.849 --> 03:56:05.118
(SPLUTTERING)

03:56:07.821 --> 03:56:09.122
"It's blood. Turns out
this fountain bleeds."

03:56:10.557 --> 03:56:12.726
"Maybe it can die."

03:56:13.326 --> 03:56:15.762
"All right, let's go."

03:56:18.064 --> 03:56:18.698
Continuing
down the spiral staircase...

03:56:21.334 --> 03:56:21.901
I just like that
that's how they're bonding.

03:56:24.270 --> 03:56:27.107
"That was pretty good."

03:56:29.542 --> 03:56:29.809
At the base of the stairs,

03:56:32.512 --> 03:56:32.646
you find an open,
arched threshold

03:56:34.714 --> 03:56:35.248
that leads
into a massive shrine,

03:56:38.251 --> 03:56:38.451
long since repurposed
as a catacomb.

03:56:40.420 --> 03:56:41.354
The intricate walls
are lined with stone reliefs

03:56:43.990 --> 03:56:44.391
of angels and demons
fighting mid-battle

03:56:46.192 --> 03:56:46.826
rising tall
to the 30 foot ceiling above

03:56:50.597 --> 03:56:52.532
where hundreds of still lit
candles fill every open pocket.

03:56:56.036 --> 03:56:56.236
Dual curving stairs rise
against the sides of the wall

03:56:58.505 --> 03:56:59.572
to climb to a risen platform

03:57:01.274 --> 03:57:01.675
where a pulpit and altar sit
on top, to the back wall

03:57:02.709 --> 03:57:04.110
far from where you look up.

03:57:05.679 --> 03:57:05.879
The center of the room

03:57:08.048 --> 03:57:08.448
holds a half dozen,
heavy, intricate stone tombs,

03:57:11.518 --> 03:57:12.419
carvings of ancient warriors
carved atop the lids,

03:57:13.687 --> 03:57:14.287
a bit scattered
in their positioning.

03:57:15.055 --> 03:57:15.789
And the floor.

03:57:20.060 --> 03:57:20.193
The floor shines with thousands
and thousands of gold pieces

03:57:23.530 --> 03:57:24.864
glittering in the light between
the scattered piles of bones.

03:57:26.966 --> 03:57:27.634
The air suddenly grows
incredibly cold,

03:57:29.169 --> 03:57:29.569
your breath immediately visible.

03:57:31.805 --> 03:57:32.238
The candles
all flicker in unison,

03:57:34.340 --> 03:57:34.741
their flames shifting
from yellow-orange

03:57:36.209 --> 03:57:36.543
to a dull blue.

03:57:38.144 --> 03:57:38.845
Pale blue.

03:57:44.651 --> 03:57:45.719
You see a spectral entity rise,
from the gold on the floor.

03:57:47.120 --> 03:57:47.954
It's a child.

03:57:50.957 --> 03:57:51.858
A boy in his teenage years,
his clothes dirty and tattered.

03:57:54.494 --> 03:57:54.928
His left leg seems
to vanish past the knee.

03:57:58.064 --> 03:58:02.836
As he floats above
within the room...

03:58:07.373 --> 03:58:08.074
(ECHOING) "More imbeciles
come to help me out."

03:58:09.375 --> 03:58:09.843
"Great."

03:58:12.679 --> 03:58:15.014
"The bigger the network,
the easier the profit."

03:58:16.449 --> 03:58:17.617
"You...

03:58:19.986 --> 03:58:21.054
see this
depressingly small hoard."

03:58:22.422 --> 03:58:23.423
"It's nowhere near enough!"

03:58:26.926 --> 03:58:27.560
"Good help seems to always
be a challenge to find."

03:58:30.830 --> 03:58:32.031
"You all look slightly
less useless than the others."

03:58:33.633 --> 03:58:33.900
"You want to live?"

03:58:34.734 --> 03:58:35.001
"Go."

03:58:36.736 --> 03:58:37.070
"Get out there

03:58:41.274 --> 03:58:44.277
in the western kingdoms and
bring me some real treasure."

03:58:47.013 --> 03:58:49.716
He floats there
awaiting a response.

03:58:54.954 --> 03:58:57.757
"I don't know about you all,
but I had no plans to go west."

03:58:59.292 --> 03:59:01.027
"I also work for no one."

03:59:02.929 --> 03:59:04.531
"Just make yourselves useful."

03:59:05.098 --> 03:59:05.598
"I need gold."

03:59:08.501 --> 03:59:09.903
-"We'll make ourselves useful."
-"Give me some."

03:59:12.105 --> 03:59:14.474
His face pouts a little bit.

03:59:16.776 --> 03:59:18.545
"Why is it
so hard to find help?"

03:59:20.880 --> 03:59:21.447
"At least
Johnny's still out there."

03:59:23.750 --> 03:59:24.651
"He'll bring me back some gold."

03:59:26.119 --> 03:59:30.190
"I'm nowhere near close."

03:59:32.592 --> 03:59:33.593
"What do you need it for,
young one?"

03:59:37.530 --> 03:59:38.631
You can see the angry
frustration in the face

03:59:39.899 --> 03:59:41.801
melt away for a second
as the spirit's eyes go distant.

03:59:43.703 --> 03:59:43.970
"I need to help her."

03:59:45.772 --> 03:59:46.039
"She deserves it."

03:59:47.307 --> 03:59:48.141
"I made a promise
that I would help her

03:59:49.809 --> 03:59:50.176
and this is
nowhere near enough."

03:59:51.978 --> 03:59:52.178
"I can't leave
until I help her."

03:59:53.713 --> 03:59:54.781
As that echoes
through the chamber,

03:59:56.649 --> 03:59:57.317
you can see his spirit
flickers and grows wider.

03:59:58.251 --> 03:59:58.384
You see the wind whip up a bit.

03:59:59.853 --> 04:00:03.623
(BREATHES HEAVILY)

04:00:04.524 --> 04:00:09.095
"Who is 'she'?"

04:00:09.729 --> 04:00:13.433
"Gillian."

04:00:14.734 --> 04:00:18.137
"Are you going
to help me or not?"

04:00:22.976 --> 04:00:25.745
"We are going to help you
leave this mortal coil."

04:00:27.146 --> 04:00:27.981
"Come, boy."

04:00:29.582 --> 04:00:30.984
"Let's play."

04:00:32.452 --> 04:00:33.720
The spirit's eyes narrow

04:00:36.055 --> 04:00:36.656
and you watch as the chamber's
temperature drops even lower.

04:00:39.192 --> 04:00:39.659
Blue flames flicker
in his spiritual eyes.

04:00:42.595 --> 04:00:45.131
You watch
as all the candles begin to dim.

04:00:46.232 --> 04:00:47.166
"If you want to walk
to your death,

04:00:48.835 --> 04:00:50.870
that's entirely up to you,
armored boy."

04:00:52.205 --> 04:00:52.572
"Fine."

04:00:56.910 --> 04:00:57.744
"Let your spirit die
in some ways like mine did."

04:01:01.714 --> 04:01:02.882
You hear the rumbling as the
bones begin to rise up and form.

04:01:05.685 --> 04:01:06.185
You watch as these massive
skeletons begin to pull out

04:01:07.687 --> 04:01:08.922
of the hoards of gold.

04:01:12.325 --> 04:01:12.759
Not quite humanoid.
Larger, stranger.

04:01:15.395 --> 04:01:15.728
Bipedal, but shouldn't be.

04:01:18.197 --> 04:01:18.831
Large, elongated skulls

04:01:21.601 --> 04:01:21.701
with curved horns,
not unlike the one on your head.

04:01:25.738 --> 04:01:26.339
You see
massive, bovine-like skeletons,

04:01:28.241 --> 04:01:28.574
holding large glaives, rise.

04:01:30.310 --> 04:01:30.910
Two of them

04:01:32.245 --> 04:01:34.380
to each side of this spirit.

04:01:34.948 --> 04:01:36.149
"The cows."

04:01:37.116 --> 04:01:37.850
"It's the cows!"

04:01:40.119 --> 04:01:41.754
"You want to step
against the spirit of Wirt?"

04:01:42.455 --> 04:01:43.189
"Then fine."

04:01:44.958 --> 04:01:46.125
"Join me."

04:01:47.794 --> 04:01:50.096
Everyone roll initiative.

04:01:52.732 --> 04:01:53.132
So, at the top of this,

04:01:55.768 --> 04:01:56.269
you see this spirit
of this boy, Wirt,

04:01:57.837 --> 04:01:58.371
angrily begin to rise

04:01:59.405 --> 04:02:00.239
and extend his hands.

04:02:01.274 --> 04:02:02.308
You see him try
and push upwards,

04:02:03.343 --> 04:02:04.010
it's almost like something's
pulling him down.

04:02:05.311 --> 04:02:06.312
He gets frustrated for a second.

04:02:08.514 --> 04:02:10.917
He's gonna go ahead
and glance...

04:02:13.219 --> 04:02:13.987
towards you, Tauro.

04:02:15.488 --> 04:02:16.189
And say,

04:02:19.492 --> 04:02:19.625
"If Johnny's not gonna help, I
need someone else to help me."

04:02:20.860 --> 04:02:22.261
"You!"

04:02:23.863 --> 04:02:25.765
Make
a wisdom saving throw for me.

04:02:28.234 --> 04:02:28.501
-Saving throw?
-Correct.

04:02:30.136 --> 04:02:30.336
-Come on.
-Cocked!

04:02:31.704 --> 04:02:32.105
Keep's getting up in...

04:02:33.206 --> 04:02:33.272
That's real bad.

04:02:35.274 --> 04:02:35.808
I rolled a 2.

04:02:37.877 --> 04:02:38.144
Three total.

04:02:40.179 --> 04:02:41.014
I think that's probably safe.

04:02:44.984 --> 04:02:45.585
Blue flames now flicker
matchingly in the eyes of Tauro

04:02:46.586 --> 04:02:47.120
as you become Wirt's thrall.

04:02:47.320 --> 04:02:48.321
You are Charmed by him,

04:02:50.356 --> 04:02:50.857
and now working
on his side for the time being.

04:02:52.625 --> 04:02:53.693
Three cows.

04:02:54.861 --> 04:02:57.363
"No, no. I'm not one of..."

04:02:58.498 --> 04:02:58.765
"Good, good."

04:03:00.700 --> 04:03:02.135
"The right attire
for the right occasion."

04:03:03.836 --> 04:03:05.138
"Kill them, please,"

04:03:06.606 --> 04:03:06.739
he says to the other skeletons

04:03:08.608 --> 04:03:09.909
and continues to float up,

04:03:11.310 --> 04:03:12.278
seemingly resisting some sort of
force that's holding him down.

04:03:13.513 --> 04:03:14.414
Although, he's still
30 feet up in the air.

04:03:15.915 --> 04:03:16.883
That is gonna bring us
to Indra's go.

04:03:18.651 --> 04:03:19.852
I all of my arcane knowledge,
would I know

04:03:20.987 --> 04:03:21.721
if physical or magical attacks
would (BLEEP) this ghost?

04:03:23.222 --> 04:03:24.290
-Roll an arcana check.
-Okay.

04:03:27.894 --> 04:03:28.728
-Arcana or religion, your call.
-What's 17 plus 8?

04:03:29.695 --> 04:03:33.299
-Good enough.
-Okay, cool.

04:03:34.467 --> 04:03:35.501
Magic of all different kinds

04:03:37.737 --> 04:03:38.404
definitely has an impact
on spectral entities.

04:03:43.176 --> 04:03:43.443
You would know that some
physical strikes tend to not be

04:03:46.846 --> 04:03:47.146
as effective,
as well as cold and poison.

04:03:49.282 --> 04:03:49.715
Seeing how they're
an undead spirit.

04:03:52.085 --> 04:03:53.086
Good to know. Thank you.

04:03:57.457 --> 04:03:57.723
I am going to look
at one of the moo moo men

04:04:00.226 --> 04:04:00.560
and cast Ray of Frost at it.

04:04:01.594 --> 04:04:02.095
All righty.

04:04:06.299 --> 04:04:06.599
Which is... Oh, dang.

04:04:07.967 --> 04:04:08.034
Does 15 hit?

04:04:10.636 --> 04:04:10.970
-Fifteen does hit.
-Dope.

04:04:14.073 --> 04:04:17.477
That is 4 D6.

04:04:18.177 --> 04:04:19.445
Laslo, you're on deck.

04:04:21.380 --> 04:04:22.181
-Fifteen points of cold damage.
-Fifteen points of cold damage.

04:04:23.716 --> 04:04:24.250
And the target speed
is also halved.

04:04:24.517 --> 04:04:25.718
-Nice.
-Awesome.

04:04:29.555 --> 04:04:29.822
So one of the hell bovines
is covered in frost and ice...

04:04:30.490 --> 04:04:31.591
crystals across it.

04:04:32.925 --> 04:04:33.793
You can see it's having
to move and push through.

04:04:36.062 --> 04:04:36.562
The joints are now
frozen and locked.

04:04:36.963 --> 04:04:37.964
It's definitely slowed

04:04:40.266 --> 04:04:40.700
and it's taken
a nice little hit to its body.

04:04:41.434 --> 04:04:42.535
Dope. (indistinct)

04:04:44.403 --> 04:04:45.605
Are you remaining there
in the stairway entryway?

04:04:47.440 --> 04:04:48.508
How far am I
from everything right now?

04:04:50.076 --> 04:04:50.676
You're about 20 feet
from the 2 skeletal bovines,

04:04:51.878 --> 04:04:52.645
you are right next to Tauro

04:04:56.082 --> 04:04:57.817
and the ghost is about 35 feet
within the chamber.

04:04:59.852 --> 04:05:00.920
Seeing as Tauro is ranged,
I'm gonna stay where I am.

04:05:02.421 --> 04:05:02.955
-I'm gonna stay put for a bit.
-You got it. Okay.

04:05:04.724 --> 04:05:05.224
Finishing your turn,
Laslo, you're up.

04:05:06.092 --> 04:05:06.425
Tauro, you're on deck.

04:05:07.193 --> 04:05:08.060
The opposite

04:05:09.295 --> 04:05:09.962
minion,

04:05:12.198 --> 04:05:12.665
I'm going to cast Decrepify on.

04:05:14.934 --> 04:05:15.535
Ooh, very nice.

04:05:18.337 --> 04:05:18.871
Curse creature
within 60 feet for 4 rounds.

04:05:19.071 --> 04:05:20.173
Their movement is halved

04:05:22.808 --> 04:05:23.376
and any physical attacks
they use deal half damage.

04:05:25.378 --> 04:05:25.678
It's a DC15, constitution.

04:05:25.978 --> 04:05:26.979
Nice.

04:05:27.813 --> 04:05:28.915
At the end of their turn.

04:05:30.116 --> 04:05:31.117
Correct, so as you reach out,
expend the essence,

04:05:33.653 --> 04:05:34.453
you watch as the shadows
pierce inside of it

04:05:35.121 --> 04:05:36.255
and almost pull it
to the ground.

04:05:39.392 --> 04:05:40.359
These tendrils of black and grey
are keeping it roped

04:05:42.695 --> 04:05:43.429
and its bone structure
is fighting against it.

04:05:45.498 --> 04:05:45.565
Elements of it
turning to dust by the contact.

04:05:47.667 --> 04:05:47.967
Both of these are
pretty hindered at the moment.

04:05:48.501 --> 04:05:49.068
Well done.

04:05:51.804 --> 04:05:52.205
I'm going to send
Spell Slots after that guy.

04:05:53.539 --> 04:05:53.940
Go Spell Slots!

04:05:55.007 --> 04:05:56.042
This is gonna...

04:05:57.677 --> 04:05:59.312
...as he's running up to him.

04:06:00.546 --> 04:06:00.813
Ten?

04:06:02.181 --> 04:06:02.381
Ten does not hit.

04:06:03.916 --> 04:06:05.451
It's like a soft pillow.

04:06:07.987 --> 04:06:08.888
More of
a gentle caress of the face.

04:06:10.723 --> 04:06:11.691
That's the end of my turn.

04:06:12.491 --> 04:06:13.159
Finishing Laslo's turn,
Tauro, you're up.

04:06:14.827 --> 04:06:15.528
Your friends or your enemies?
Your choice.

04:06:18.097 --> 04:06:19.131
Do I get to try and save from
this at the top of my turn?

04:06:20.399 --> 04:06:21.834
-At the end of your turn.
-At the end of my turn.

04:06:23.102 --> 04:06:23.869
Okay.

04:06:27.773 --> 04:06:28.374
Who do I see
in my nearest periphery?

04:06:28.641 --> 04:06:29.775
You're right next to Indra.

04:06:31.244 --> 04:06:31.510
You are right next to
all your friends, essentially.

04:06:34.280 --> 04:06:34.947
You guys are
still standing in the stairway.

04:06:35.748 --> 04:06:36.682
You have the pick of the litter.

04:06:38.818 --> 04:06:39.018
Five, 10, 15, 20.
I'm gonna roll to see.

04:06:42.989 --> 04:06:43.189
I'm gonna attack Mordred.

04:06:44.457 --> 04:06:44.991
Go for it.

04:06:49.595 --> 04:06:49.729
As you're bearing down,
getting ready to charge in.

04:06:50.263 --> 04:06:52.932
"Wait, what are you..."

04:06:54.634 --> 04:06:56.502
"Moo (BLEEP)."

04:06:58.938 --> 04:06:59.505
I'm going to do Hungering Arrow.

04:07:00.406 --> 04:07:04.277
"I can't get out the way!"

04:07:06.679 --> 04:07:07.480
Do I hit? I rolled low.

04:07:08.681 --> 04:07:09.215
That's a GIF
if I've ever heard one.

04:07:11.984 --> 04:07:12.718
-Moo, (BLEEP).
-Moo, (BLEEP).

04:07:14.587 --> 04:07:14.854
Can't get out the way.

04:07:18.991 --> 04:07:20.559
Okay, the first one is a 10 to
hit, which I don't think hits.

04:07:21.661 --> 04:07:23.596
The next one is a 15.

04:07:24.096 --> 04:07:25.031
Miss?

04:07:25.398 --> 04:07:25.898
-Both impact on the shield.
-Both miss.

04:07:27.500 --> 04:07:28.434
I rolled a 9 and a 3.

04:07:29.268 --> 04:07:29.835
Now go ahead
and roll a wisdom saving throw.

04:07:32.872 --> 04:07:33.272
No, wait, 8 plus 9 is 17.

04:07:33.973 --> 04:07:35.107
-No.
-Right?

04:07:37.543 --> 04:07:38.311
Am I doing this right?
Yes I am, so 17. But still no.

04:07:39.612 --> 04:07:39.879
-Okay, both miss.
-All right.

04:07:41.847 --> 04:07:44.116
"Whoa! Tauro!"

04:07:45.418 --> 04:07:48.854
Oh, no.

04:07:50.189 --> 04:07:51.624
Things...

04:07:53.492 --> 04:07:55.394
You're a different Tauro.

04:07:58.297 --> 04:07:58.497
I will do my bonus action,

04:08:03.035 --> 04:08:03.102
to spend discipline
to do Shadow Power.

04:08:06.405 --> 04:08:07.406
So, every time I attack,
I heal myself.

04:08:10.209 --> 04:08:11.243
You watch now as
the blue glows in Tauro's eyes.

04:08:13.279 --> 04:08:14.246
These black, shadow wings appear
from the back,

04:08:15.281 --> 04:08:16.282
these black tendrils
in the shape of wings

04:08:18.818 --> 04:08:19.618
and this aura
of black energy surrounds her.

04:08:22.254 --> 04:08:22.888
Pouring out from under the mask
and the helm.

04:08:23.289 --> 04:08:24.457
That finishes your go, Tauro.

04:08:26.158 --> 04:08:26.459
Go ahead and make a wisdom
saving throw for me, please.

04:08:27.493 --> 04:08:28.494
(MUMBLING)

04:08:29.995 --> 04:08:30.129
-You can do it. Come on.
-All right. Come on.

04:08:31.430 --> 04:08:31.931
Big money.

04:08:33.232 --> 04:08:33.499
Big money?

04:08:35.101 --> 04:08:35.468
Oh my God, no. Four.

04:08:36.502 --> 04:08:36.802
I rolled a 3.

04:08:38.170 --> 04:08:38.371
Hell yes.

04:08:39.538 --> 04:08:40.072
No!

04:08:41.640 --> 04:08:42.541
That was small money.

04:08:45.611 --> 04:08:46.245
-Small money, 4 dollars.
-Four dollars?

04:08:47.046 --> 04:08:47.980
Oh no!

04:08:49.081 --> 04:08:49.749
How are you supposed
to buy chicken nuggets?

04:08:51.150 --> 04:08:53.519
Are there any pots in this room?

04:08:56.689 --> 04:08:57.223
Just go over
and kick some pots angrily.

04:08:57.757 --> 04:08:57.957
Finishing Tauro's turn,

04:08:59.792 --> 04:09:01.060
the two hell bovine skeletons
begin to lurch forward

04:09:03.062 --> 04:09:03.696
They're both slowed and can only
get to the very front line,

04:09:04.964 --> 04:09:05.364
which means their only target

04:09:07.733 --> 04:09:08.601
is gonna be you at the moment,
since you're the one in front.

04:09:09.368 --> 04:09:10.603
By slowing them down,

04:09:12.371 --> 04:09:12.938
they can't get to any of the
meatier pieces, unfortunately.

04:09:14.173 --> 04:09:16.409
Both of them swing towards you.

04:09:18.878 --> 04:09:19.245
They both have
the large glaives.

04:09:20.079 --> 04:09:20.379
One of them...

04:09:21.046 --> 04:09:21.514
To glaive.

04:09:23.149 --> 04:09:23.949
That's a 24 to hit.

04:09:25.017 --> 04:09:25.351
-That does kind of hit.
-Indeed.

04:09:26.619 --> 04:09:27.386
You take...

04:09:30.956 --> 04:09:31.323
13 points of physical damage
from the one slowed by you.

04:09:32.224 --> 04:09:32.425
The other one,

04:09:35.327 --> 04:09:35.761
that's gonna be a 19 to hit.

04:09:36.595 --> 04:09:37.530
-Hits.
-Hits again.

04:09:38.664 --> 04:09:39.031
This one, however,
is Decrepified by you.

04:09:41.534 --> 04:09:42.601
Which means you would take 11,

04:09:44.069 --> 04:09:44.170
reduced to 5 points
of physical damage from him.

04:09:48.441 --> 04:09:48.707
They both also are jailers,
so you watch as...

04:09:51.510 --> 04:09:51.777
Suddenly, I need you
to make a wisdom saving throw.

04:09:51.844 --> 04:09:53.446
Jailers?

04:09:54.547 --> 04:09:54.847
And you make
a wisdom saving throw.

04:09:55.815 --> 04:09:56.382
Real low.

04:09:58.484 --> 04:09:59.385
That is a 5.

04:10:01.020 --> 04:10:01.520
Your movement is reduced to 0
until the end of the next turn.

04:10:02.154 --> 04:10:02.822
I don't need movement.

04:10:03.422 --> 04:10:04.290
-Crit fail.
-Crit fail?

04:10:04.557 --> 04:10:05.825
Your movement
is also reduced to 0.

04:10:07.793 --> 04:10:08.761
You're both locked into place
by some strange, arcane power

04:10:09.495 --> 04:10:09.728
and your feet
cannot move off the ground.

04:10:10.763 --> 04:10:11.330
Oh no.

04:10:15.201 --> 04:10:15.334
That finishes their turn. That
brings us to Mordred and Remy.

04:10:16.669 --> 04:10:17.670
As a bonus action,

04:10:19.939 --> 04:10:20.473
I will recite
more scripture from the church

04:10:21.574 --> 04:10:21.807
and use Laws of Justice

04:10:24.643 --> 04:10:25.678
to grant myself
and allies within 30 feet

04:10:27.780 --> 04:10:28.781
resistance to cold,
fire and lightning damage.

04:10:30.015 --> 04:10:30.850
And I lose my action

04:10:33.018 --> 04:10:33.452
to consecrate
the ground we stand on.

04:10:36.121 --> 04:10:36.222
For the next 4 rounds,
we will heal.

04:10:41.727 --> 04:10:42.328
At the start of our turns,
we get back 1 D6 plus 2.

04:10:43.562 --> 04:10:43.829
At the start of your turns.

04:10:44.463 --> 04:10:44.630
You've got it.

04:10:47.299 --> 04:10:49.935
"Have pity,
they are all mooman beings."

04:10:51.804 --> 04:10:52.471
-Oh, no.
-How long did you have that?

04:10:54.573 --> 04:10:56.342
-How long?
-Five minutes.

04:10:57.710 --> 04:10:58.978
Just waiting for the right time.

04:11:00.079 --> 04:11:01.180
Finishing your go, Mordred, and
unable to move from your space,

04:11:02.548 --> 04:11:03.415
you slam your shield
into the ground and you watch

04:11:05.618 --> 04:11:05.751
as this arcane circle
apparates out

04:11:07.319 --> 04:11:08.254
in a space around Mordred.

04:11:09.989 --> 04:11:11.156
As you does,
you feel the soft, divine energy

04:11:13.792 --> 04:11:14.059
beginning to close any wounds
as they begin to arrive.

04:11:15.294 --> 04:11:15.628
Remy, what are you doing?

04:11:17.796 --> 04:11:18.397
Well first,
I'm gonna heal 3 points.

04:11:19.431 --> 04:11:21.233
-Yeah.
-There you go.

04:11:23.335 --> 04:11:23.736
Then, I'm gonna

04:11:27.373 --> 04:11:27.940
run up behind the bovine

04:11:29.008 --> 04:11:29.975
that's attacking Mordred.

04:11:32.411 --> 04:11:32.845
Actually, Mordred's probably got
it handled, I'm gonna run up

04:11:33.646 --> 04:11:34.713
behind Laslo.

04:11:36.815 --> 04:11:37.416
You just seem
a little bit smaller.

04:11:39.485 --> 04:11:40.152
Both of you are actually
pretty hardcore, aren't you?

04:11:40.719 --> 04:11:41.587
I'm pretty (BLEEP) up, actually.

04:11:43.956 --> 04:11:44.123
I'm gonna run up behind you,
the one attacking him.

04:11:45.724 --> 04:11:46.525
It's not gonna kill him anyway.

04:11:47.793 --> 04:11:48.661
And I'm gonna,
as I'm running up,

04:11:50.729 --> 04:11:51.063
turn into my crocodile form.

04:11:51.463 --> 04:11:52.231
You got it.

04:11:54.967 --> 04:12:00.172
-And I'm gonna Maul.
-Go for it. Maul.

04:12:01.473 --> 04:12:02.374
Whoa, that was aggressive.

04:12:06.278 --> 04:12:06.745
-Plus 9, so 18.
-Eighteen does hit.

04:12:07.112 --> 04:12:12.651
All right.

04:12:15.621 --> 04:12:15.821
-Eleven points.
-Eleven points of damage.

04:12:17.489 --> 04:12:17.690
As you reach out, transforming,

04:12:20.025 --> 04:12:20.759
You reach over with your claws
and bite towards him.

04:12:21.226 --> 04:12:22.294
You take a chunk
of its bone off.

04:12:23.162 --> 04:12:23.996
You can see part of the ribs
broken on the inside

04:12:24.730 --> 04:12:27.800
and still holding
itself together.

04:12:28.367 --> 04:12:29.168
Well done.

04:12:29.435 --> 04:12:30.235
-Does that finish your go?
-Yeah.

04:12:32.438 --> 04:12:33.038
All righty.
That now brings us to...

04:12:34.506 --> 04:12:35.374
At the top of the ramp,
there's Wart (indistinct).

04:12:37.042 --> 04:12:37.309
Wart is now shouting out
into the field.

04:12:39.345 --> 04:12:39.979
"Gillian, I'm trying,

04:12:41.280 --> 04:12:42.781
but they're getting in my way.

04:12:43.349 --> 04:12:43.916
I'll stop you,

04:12:45.618 --> 04:12:46.452
for her sake."

04:12:47.586 --> 04:12:48.587
As he raises his hands
into the sky,

04:12:50.122 --> 04:12:50.589
the wind whips up
and the ghoul begins to...

04:12:51.290 --> 04:12:51.724
pick up in the wind,

04:12:53.092 --> 04:12:53.459
faster and faster.

04:12:58.664 --> 04:12:59.298
Suddenly, you're all being
pelted by a storm of gold coins.

04:13:00.199 --> 04:13:01.133
I need everybody in the space

04:13:02.935 --> 04:13:03.902
to go ahead and make
a dexterity saving throw

04:13:05.804 --> 04:13:06.639
against his affluent
poltergeist stability.

04:13:07.373 --> 04:13:08.207
What we love most
is betraying us.

04:13:09.274 --> 04:13:09.942
-Is that including me?
-Including you.

04:13:12.244 --> 04:13:12.444
And including the bovines.
It's everything.

04:13:13.479 --> 04:13:15.514
No!

04:13:15.981 --> 04:13:16.515
I got 8 doubled.

04:13:18.417 --> 04:13:19.585
Nineteen.

04:13:21.420 --> 04:13:22.187
Natural 20.

04:13:23.722 --> 04:13:24.023
-Nice!
-Ooh!

04:13:25.724 --> 04:13:26.291
Natural 6.

04:13:27.192 --> 04:13:27.826
Twenty-three.

04:13:29.328 --> 04:13:30.863
Is this how the pots get full?

04:13:31.830 --> 04:13:32.731
We've figured it out.

04:13:33.432 --> 04:13:34.366
-Success.
-We're witnessing a phenomenon.

04:13:36.335 --> 04:13:36.802
You take what
would have been 23 points

04:13:38.437 --> 04:13:38.937
of physical damage.

04:13:41.106 --> 04:13:41.206
Instead, you take 11.

04:13:42.708 --> 04:13:42.908
-Sheebus!
-What did you roll?

04:13:43.909 --> 04:13:44.743
Natural 20 for 22.

04:13:45.744 --> 04:13:45.944
Eleven points
of physical damage.

04:13:46.211 --> 04:13:47.146
Six.

04:13:48.447 --> 04:13:49.014
Twenty-three points
of physical damage.

04:13:49.915 --> 04:13:50.382
-Wart is down.
-Oh no!

04:13:51.316 --> 04:13:51.984
S***!

04:13:53.686 --> 04:13:54.019
Is the ground still consecrated?

04:13:55.287 --> 04:13:55.821
"Avenge me!"

04:13:56.422 --> 04:13:56.889
The consecration stays.

04:13:57.456 --> 04:13:57.956
Oh, thank goodness.

04:13:58.290 --> 04:13:58.757
Wait, does Mordred...?

04:13:59.591 --> 04:14:00.592
He'll heal as he...?

04:14:01.927 --> 04:14:02.394
-At the top of--
-If it's his turn, he will.

04:14:03.595 --> 04:14:04.496
-Uh-oh!
-Oh no!

04:14:05.597 --> 04:14:06.432
Mess with the bull,
you get the horns.

04:14:07.199 --> 04:14:07.800
Do I have to roll
for Spell Slots?

04:14:09.301 --> 04:14:10.769
-Dab!
-Yes.

04:14:11.904 --> 04:14:12.371
-Three.
-Up!

04:14:13.072 --> 04:14:13.472
Up and away from me.

04:14:15.741 --> 04:14:17.009
You take eleven points
of damage.

04:14:19.411 --> 04:14:20.679
As you're shielding, you look
past the storm of gold coins.

04:14:22.781 --> 04:14:23.615
You look out and see Spell Slots
turns around to you with...

04:14:25.117 --> 04:14:25.484
If a skeleton
could make a sad face...

04:14:26.518 --> 04:14:27.219
It reaches...

04:14:30.756 --> 04:14:31.256
In that moment,
Laslo realizes...

04:14:33.559 --> 04:14:35.194
"You've been my son
this entire time."

04:14:36.895 --> 04:14:37.396
# Only time

04:14:39.732 --> 04:14:40.199
The jaw gets torn off.

04:14:40.466 --> 04:14:41.400
The arm is torn off.

04:14:42.000 --> 04:14:42.568
Eventually,
the skeleton is pulled apart

04:14:43.202 --> 04:14:43.969
by the pelting gold coins.

04:14:45.237 --> 04:14:45.804
Gone.

04:14:46.105 --> 04:14:46.872
Gone.

04:14:48.140 --> 04:14:51.610
Gone.

04:14:53.378 --> 04:14:54.279
-Twenty-three total.
-Twenty-three.

04:14:54.747 --> 04:14:55.380
You take 11 points
of physical damage.

04:14:56.048 --> 04:14:56.115
And make another saving throw.

04:14:58.350 --> 04:14:59.184
-And make another saving throw.
-Correct.

04:15:00.853 --> 04:15:01.420
Okay.
That will bring it up to 27.

04:15:03.455 --> 04:15:03.722
Just a wisdom saving throw?

04:15:04.490 --> 04:15:05.591
Wisdom saving throw, yeah.

04:15:07.526 --> 04:15:08.260
-Roll to 3 again.
-Nope. Still in (indistinct).

04:15:09.595 --> 04:15:09.795
-Alright, cool.
-Oh my God.

04:15:10.562 --> 04:15:11.630
That finishes Wart's turn.

04:15:13.465 --> 04:15:14.066
You can see now that
there's this angst in his face,

04:15:15.300 --> 04:15:16.368
this deep sadness and anger,

04:15:18.470 --> 04:15:19.438
and just, right now,
he's conflicted in this moment.

04:15:20.572 --> 04:15:21.740
That finishes his turn.
Indra, you're up.

04:15:22.307 --> 04:15:23.041
Laslo, you're on deck.

04:15:27.279 --> 04:15:27.780
-So, back to the 15 feet thing?
-Yeah.

04:15:29.548 --> 04:15:29.748
The bovines?

04:15:32.584 --> 04:15:33.051
They are within 15 feet
of each other?

04:15:33.318 --> 04:15:34.419
Next to each other?

04:15:35.454 --> 04:15:35.687
They are. They both swarmed
towards Mordred, yes.

04:15:36.155 --> 04:15:36.955
Right.

04:15:37.723 --> 04:15:38.457
-Is it possible...?
-It might...

04:15:40.092 --> 04:15:40.359
There's a chance
you could hit...

04:15:41.326 --> 04:15:41.527
Remy, but...

04:15:43.028 --> 04:15:43.929
if you wanna risk it...

04:15:44.930 --> 04:15:45.397
I'm behind.

04:15:46.131 --> 04:15:46.265
You're behind, okay.

04:15:48.433 --> 04:15:48.634
Then I resend that.

04:15:50.135 --> 04:15:50.435
Or go for it. Your call.

04:15:51.804 --> 04:15:52.171
You know...

04:15:53.372 --> 04:15:53.505
Nah.

04:15:54.873 --> 04:15:55.941
(indistinct) up or down.

04:15:58.544 --> 04:15:59.278
Oh! You said one...
I get a D6 plus... How much?

04:16:00.245 --> 04:16:00.546
-Plus 2.
-Plus 2. All right.

04:16:02.181 --> 04:16:03.048
Oh. Oh, 6!

04:16:07.019 --> 04:16:07.286
And I'm going to Ray of Frost
at the same one.

04:16:09.254 --> 04:16:10.622
Okay. Go ahead and roll again.

04:16:11.623 --> 04:16:12.524
Sixteen plus... Twenty-six?

04:16:12.925 --> 04:16:13.492
-Did that hit him?
-It definitely hit.

04:16:15.427 --> 04:16:16.562
Wonderful. Now it's 5 D6.

04:16:17.596 --> 04:16:17.863
The damage is increasing
because your focusing the beam.

04:16:18.530 --> 04:16:18.931
Exactly.

04:16:20.365 --> 04:16:20.666
That's 5, yeah.

04:16:21.033 --> 04:16:21.733
That's 6.

04:16:25.604 --> 04:16:26.071
Five, five at sixteen, plus six.

04:16:28.740 --> 04:16:28.874
-That's twenty-two.
-Twenty-two. Twenty-four.

04:16:31.043 --> 04:16:31.510
Twenty-four points of Chilly.

04:16:32.077 --> 04:16:33.045
With that,

04:16:33.879 --> 04:16:34.847
the first move
is him focusing his beam on you.

04:16:38.083 --> 04:16:38.183
You're pushing
and focusing this intense...

04:16:41.019 --> 04:16:42.120
arcane blast
of frozen death on to it.

04:16:44.256 --> 04:16:45.457
As it does, the ice builds up,
builds up around it,

04:16:46.992 --> 04:16:47.626
and it's pushing forward and
pulling its glaive into the air.

04:16:49.494 --> 04:16:49.995
It's about to bring it down...

04:16:50.829 --> 04:16:51.129
It freezes solid.

04:16:53.232 --> 04:16:53.498
As the coins hit it...

04:16:56.668 --> 04:16:57.236
it breaks away into thousands
of tiny, frozen bone fragments.

04:16:58.804 --> 04:16:59.638
-Yeah!
-Dope, dope!

04:17:00.973 --> 04:17:01.607
Laslo, you're up.

04:17:03.942 --> 04:17:04.276
Do I have a clean line of...?

04:17:07.512 --> 04:17:08.280
A clean line
to hit that other bovine?

04:17:09.715 --> 04:17:10.515
-With a bit of movement, yes.
-Okay.

04:17:12.684 --> 04:17:13.118
-Can I take that movement?
-Sure.

04:17:13.385 --> 04:17:14.486
Shift to the side

04:17:16.855 --> 04:17:18.023
and you now can see
it's between Mordred and Remy.

04:17:20.425 --> 04:17:20.659
So, you're now hitting them
from a flailing position.

04:17:23.495 --> 04:17:24.162
Great. I'm gonna
undo my coat real quick.

04:17:27.065 --> 04:17:27.532
And Laslo reveals his rib cage.

04:17:28.734 --> 04:17:29.568
It starts coming out

04:17:31.837 --> 04:17:32.271
and twisting
into a very long spear

04:17:33.572 --> 04:17:34.373
right at this guy.

04:17:35.307 --> 04:17:36.208
-All right.
-I'm casting Bone Spear.

04:17:37.442 --> 04:17:37.910
You got it.
Go ahead and... for that.

04:17:39.678 --> 04:17:40.312
He has... the CC14.

04:17:41.380 --> 04:17:41.647
That's right. Dexterity save.

04:17:42.514 --> 04:17:42.881
No, natural 6.

04:17:43.548 --> 04:17:44.149
He's not safe.

04:17:45.651 --> 04:17:46.251
Eleven, eleven. Twenty-two.

04:17:46.718 --> 04:17:47.185
Twenty-two points of damage?

04:17:48.587 --> 04:17:48.854
-Yeah.
-Damn.

04:17:50.789 --> 04:17:51.623
That's just enough, actually.

04:17:53.358 --> 04:17:53.558
As you come out, (indistinct)...

04:17:56.762 --> 04:17:57.596
the ribs come out and form
this spiraling drill, almost.

04:17:58.697 --> 04:17:59.865
Magical spears blast
into the side.

04:18:01.867 --> 04:18:02.501
You watch as it shatters
the midsection of the pelvis.

04:18:02.868 --> 04:18:03.769
His spinal column is just gone

04:18:04.836 --> 04:18:05.837
and the rest of it
is standing there...

04:18:08.640 --> 04:18:09.374
hits the ground and falls apart
into pieces of bone.

04:18:12.311 --> 04:18:12.411
Yeah, and as it goes down,

04:18:13.645 --> 04:18:14.179
under his breath, he goes...

04:18:15.781 --> 04:18:18.150
"You killed Spell Slots!"

04:18:20.385 --> 04:18:23.021
That's how
origin stories start, guys.

04:18:26.625 --> 04:18:27.225
Awesome. Finishing your turn.
Tauro, you're up.

04:18:29.027 --> 04:18:29.628
So, okay...

04:18:31.096 --> 04:18:31.296
Five, two, fifty, twenty.
I'll do it again.

04:18:32.597 --> 04:18:32.864
See how I hit.

04:18:33.932 --> 04:18:34.700
I have natural 20.

04:18:37.302 --> 04:18:37.536
-What? Oh, now?
-Who to pick?

04:18:37.736 --> 04:18:37.936
So...

04:18:40.005 --> 04:18:40.839
How much hatred have you got?

04:18:42.574 --> 04:18:42.708
-Ten hatred.
-Okay.

04:18:44.376 --> 04:18:45.043
So, I'm gonna...

04:18:47.446 --> 04:18:49.581
Hungering Arrow again.

04:18:51.984 --> 04:18:52.417
Good hit. Great rolls.

04:18:53.685 --> 04:18:54.920
Just great rolls.

04:18:56.888 --> 04:18:57.222
-Nineteen for the first one.
-That hits.

04:18:59.358 --> 04:18:59.658
I'll go ahead and do damage.

04:19:01.960 --> 04:19:02.861
Great roll. 10 damage.

04:19:07.532 --> 04:19:07.899
-Okay.
-And then 23 for the second one.

04:19:09.067 --> 04:19:10.369
-That hits.
-That looks like it hit.

04:19:11.837 --> 04:19:13.372
-Nine damage.
-Okay.

04:19:14.506 --> 04:19:15.007
That's cool.

04:19:15.207 --> 04:19:16.308
And I'm gonna spend--

04:19:16.942 --> 04:19:17.542
We'll still be friends
if you spend this. That's fine.

04:19:20.379 --> 04:19:21.313
I'm gonna spend 6 hatred...

04:19:24.649 --> 04:19:24.950
to toss out
a spike trap in backup.

04:19:25.717 --> 04:19:27.019
All right.

04:19:28.620 --> 04:19:29.421
After you fire twice into Laslo,
suddenly, you're like, "Argh!"

04:19:30.222 --> 04:19:31.490
You don't even see it
in the moment,

04:19:33.525 --> 04:19:34.159
but you slip and throw a little
trap right underneath Laslo

04:19:34.926 --> 04:19:35.394
that he does not even notice.

04:19:35.894 --> 04:19:36.495
-Okay.
-Oh...

04:19:36.795 --> 04:19:37.562
-So sad.
-And I'll hold.

04:19:39.064 --> 04:19:39.731
All right.
That finishes your turn.

04:19:40.232 --> 04:19:41.466
Both hell bovines are destroyed.

04:19:43.368 --> 04:19:44.169
-Mordred and Remy, you're up.
-Do I get to roll? I do, right?

04:19:44.436 --> 04:19:45.037
-To see if I save?
-You do, yes.

04:19:46.571 --> 04:19:47.072
-Come on!
-Come on!

04:19:48.373 --> 04:19:48.740
-Big money!
-Okay!

04:19:49.508 --> 04:19:50.375
There's a 15,

04:19:51.276 --> 04:19:52.210
plus my wizard's save
for 16 total.

04:19:54.346 --> 04:19:54.813
You break free
of the influence of Wart.

04:19:55.080 --> 04:19:56.281
So, I'm about to...

04:19:59.751 --> 04:20:00.218
I back up and I'm about to hit
the detonator on the trap.

04:20:00.819 --> 04:20:03.555
And I'm gonna go...

04:20:04.089 --> 04:20:05.057
Perfect.

04:20:06.091 --> 04:20:06.691
That finishes your go.
What are you guys doing?

04:20:08.860 --> 04:20:09.394
Well, I rolled a 6 on a D6,

04:20:10.362 --> 04:20:11.630
so I get 18 points back.

04:20:13.398 --> 04:20:14.199
Indeed. So, you heal, come to
consciousness and look around.

04:20:15.801 --> 04:20:16.802
Who...

04:20:17.436 --> 04:20:18.537
The wind is still
whipping coins around you

04:20:20.138 --> 04:20:20.705
and you can barely see
above the glowing spectral form

04:20:21.506 --> 04:20:22.707
of this infuriated child.

04:20:24.376 --> 04:20:25.243
"There's nothing I can do
to get up there, so I just..."

04:20:27.979 --> 04:20:28.680
Am I still held in place
from the...?

04:20:30.715 --> 04:20:31.516
-Bovines? Yeah.
-The bovines are dead.

04:20:32.250 --> 04:20:33.318
-So, I can move, right?
-Indeed.

04:20:34.186 --> 04:20:34.586
Can I use half my movement
to return to standing?

04:20:35.654 --> 04:20:36.755
You get back up.

04:20:39.591 --> 04:20:40.158
Then I will continue
to recite the Laws of Justice

04:20:40.358 --> 04:20:41.026
to keep up our resistance,

04:20:42.127 --> 04:20:42.794
because it's about all I can do.

04:20:44.729 --> 04:20:45.530
Maybe Gillian's under the gold.

04:20:47.999 --> 04:20:53.305
He keeps...
He keeps pointing down.

04:20:54.406 --> 04:21:02.214
Make a history check for me.

04:21:03.815 --> 04:21:08.487
-Ten.
-Ten?

04:21:10.755 --> 04:21:11.556
It's hard to place, but you've
come across a Gillian before.

04:21:12.958 --> 04:21:15.093
You can't quite pinpoint it,
though.

04:21:16.128 --> 04:21:16.795
She did sound familiar.

04:21:17.963 --> 04:21:18.830
Gillian Anderson of the X-Files.

04:21:20.365 --> 04:21:21.266
-That's your turn?
-That's it, yeah.

04:21:21.867 --> 04:21:22.134
All righty.
What are you doing, Remy?

04:21:24.369 --> 04:21:24.703
The only thing I can try to do

04:21:25.937 --> 04:21:26.805
is Windshear.

04:21:28.673 --> 04:21:28.940
So, I'm gonna
hold up my arm again.

04:21:32.544 --> 04:21:32.911
A Spectral Blade is gonna
shoot out towards the child.

04:21:34.079 --> 04:21:38.750
You've got it.

04:21:41.419 --> 04:21:41.786
That's a 27 to hit.

04:21:42.821 --> 04:21:44.422
That does hit.

04:21:45.357 --> 04:21:45.991
Three D8s.

04:21:47.058 --> 04:21:50.362
Oh, s****.

04:21:54.599 --> 04:21:55.934
-Seventeen... points.
-Seventeen points. Nice.

04:21:57.002 --> 04:21:58.236
So, it does strike him.

04:22:00.805 --> 04:22:01.740
But the Windshear doesn't impact
as heavily as you'd hope.

04:22:02.240 --> 04:22:02.841
The spectral form
is seemingly resistant

04:22:04.709 --> 04:22:05.677
to a lot of physical damage.

04:22:06.077 --> 04:22:06.511
Yeah, I can only
do physical damage, guys.

04:22:07.145 --> 04:22:08.046
Sorry about that.

04:22:10.282 --> 04:22:11.216
So, he is still
sitting strong, angry,

04:22:11.816 --> 04:22:11.883
and the storm
is still whipping around.

04:22:13.084 --> 04:22:13.418
That finishes your turn.

04:22:14.686 --> 04:22:16.621
I'm gonna...

04:22:17.355 --> 04:22:18.523
Go with me on this.

04:22:20.792 --> 04:22:21.026
I'm gonna send my swarm
of insects as a bonus action.

04:22:21.293 --> 04:22:22.394
Okay.

04:22:24.129 --> 04:22:24.429
But I'm gonna swarm them down
and under the gold.

04:22:26.331 --> 04:22:26.565
-Okay.
-Scurrying for something...

04:22:27.232 --> 04:22:27.732
Okay.

04:22:28.833 --> 04:22:29.968
We'll come to you
next round, then.

04:22:31.169 --> 04:22:32.237
Coming to the top of the round,
it's Wart's turn again.

04:22:33.238 --> 04:22:34.372
He's gonna continue
towards the center in a frenzy.

04:22:35.707 --> 04:22:36.107
Everyone, once again,
make a dexterity saving throw.

04:22:37.609 --> 04:22:38.243
-Go down--
-Oh, boy!

04:22:39.511 --> 04:22:40.212
I'm gonna go back down again.

04:22:41.012 --> 04:22:41.780
-Hm-hmm.
-Ooh, that's bad.

04:22:44.316 --> 04:22:44.583
Oh, actually, it might be okay.

04:22:45.183 --> 04:22:45.684
Fifteen.

04:22:47.419 --> 04:22:47.819
Nineteen points
of physical damage.

04:22:48.019 --> 04:22:48.420
Is that halved?

04:22:49.321 --> 04:22:49.888
No, she failed.

04:22:52.023 --> 04:22:52.824
-Ooh! Fails.
-Okay.

04:22:54.159 --> 04:22:55.026
I failed.

04:22:55.427 --> 04:22:55.727
Nineteen points
of physical damage.

04:22:56.461 --> 04:22:56.795
Nineteen.

04:22:57.829 --> 04:22:58.330
You take...

04:22:59.664 --> 04:23:00.465
nine points of physical damage.

04:23:02.200 --> 04:23:02.534
-Mordred is down.
-Oh, Mordred!

04:23:02.801 --> 04:23:03.668
Twenty-one.

04:23:04.569 --> 04:23:05.103
Take nine points
of physical damage.

04:23:06.304 --> 04:23:07.239
I failed. Fifteen, so...

04:23:07.772 --> 04:23:10.575
Take nineteen points
of physical damage.

04:23:12.344 --> 04:23:12.611
You're getting...

04:23:14.112 --> 04:23:14.779
This is turning very badly.

04:23:17.082 --> 04:23:18.350
You're getting the sense that...

04:23:21.853 --> 04:23:22.520
on a physical feature,
combat-on-combat scenario,

04:23:23.121 --> 04:23:24.055
you're at a severe disadvantage,

04:23:24.856 --> 04:23:25.957
and this is already
turning against you.

04:23:26.958 --> 04:23:28.360
That brings us to Indra.

04:23:30.195 --> 04:23:30.495
So, I'm gonna start...

04:23:33.164 --> 04:23:33.365
opening a tear in the universe.

04:23:34.199 --> 04:23:34.699
Okay.

04:23:38.803 --> 04:23:38.903
"But before I destroy
all of your treasures and gold,

04:23:40.939 --> 04:23:41.306
because I can and I will...

04:23:43.241 --> 04:23:46.011
what do you want us to do?"

04:23:47.178 --> 04:23:48.680
Make a persuasion check.

04:23:50.382 --> 04:23:50.649
Oh, I'm good at that!

04:23:51.816 --> 04:23:52.217
Come on, come on!

04:23:53.251 --> 04:23:54.786
Come on, Indra!

04:23:55.153 --> 04:23:56.655
Thirteen.

04:23:57.789 --> 04:23:57.989
Yeah.

04:24:01.293 --> 04:24:02.227
He's, at this point,
just in this rage

04:24:02.927 --> 04:24:05.096
and glances over towards you
and goes...

04:24:09.100 --> 04:24:09.668
"You have already passed
the point of being helpful

04:24:11.236 --> 04:24:11.503
by destroying my friends."

04:24:13.705 --> 04:24:14.406
"What if
we get you more friends?"

04:24:16.975 --> 04:24:17.175
"Just bring me gold for her.

04:24:18.743 --> 04:24:19.110
All you can find.

04:24:20.378 --> 04:24:20.512
She...

04:24:22.480 --> 04:24:23.715
is too good for all of you!"

04:24:26.084 --> 04:24:26.584
"Who's 'she'? We can't help you
if you don't tell us things."

04:24:28.053 --> 04:24:28.620
"Gillian, obviously."

04:24:30.255 --> 04:24:30.755
You heard Gillian earlier.

04:24:31.690 --> 04:24:32.424
"And who is Gillian?"

04:24:33.158 --> 04:24:34.492
-Make a history check.
-Nah.

04:24:35.794 --> 04:24:36.728
Come on.

04:24:38.263 --> 04:24:38.530
-Fifteen.
-Fifteen?

04:24:41.566 --> 04:24:41.933
You did come across a Gillian
in Caldeum once.

04:24:43.201 --> 04:24:43.601
She...

04:24:44.869 --> 04:24:45.403
was raising a small child.

04:24:49.607 --> 04:24:52.344
-This is a few years ago.
-Oh, no. Mommy.

04:24:53.878 --> 04:24:53.978
She was raising a small child.

04:24:57.782 --> 04:24:59.751
The tear won't close,
but Indra lowers her staff.

04:25:00.285 --> 04:25:01.619
"Is that your mom?"

04:25:02.087 --> 04:25:02.420
"No!

04:25:03.822 --> 04:25:05.256
Not my mom!"

04:25:07.392 --> 04:25:08.460
"Sorry for assuming!"

04:25:09.260 --> 04:25:09.527
That ends your turn.
He is not happy about that.

04:25:10.795 --> 04:25:11.930
Oh, God!

04:25:13.565 --> 04:25:14.566
What are you doing, Laslo?

04:25:15.467 --> 04:25:16.134
How far up is he?

04:25:17.569 --> 04:25:17.769
About 30 feet from you. 35 feet.

04:25:18.036 --> 04:25:18.937
Oh!

04:25:20.939 --> 04:25:21.206
-Too far.
-Move to get closer if you want.

04:25:22.374 --> 04:25:22.941
Even...

04:25:26.678 --> 04:25:27.178
Yeah, if he's floating, I want
to cast Death Nova again...

04:25:30.648 --> 04:25:31.316
the poison,
but it's 20 feet from me?

04:25:31.583 --> 04:25:32.550
Yeah, it's not gonna reach him.

04:25:34.586 --> 04:25:34.853
If my hair's really high,
will it hook...?

04:25:37.489 --> 04:25:38.823
-Not quite.
-Jump up in the air.

04:25:40.625 --> 04:25:42.560
Yeah, then...

04:25:44.062 --> 04:25:44.262
I'm gonna try to...

04:25:46.564 --> 04:25:47.098
There's nothing I can do.
This is all physical.

04:25:47.365 --> 04:25:47.832
I might Bone Spear him.

04:25:48.433 --> 04:25:49.067
-Okay.
-Yeah.

04:25:49.801 --> 04:25:50.201
Go for it. All right, so he...

04:25:50.902 --> 04:25:51.336
Dexterity save.

04:25:53.071 --> 04:25:53.905
Does not save.
Go ahead and roll again.

04:25:56.875 --> 04:25:57.409
So, that's a nine plus...

04:25:57.909 --> 04:25:58.710
nine.

04:25:59.110 --> 04:25:59.611
-Eighteen.
-Eighteen. All right.

04:26:01.045 --> 04:26:02.147
The spear strikes him.

04:26:02.881 --> 04:26:03.548
Once again, the spectral form
shimmers as it hits,

04:26:04.816 --> 04:26:05.750
but as a physical damage source,

04:26:07.552 --> 04:26:07.752
it's not doing
quite as much as you want.

04:26:09.687 --> 04:26:10.355
-Does that finish your turn?
-That finishes it.

04:26:11.022 --> 04:26:11.289
-Tauro, you're up.
-Okay.

04:26:14.592 --> 04:26:15.260
I'm going to use my discipline

04:26:16.461 --> 04:26:17.028
to cast Marked for Death on him.

04:26:17.462 --> 04:26:18.129
-Okay.
-And then...

04:26:19.264 --> 04:26:20.398
That brings it back down to 13.

04:26:22.367 --> 04:26:24.235
-And then, I'm going to spend...
-Mordred, (indistinct).

04:26:27.439 --> 04:26:27.705
Spend 12 hatred

04:26:29.407 --> 04:26:29.574
to do Rapid Fire.

04:26:31.943 --> 04:26:32.577
So, that brings me down
to 3 hatred. Okay.

04:26:35.680 --> 04:26:35.980
All right. So, 6 attacks at him.

04:26:36.181 --> 04:26:38.016
Go for it.

04:26:40.985 --> 04:26:41.519
All plus 5 to hit,
so first attack

04:26:45.457 --> 04:26:45.757
is a natural 18, so 23.

04:26:46.458 --> 04:26:46.858
That hits.

04:26:49.194 --> 04:26:49.727
-Shall I do these one at a time?
-Roll your attacks upfront.

04:26:51.196 --> 04:26:51.596
-Okay.
-One hit.

04:26:53.465 --> 04:26:54.032
That hits.
Ooh, that's not as good.

04:26:56.167 --> 04:26:58.369
-That is a 13.
-Misses.

04:26:59.771 --> 04:27:01.039
-That's even worse.
-Misses.

04:27:02.674 --> 04:27:02.974
-Fifteen.
-Misses.

04:27:03.975 --> 04:27:04.275
Oh my God.

04:27:07.445 --> 04:27:07.712
-Is this attack four?
-This is the fifth attack now.

04:27:11.382 --> 04:27:12.083
-Oh my God. A natural one.
-Misses. Last attack.

04:27:16.554 --> 04:27:17.322
Okay. And... a 13, so 18 total.

04:27:19.290 --> 04:27:19.491
-Yeah, so 2 hits.
-Oh! Yikes.

04:27:20.758 --> 04:27:22.694
Another 6. Okay.

04:27:24.496 --> 04:27:24.729
Two D6 on this one, plus two.

04:27:25.763 --> 04:27:26.498
Okay.

04:27:28.032 --> 04:27:28.299
So, that is...

04:27:29.501 --> 04:27:29.734
8 damage on the first one.

04:27:30.768 --> 04:27:31.503
Okay.

04:27:32.136 --> 04:27:32.804
Okay.

04:27:34.506 --> 04:27:35.640
And... 12 damage on the second.

04:27:37.775 --> 04:27:38.776
-Okay. So, 20 damage halved--
-Twenty damage total.

04:27:39.711 --> 04:27:40.245
Physical damage
not quite impacting heavily

04:27:40.645 --> 04:27:42.447
on the spiritual entity.

04:27:43.181 --> 04:27:43.748
Okay.

04:27:44.816 --> 04:27:45.183
This is not looking good.

04:27:46.951 --> 04:27:47.519
That finishes your turn, Tauro.

04:27:48.553 --> 04:27:49.187
Mordred, Remy, you're up.

04:27:51.523 --> 04:27:52.590
Okay. Mordred comes to again.

04:27:53.658 --> 04:27:54.125
How are you doing?

04:27:57.228 --> 04:27:57.695
As a bonus action, I will do
Laws of Justice for everybody,

04:27:58.997 --> 04:27:59.364
but then I will say,

04:28:00.665 --> 04:28:01.633
"Come, child.

04:28:03.735 --> 04:28:04.269
Perhaps we can leave
this place together."

04:28:06.137 --> 04:28:06.371
And I will provoke him.

04:28:06.638 --> 04:28:07.605
Okay.

04:28:09.140 --> 04:28:09.474
So, he has to make it easy.
Wisdom of 14.

04:28:10.708 --> 04:28:11.376
Natural one.

04:28:12.176 --> 04:28:13.177
-So, he's gonna come for me.
-Yes, he does.

04:28:15.113 --> 04:28:16.381
And I'll just stay
on the ground, smiling up.

04:28:16.681 --> 04:28:17.549
Okay.

04:28:18.883 --> 04:28:19.417
Remy, what are you doing?

04:28:20.218 --> 04:28:21.553
I'm gonna say, "Gillian?

04:28:23.021 --> 04:28:26.124
I've heard of a Gillian."

04:28:27.258 --> 04:28:29.127
Make a persuasion check.

04:28:32.130 --> 04:28:32.430
-Big money.
-With advantage, using the name.

04:28:34.265 --> 04:28:37.235
Oh. Okay.

04:28:38.770 --> 04:28:40.271
Okay...

04:28:42.206 --> 04:28:42.774
Seventeen.

04:28:43.942 --> 04:28:44.909
You watch as the anger
and frustration

04:28:46.678 --> 04:28:48.346
in the middle of this child's
face goes...

04:28:48.746 --> 04:28:50.081
"You two...

04:28:51.349 --> 04:28:51.683
Where?

04:28:52.750 --> 04:28:53.117
How?

04:28:54.185 --> 04:28:55.219
Where is she?"

04:28:57.922 --> 04:28:58.389
The coins begin
to slow down and...

04:28:59.123 --> 04:28:59.791
fall around.

04:29:01.759 --> 04:29:02.126
"Calm down and we can tell you."

04:29:04.028 --> 04:29:11.736
Looking back at Mordred...

04:29:13.104 --> 04:29:13.905
The coins begin
to slow even further,

04:29:15.807 --> 04:29:16.708
and you're no longer
being pelted

04:29:17.508 --> 04:29:18.242
like in the middle
of a terrible storm,

04:29:19.811 --> 04:29:20.445
and more
just a gentle battering.

04:29:21.279 --> 04:29:22.180
As the spirit glides down,

04:29:23.748 --> 04:29:24.148
the candles
flicker brighter once more

04:29:24.415 --> 04:29:25.550
and float there.

04:29:28.720 --> 04:29:29.387
The once extremely intense
and angry, wrathful spirit

04:29:31.656 --> 04:29:31.923
now looks more age appropriate.

04:29:32.690 --> 04:29:33.024
This...

04:29:33.591 --> 04:29:34.626
child entity

04:29:36.828 --> 04:29:37.161
looks at you with
this snot-nosed, mid-teens face

04:29:38.196 --> 04:29:38.463
and goes...

04:29:39.364 --> 04:29:40.431
"What...?

04:29:40.765 --> 04:29:41.866
How...?"

04:29:44.035 --> 04:29:45.770
"How did you
get taken from her?"

04:29:47.405 --> 04:29:48.373
"All of us did here.

04:29:49.707 --> 04:29:51.242
And they
destroyed the town, but...

04:29:52.810 --> 04:29:53.411
she got away in time, I think.

04:29:54.946 --> 04:29:55.580
I wasn't ready.
The project wasn't ready.

04:29:58.249 --> 04:29:58.516
I was saving. It's not enough.

04:30:01.119 --> 04:30:02.720
I have to keep saving,
make sure she's okay.

04:30:03.054 --> 04:30:07.125
"Child.

04:30:09.460 --> 04:30:10.328
We can take you to her.

04:30:14.432 --> 04:30:16.100
This is more gold
than she could ever want."

04:30:18.436 --> 04:30:18.703
"I can't save...

04:30:19.470 --> 04:30:19.837
myself from this.

04:30:20.872 --> 04:30:22.106
I can't leave.

04:30:24.575 --> 04:30:26.978
Not until I have enough.

04:30:28.279 --> 04:30:29.647
She's...

04:30:30.915 --> 04:30:34.385
She's worth all of this."

04:30:36.754 --> 04:30:39.123
Roll the nature check for me,
if you would, Mordred.

04:30:40.391 --> 04:30:41.325
Oh, very nice. 20.

04:30:44.495 --> 04:30:44.862
Often, wrathful spirits
that are left behind

04:30:47.231 --> 04:30:47.432
are bound
by unfinished business...

04:30:49.500 --> 04:30:50.001
or the thought
of unfinished business,

04:30:50.802 --> 04:30:51.602
or something
is binding them there.

04:30:52.837 --> 04:30:53.771
You're not certain
how sincere he is,

04:30:54.972 --> 04:30:55.273
but based on the words
that he's saying,

04:30:56.708 --> 04:31:01.079
he does not feel he can leave.

04:31:03.981 --> 04:31:07.051
"How much gold
do you think you have here?"

04:31:09.954 --> 04:31:10.088
"13,261...

04:31:12.356 --> 04:31:13.424
not including
what you brought here.

04:31:16.194 --> 04:31:16.327
"And what were you
trying to build for her?"

04:31:17.595 --> 04:31:18.996
"A future.

04:31:21.199 --> 04:31:21.466
Tristram
couldn't provide for her.

04:31:24.402 --> 04:31:24.769
I was planning to take her
with me when I got away.

04:31:26.437 --> 04:31:26.738
I know
she's a little older, but...

04:31:28.072 --> 04:31:28.339
I'd grow up eventually."

04:31:29.540 --> 04:31:30.174
"You were in love with her."

04:31:31.409 --> 04:31:34.112
"No!

04:31:36.581 --> 04:31:39.817
I just wanted
to make sure she was okay."

04:31:42.153 --> 04:31:45.890
"Can we look in on her for you?"

04:31:47.959 --> 04:31:51.863
Make a persuasion check.

04:31:53.231 --> 04:31:56.734
Twenty-one.

04:31:57.268 --> 04:31:58.803
"Would you do that?

04:31:59.971 --> 04:32:01.372
Would you bring her this?"

04:32:03.441 --> 04:32:05.309
He gestures to the gold
in the chamber.

04:32:08.212 --> 04:32:10.715
"If it will bring rest to you
in this place."

04:32:14.118 --> 04:32:14.685
The spirit glides to the ground,
floating just inches above it.

04:32:17.321 --> 04:32:17.889
It mimics sitting on the edge
of one of the tombs,

04:32:19.791 --> 04:32:20.491
and this wrathful spirit,

04:32:21.692 --> 04:32:23.561
more than you've noticed
at this point, just looks...

04:32:24.862 --> 04:32:26.063
pitiful.

04:32:28.199 --> 04:32:29.100
"We're hoping to...

04:32:30.134 --> 04:32:30.334
rid Tristram

04:32:31.836 --> 04:32:33.004
of this pain and suffering...

04:32:33.771 --> 04:32:35.439
and rebuild.

04:32:39.377 --> 04:32:39.644
This could go a long way
towards that life.

04:32:40.478 --> 04:32:41.312
A happy life for Gillian."

04:32:42.079 --> 04:32:42.580
"I don't care
about Tristram anymore.

04:32:43.381 --> 04:32:43.581
This place is ruined.

04:32:45.183 --> 04:32:46.117
Too much evil has happened here

04:32:47.285 --> 04:32:47.552
and it's just gonna
keep getting worse.

04:32:48.286 --> 04:32:48.786
But if you think--"

04:32:49.921 --> 04:32:50.254
"Tristram Smishstram.

04:32:51.489 --> 04:32:52.390
This gold's for Gillian.

04:32:54.458 --> 04:32:56.160
We'll take it to Gillian."

04:32:57.428 --> 04:32:58.196
"Okay.

04:32:59.463 --> 04:32:59.997
Okay."

04:33:02.366 --> 04:33:02.633
And with that, you see
the spirit begin to fade

04:33:04.302 --> 04:33:04.502
and drift into the ground.

04:33:06.404 --> 04:33:06.671
All the rest of the gold...

04:33:07.271 --> 04:33:07.839
Ting! Ting!

04:33:09.073 --> 04:33:11.742
...falls around the stone.

04:33:15.513 --> 04:33:15.780
And it's hard to explain, but
in that moment, if feels like...

04:33:16.347 --> 04:33:16.981
a tension.

04:33:19.217 --> 04:33:21.752
A thickness in the air
seems to lighten.

04:33:23.955 --> 04:33:24.055
And with that,
you begin to gather the coins

04:33:25.756 --> 04:33:26.457
and the treasure

04:33:27.658 --> 04:33:28.259
and all the valuables that
have been gathered over time

04:33:29.861 --> 04:33:30.294
by whatever grave robbers...

04:33:33.531 --> 04:33:33.831
and tomb raiders and such that
have found their way into...

04:33:35.766 --> 04:33:36.300
the sub
cathedral region.

04:33:38.102 --> 04:33:38.636
I couldn't dig under
where he was perched

04:33:39.303 --> 04:33:40.271
at the top of the mound.

04:33:42.473 --> 04:33:42.740
Is there anything of importance
under there...

04:33:44.475 --> 04:33:44.942
as to why he was there?

04:33:46.177 --> 04:33:47.178
Yeah, swarm full of bugs.

04:33:48.079 --> 04:33:48.512
Oh God!

04:33:49.847 --> 04:33:50.047
-Oh!
-True.

04:33:51.682 --> 04:33:52.984
What you do find is...

04:33:54.552 --> 04:33:57.688
a small locket...

04:33:58.022 --> 04:33:59.323
with...

04:33:59.991 --> 04:34:00.858
a drawing.

04:34:03.027 --> 04:34:04.128
Not a very well-done drawing,
but it looks to be a woman.

04:34:04.996 --> 04:34:05.429
Okay.

04:34:07.465 --> 04:34:07.732
Young. Dark hair.

04:34:11.068 --> 04:34:11.269
I show it to Indra and Remy.

04:34:13.070 --> 04:34:13.804
"Does this look like
the Gillian you remember?"

04:34:17.208 --> 04:34:17.608
"I... I just recognize her name.
I really don't have any idea."

04:34:18.342 --> 04:34:18.943
Does it?

04:34:20.077 --> 04:34:20.811
It does. It's poorly drawn.

04:34:22.346 --> 04:34:23.214
-Yeah.
-It can kind of pass.

04:34:23.547 --> 04:34:24.248
It's like
a Ramona Flowers drawing?

04:34:25.449 --> 04:34:25.917
-Yeah.
-Yeah, straight up.

04:34:26.284 --> 04:34:28.219
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

04:34:29.186 --> 04:34:30.554
Put it over my...

04:34:30.855 --> 04:34:32.189
neck.

04:34:35.059 --> 04:34:36.260
"Alright, I guess
we're gonna be messengers."

04:34:38.696 --> 04:34:39.096
Mordred shoves an empty pot
into Laslo's hands.

04:34:40.464 --> 04:34:41.365
"Hold this."

04:34:41.699 --> 04:34:45.703
"One..."

04:34:49.573 --> 04:34:50.207
For the hours it takes to gather
this treasure that's left here,

04:34:52.810 --> 04:34:53.778
you finally have the last
gold piece in your grasp.

04:34:55.479 --> 04:34:56.147
And as you begin to exit
up the staircase,

04:34:57.148 --> 04:34:58.115
the voice once more creeps in...

04:35:01.018 --> 04:35:01.852
"She gets every coin.

04:35:04.855 --> 04:35:04.989
Or I'll follow you
for the rest of my days.

04:35:09.126 --> 04:35:12.496
I'm not above being
a little s*** for eternity."

04:35:14.432 --> 04:35:15.599
And that's where
we'll end this session.

04:35:16.667 --> 04:35:17.969
You'll have
to follow us to Vegas

04:35:18.903 --> 04:35:21.772
because
we're getting f****** up!

04:35:25.776 --> 04:35:26.043
We go straight to a priest.
We all get exorcised.

04:35:27.078 --> 04:35:27.578
LAUGHTER

04:35:28.145 --> 04:35:29.046
We take all the gold.

04:35:30.848 --> 04:35:31.415
Historically, it goes over
really well

04:35:31.682 --> 04:35:31.983
in the land of Sanctuary.

04:35:32.817 --> 04:35:33.551
Oh, yeah!

04:35:34.385 --> 04:35:35.219
-We're friends, you know?
-That's sweet. Yeah.

04:35:36.220 --> 04:35:36.787
-Great.
-Justice for Spell Slots!

04:35:37.288 --> 04:35:38.422
Yeah, none of you guys...

04:35:40.725 --> 04:35:42.226
None of you guys showed up
for Spell Slots's funeral.

04:35:43.361 --> 04:35:44.161
"We already buried him once."

04:35:44.862 --> 04:35:45.696
What can I say
about Spell Slots?

04:35:47.098 --> 04:35:48.733
He was the best among us.

04:35:51.669 --> 04:35:53.304
He was a dirty little Kanye fan,
but we loved him all the same.

04:35:55.106 --> 04:35:55.740
I bury him like this...

04:35:58.476 --> 04:36:00.845
He is next to his face.

04:36:03.247 --> 04:36:03.447
Thank you, guys, for
joining me into this rapid...

04:36:04.415 --> 04:36:04.815
Yay!

04:36:06.117 --> 04:36:06.417
...dungeon delve

04:36:07.685 --> 04:36:08.552
in Diablo.

04:36:09.987 --> 04:36:10.588
We ran a little over. Thank you
for your patience, everyone.

04:36:11.489 --> 04:36:12.423
Thank you all for watching.

04:36:13.024 --> 04:36:13.657
We hope you enjoyed it
as much as we did.

04:36:16.460 --> 04:36:16.594
Being ridiculous and dark
and silly and fun

04:36:18.596 --> 04:36:18.963
and killing monsters...

04:36:20.131 --> 04:36:21.232
-And grave robbers.
-And grave robbers.

04:36:22.433 --> 04:36:22.900
You can hit the gammon today.
It worked out well.

04:36:24.301 --> 04:36:25.369
If you wanna rewatch
this campaign

04:36:26.737 --> 04:36:27.271
or check out any of
the other amazing free content,

04:36:28.472 --> 04:36:29.006
as part of BlizzConline,

04:36:30.074 --> 04:36:30.608
visit BlizzConline.com.

04:36:31.876 --> 04:36:32.143
Thank you for having us.

04:36:33.444 --> 04:36:34.445
We love you very much.

04:36:36.447 --> 04:36:36.647
-We'll get that treasure goblin!
-Good night.

04:36:37.615 --> 04:36:44.822
LAUGHTER

04:36:46.223 --> 04:36:47.625
# PIANO MUSIC

04:36:51.695 --> 04:36:52.696
J. ALLEN BRACK: Games are
here for us during good times,

04:36:54.632 --> 04:36:55.232
and they're here for us
even when we feel alone.

04:36:56.868 --> 04:36:57.868
They give us experiences

04:36:59.804 --> 04:37:00.838
that are relevant
to the times in our lives,

04:37:03.874 --> 04:37:04.542
and experiences
that we carry forward with us.

04:37:08.279 --> 04:37:08.679
You know, online worlds have
been a huge part of our lives

04:37:09.280 --> 04:37:10.414
for decades now.

04:37:13.684 --> 04:37:13.951
The world has thrown a lot at us
since the last BlizzCon,

04:37:17.688 --> 04:37:18.556
and the thing that's really kept
everyone going on the WoW team

04:37:20.324 --> 04:37:20.591
has been connecting
with all of you.

04:37:23.160 --> 04:37:24.028
And on behalf of all of us
at Hearthstone,

04:37:25.963 --> 04:37:26.397
we want to thank
the many millions of you

04:37:27.631 --> 04:37:27.898
who play our game.

04:37:29.700 --> 04:37:30.601
Your dedication and support

04:37:31.235 --> 04:37:32.069
is what drives us
to make awesome updates

04:37:35.039 --> 04:37:36.006
and pursue ambitious
and fun ideas.

04:37:37.341 --> 04:37:38.209
LUIS BARRIGA:
And I am honored to be here

04:37:39.243 --> 04:37:39.910
on behalf of all
of our Diablo teams.

04:37:40.778 --> 04:37:41.979
And I hope you'll agree with me

04:37:43.347 --> 04:37:43.914
that it's a great time to be
a member of this community.

04:37:46.984 --> 04:37:48.219
JEFF KAPLAN: The thing
that I'm most excited about

04:37:51.522 --> 04:37:51.989
is that moment when we hand
the game over to the players.

04:37:52.924 --> 04:37:53.357
That's why we do it.

04:37:53.958 --> 04:37:54.992
We create the game

04:37:57.295 --> 04:37:57.928
because we want it to become
part of your life,

04:38:00.198 --> 04:38:02.500
and for you to experience it.

04:38:05.503 --> 04:38:06.403
SARALYN SMITH: That concludes
our first ever BlizzConline.

04:38:07.438 --> 04:38:08.105
We've had
millions of players tune in

04:38:09.373 --> 04:38:10.040
from all corners of the planet,

04:38:11.876 --> 04:38:12.877
lots of reactions to our games,

04:38:14.745 --> 04:38:15.513
and love shared
for our incredibly talented,

04:38:17.014 --> 04:38:18.282
motivated,
and generous community.

04:38:21.986 --> 04:38:22.620
We are all united
by love of gaming,

04:38:24.689 --> 04:38:25.256
and at this time in humanity,

04:38:25.590 --> 04:38:26.257
finding what connects us,

04:38:27.625 --> 04:38:28.492
and human connection in general,

04:38:30.294 --> 04:38:31.162
can be a light
during darker moments.

04:38:33.731 --> 04:38:34.265
For many of us,
BlizzCon is a light.

04:38:37.668 --> 04:38:38.302
Yes, we love seeing Blizzard's
latest announcements revealed,

04:38:39.704 --> 04:38:40.104
but it's even more than that.

04:38:40.571 --> 04:38:40.872
It's connection,

04:38:41.639 --> 04:38:42.607
inclusion,

04:38:45.009 --> 04:38:45.910
a reminder to proudly embrace
our inner geek,

04:38:47.645 --> 04:38:48.713
and that there are
so many people out there

04:38:51.048 --> 04:38:51.882
creating and playing
in these fantastical worlds.

04:38:55.519 --> 04:38:56.487
These past two days, we came
together for BlizzConline,

04:38:58.622 --> 04:38:59.256
from our studio shoot
of Opening Ceremony

04:39:01.325 --> 04:39:01.459
with epic Blizzard cinematics,

04:39:04.929 --> 04:39:05.863
to hearing from the folks that
dreamt up Blizzard 30 years ago.

04:39:07.731 --> 04:39:08.899
Those early days were so pure
and so simple.

04:39:10.868 --> 04:39:12.469
Let's just make games
and have some fun.

04:39:14.405 --> 04:39:15.239
We brought back
BlizzCon headliners,

04:39:16.173 --> 04:39:17.341
like Metallica
and Lindsey Stirling...

04:39:20.778 --> 04:39:21.145
visited with our ever-amazing
voice actors...

04:39:23.981 --> 04:39:24.615
Be blessed, be well,
be happy, be healthy.

04:39:25.716 --> 04:39:26.784
But most importantly, be you.

04:39:30.454 --> 04:39:31.722
Just know that you...
you are all so beautiful.

04:39:35.359 --> 04:39:35.659
When things seem the darkest,
the light is always with you.

04:39:36.460 --> 04:39:37.595
...watched fun competitions,

04:39:39.863 --> 04:39:39.964
like the battles from StarCraft
Legends, held in Korea.

04:39:42.800 --> 04:39:43.200
And congrats to our
Community Showcase winners.

04:39:43.867 --> 04:39:45.069
I am so thrilled

04:39:47.571 --> 04:39:48.406
pet cosplay seems like it's
a thing that's here to stay.

04:39:49.573 --> 04:39:50.474
I am thrilled
to be back with you!

04:39:52.977 --> 04:39:53.477
Thrilled!
Do you hear me saying this?

04:39:53.677 --> 04:39:54.712
Thank you, thank you,

04:39:55.145 --> 04:39:55.813
thank you, all,
for sharing your time with us.

04:39:56.814 --> 04:39:57.881
Wherever you are watching from,

04:40:00.484 --> 04:40:01.151
I hope that you and yours
are safe and healthy.

04:40:01.619 --> 04:40:02.386
SARALYN: The spirit of BlizzCon

04:40:04.154 --> 04:40:04.755
has a special place
in our hearts,

04:40:05.623 --> 04:40:06.624
largely thanks to all of you

04:40:08.125 --> 04:40:08.960
and how you have shown up for us
over the years,

04:40:10.861 --> 04:40:11.362
whether that's
dressed as a Murloc

04:40:12.329 --> 04:40:12.964
or in Tracer cosplay,

04:40:14.298 --> 04:40:14.732
with your guild, your partner,

04:40:16.701 --> 04:40:16.968
family or friends.

04:40:17.735 --> 04:40:18.102
Thank you.

04:40:19.136 --> 04:40:20.004
Happy 30 years, Blizzard,

04:40:22.139 --> 04:40:22.773
and thanks to all of you
for joining us.

04:40:24.208 --> 04:40:24.975
We hope to see you again soon.

